Postal Service and Post Offices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stamps (Postal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-01T11:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zeynep Tufekci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zeynep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tufekci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6022ea8-8f34-55c8-a38b-c5c0424faddf', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6022ea8-8f34-55c8-a38b-c5c0424faddf'}, {'abstract': 'At all cost the man in the white beard had to be kept away from the men with black beards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/02/opinion/isis-war-on-christmas.html', 'snippet': 'At all cost the man in the white beard had to be kept away from the men with black beards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oran, Algeria — IT might have been an occasion for collectors of omens to rejoice: For the first time in nearly five centuries, in 2015 the Prophet Muhammad’s birthday coincided with Jesus’ birthday. A cause for hope? Too little, it turns out.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ISIS’ War on Christmas', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ISIS’ War on Christmas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daoud, Kamel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-01T11:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kamel Daoud', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kamel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daoud', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/95edcb90-2082-5889-b4d3-d876c10fd1b9', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95edcb90-2082-5889-b4d3-d876c10fd1b9'}, {'abstract': 'Il fallait à tout prix chasser le barbu blanc des parages des barbes noires.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/02/opinion/daech-en-guerre-contre-noel.html', 'snippet': 'Il fallait à tout prix chasser le barbu blanc des parages des barbes noires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oran, Algérie — L’occasion aurait pu faire le bonheur des collectionneurs de présages : pour la première fois depuis presque cinq siècles, l’anniversaire de la naissance du Prophète Mahomet et l’anniversaire de la naissance de Jésus ont coïncidé en 2015. De quoi inspirer de l’espoir ? Si peu, en fait.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daech en guerre contre Noël', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daech en guerre contre Noël', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-01T11:51:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Kamel Daoud', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kamel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daoud', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/865c606c-a889-5e5a-bf23-9879233769e7', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/865c606c-a889-5e5a-bf23-9879233769e7'}, {'abstract': 'Recalling the wait for a favorite dish and a life away from the war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/03/magazine/a-lingering-taste.html', 'snippet': 'Recalling the wait for a favorite dish and a life away from the war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1984, while my parents traveled to the United States to assess a possible life there, they rented a chalet in the Lebanese coastal town Jounieh and left us in the care of my maternal grandmother. It was a thrilling summer for me. More than any of my siblings, I was tired of the war in Lebanon, which had been going strong for almost a decade. I was particularly fed up with living in constant fear — from the shellings, the sniper attacks, the bombings, the checkpoints, the kidnappings and the threats directed at my Palestinian-born parents, who met and married in Beirut. I spent much of my time daydreaming about a new, perfect and utterly ‘‘normal’’ life in America.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/magazine/03lives/03mag-03lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/03/magazine/03lives/03mag-03lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 843}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/magazine/03lives/03mag-03lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 