nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3117bb7-2bd9-5cdd-9628-751628105971', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3117bb7-2bd9-5cdd-9628-751628105971'}, {'abstract': 'In his first message of 2016, he said that apathy “creates barriers, suspicions, fears and closure,” and he called on people to open their hearts to the needs of others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/02/world/europe/pope-francis-new-years-message.html', 'snippet': 'In his first message of 2016, he said that apathy “creates barriers, suspicions, fears and closure,” and he called on people to open their hearts to the needs of others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first message of 2016, Pope Francis summoned humanity to show compassion and to transcend the apathy that impedes peace in a world that has been filled of late with conflict and suffering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope Francis Urges Overcoming ‘Indifference’ to Attain Peace', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '&#8216;Indifference&#8217; Hinders Peace, Francis Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-01T13:49:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e20e7466-ab79-5ede-aa6f-cbb142436651', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e20e7466-ab79-5ede-aa6f-cbb142436651'}, {'abstract': 'Blockbusters like “Star Wars: The Force Awakens” and “Mad Max: Fury Road” delivered much of the year’s best cinema and ought to be up for Oscars. Wait, what?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/03/movies/the-year-the-studios-get-it-right.html', 'snippet': 'Blockbusters like “Star Wars: The Force Awakens” and “Mad Max: Fury Road” delivered much of the year’s best cinema and ought to be up for Oscars. Wait, what?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February, the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences will consecrate a best picture, most likely choosing from among a roster of respectable, serious dramas. A few early favorites have already faded — does anyone remember “The Walk” or “Everest”? “Sicario” or “Black Mass”? — but the field of Oscar movies is crowded with aspirants. Meanwhile, movie audiences have had other ideas, driving box-office totals to record heights with their enthusiasm for reanimated dinosaurs, romantic trainwrecks and galactic battles. Popularity is not the same as quality, of course, but 2015 was a year when a lot of the best cinematic art could be found at the multiplex, amid the sequels and blockbusters.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/arts/03CRITICS1/03CRITICS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/03/arts/03CRITICS1/03CRITICS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/arts/03CRITICS1/03CRITICS1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'lega