'nyt://article/26ef32f5-9ea8-541f-9e5a-0c3bb7c05d47', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26ef32f5-9ea8-541f-9e5a-0c3bb7c05d47'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Cosby made his first public statement since being charged with aggravated indecent assault, posting a message to Twitter saying, “Friends and fans, Thank You.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/02/us/pennsylvania-cosby-thanks-fans-in-message-on-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Cosby made his first public statement since being charged with aggravated indecent assault, posting a message to Twitter saying, “Friends and fans, Thank You.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Cosby made his first public statement since being charged with aggravated indecent assault\xa0in Pennsylvania on Wednesday, posting a message on Twitter\xa0on Thursday\xa0night that said, “Friends and fans, Thank You.” The charges facing the 78-year-old entertainer stem from an accusation made by Andrea Constand that Mr. Cosby drugged and sexually abused her in 2004 in his home in Cheltenham Township, a suburb north of Philadelphia, prosecutors said. Aggravated indecent assault carries a punishment of five to 10 years in prison and a $25,000 fine. Mr. Cosby was charged after being dogged for years by sexual assault allegations made by dozens of women. In recent months, he has filed defamation lawsuits against eight of his accusers, including the former model Beverly Johnson. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pennsylvania: Cosby Thanks Fans in Message on Twitter', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Mid-Atlantic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pennsylvania: Cosby Thanks Fans in Message on Twitter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cosby, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stack, Liam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Constand, Andrea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-02T01:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e539377-4a05-5819-82f7-037384e21ff5', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e539377-4a05-5819-82f7-037384e21ff5'}, {'abstract': 'McCaffrey, the Heisman runner-up, amassed 368 yards by every conceivable means — rushes, receptions and punt and kick returns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/02/sports/ncaafootball/christian-mccaffrey-stanford-iowa-rose-bowl.html', 'snippet': 'McCaffrey, the Heisman runner-up, amassed 368 yards by every conceivable means — rushes, receptions and punt and kick returns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PASADENA, Calif. — On Friday, Christian McCaffrey presented an argument to extend the Heisman Trophy voting beyond the regular season, and Stanford made the case that defeats suffered way back on Labor Day weekend should be discounted when ultimately evaluating teams for bowl games and in year-end polls.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/02/sports/02ROSE1/02ROSE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/02/sports/02ROSE1/02ROSE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2