4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b8c71a18-1d3d-5afa-a080-04cfea29a214'}, {'abstract': 'A generation of Indian energy entrepreneurs is out to prove that a fast, clean and economical route to universal electrification is through solar home systems, financed with small bank loans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/03/business/energy-environment/electrifying-india-with-the-sun-and-small-loans.html', 'snippet': 'A generation of Indian energy entrepreneurs is out to prove that a fast, clean and economical route to universal electrification is through solar home systems, financed with small bank loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, the hundred or so residents of Paradeshappanamatha, a secluded hamlet in the southern Indian state of Karnataka, gathered along the central pathway between their 22 densely clustered homes, and watched as government workers hoisted a solar-powered streetlamp. As the first display of electricity in the town, it was an object of mild interest, but, being outside, the light didn’t help anyone cook or study, and only attracted moths.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electrifying India, With the Sun and Small Loans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Electrifying India, With the Sun and Small Loans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bearak, Max', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Solar Electric Light Company (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hande, Harish (1967- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoner, Robert J (1962- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-02T17:02:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Max Bearak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Max', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c522df63-626e-544e-abcd-ec7a30dbd942', 'word_count': 2421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c522df63-626e-544e-abcd-ec7a30dbd942'}, {'abstract': 'A regulatory change that would allow companies more discretion in deciding what is “material” information arouses concern among investors and auditors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/03/business/fasb-proposes-to-curb-what-companies-must-disclose.html', 'snippet': 'A regulatory change that would allow companies more discretion in deciding what is “material” information arouses concern among investors and auditors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Accounting rule makers are not generally known as flame-throwers. But with a new proposal, the Financial Accounting Standards Board has lobbed a miniature Molotov cocktail into the usually staid world of audit standards, upsetting investor groups and experts in the field.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FASB Proposes to Curb What Companies Must Disclose', 'kicker': 'Fair Game', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Board Hurls a Bombshell Into Auditing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenson, Gretchen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Accounting Standards Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compan