-different-note-on-race-at-yale.html', 'snippet': 'A music professor has sought to address a history of segregation in shape-note singing, as social justice protests have roiled universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ian Quinn, a professor of music at Yale, attended his first sacred harp hymn-singing session in a stone chapel in Berkeley, Calif., in 2008, he was so impressed with the session’s openness to all comers, and the egalitarian message it sent to music-makers generally, that he decided to push for a similar session when he returned to New Haven.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03ARTSCT1sub/03ARTSCT1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03ARTSCT1sub/03ARTSCT1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03ARTSCT1sub/03ARTSCT1sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03ARTSCT1sub/03ARTSCT1sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03ARTSCT1sub/03ARTSCT1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03ARTSCT1sub/03ARTSCT1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 