ave traditionally clustered in Koreatown, in Manhattan in the 30s. But just two weeks ago, the restaurant Insa opened in Gowanus, offering a wide array of Korean barbecue dishes and after-dinner entertainment in one of five karaoke rooms with wacky themes. Owned by Sohui Kim and Ben Schneider, the married couple behind the Good Fork in Red Hook, Insa, which occupies a sprawling former warehouse at 328 Douglass Street, may be the only place in Brooklyn where you can cook cuttlefish and octopus on your table grill and then repair to the Jungle Room for a performance of “Hound Dog.” Last week, a group of Brooklynites was planning to do precisely that — albeit with a bit more food and without the Elvis.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03TABLE1/03TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03TABLE1/03TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03TABLE1/03TABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03TABLE1/03TABLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03TABLE1/03TABLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/03/nyregion/03TABLE1/03TABLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 