b_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-the-week-of-jan-4.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for the Week of Jan. 4', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Municipal Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-03T22:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32cdeab4-e85f-50c2-b641-cea9cbd27d01', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32cdeab4-e85f-50c2-b641-cea9cbd27d01'}, {'abstract': 'The movie, the basis of a possible series, dramatizes the year 1990, when rap music was suspended between its gritty urban roots and mainstream acceptance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/arts/television/the-breaks-a-tv-movie-on-vh1-examines-the-year-hip-hop-found-its-flow.html', 'snippet': 'The movie, the basis of a possible series, dramatizes the year 1990, when rap music was suspended between its gritty urban roots and mainstream acceptance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1990, hip-hop was a subculture striving to breach the mainstream without losing its soul. The music had matured at breakneck speed in the 1980s. Rappers pushed past boasts and chants with storytelling, complex wordplay and sociopolitical consciousness, as producers vastly extended the sound-collage possibilities of sampling. “Yo! MTV Raps,” which started in 1988, was expanding the hip-hop audience beyond its urban core, and MC Hammer had a worldwide hit with “U Can’t Touch This.” But at the same time the crack epidemic was closing down the New York City clubs that had been hip-hop laboratories, while radio stations still resisted hip-hop’s genuine innovators and major labels considered hip-hop a novelty that would run its course. Everyone involved was inventing the music and the business on the spot.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/arts/04THEBREAKS/04THEBREAKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/04/arts/04THEBREAKS/04THEBREAKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/arts/04THEBREAKS/04THEBREAKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/arts/04THEBREAKS/04THEBREAKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1062, 'width': 1593, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/arts/04THEBREAKS/04THEBREAKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/04/arts/04THEBREAKS/04THEBREAKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '