anning stood stoutly on the Broncos’ sideline, not once appearing to favor his left foot, with a torn plantar fascia that had caused him to miss six games. Manning looked fine, which caused a woolen blanket of disbelief to settle over Sports Authority Field at Mile High during the Broncos’ regular-season finale against the San Diego Chargers.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/0404BRONCOS1/0404BRONCOS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peyton Manning Returns and Leads Broncos to No. 1 Seed in A.F.C.', 'kicker': 'Broncos 27, Chargers 20', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manning Returns and Helps Broncos Capture No. 1 Seed in the A.F.C. ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Chargers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-04T01:37:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda365f3-6948-5c77-b80e-a55a1719fa11', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dda365f3-6948-5c77-b80e-a55a1719fa11'}, {'abstract': 'Angus’ Cafe Bistro, a restaurant on West 44th Street, attracted stars and producers of ‘The Producers’ as investors and patrons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/nyregion/a-homey-hangout-for-broadway-stars-closes-after-14-years.html', 'snippet': 'Angus’ Cafe Bistro, a restaurant on West 44th Street, attracted stars and producers of ‘The Producers’ as investors and patrons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trent Rhoton was drinking a pint and a shot at the bar of Angus’ Cafe Bistro on Sunday afternoon when a friend wandered over to greet him. “It’s the end of an era,” said the friend, John McMahon, as they clinked glasses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/nyregion/04ANGUSweb1/04ANGUSweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Homey Hangout for Broadway Stars Closes After 14 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Homey Broadway Haunt Ends Its 14-Year Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Angus's Cafe and Bistro (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-04T01:39:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c52c44fc-2dd8-51bd-8ec2-8d27b52efbe0', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c52c44fc-2dd8-51bd-8ec2-8d27b52efbe0'}, {'abstract': 'At the American Economic Association’s annual meeting, what was once mainly an issue among players on the margins of the profession is taking center stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/business/economy/economists-take-aim-at-wealth-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'At the American Economic Association’s annual meeting, what was once mainly an issue among players on the margins of the profession is taking center stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — When pundits and presidential candidates talk about inequality and the tiny sliver of the population whose fortunes have soared, they often drop names like Warren Buffett, Bill Gates, Sheldon Adelson and Mark Zuckerberg.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economists Take Aim at Wealth Inequality', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economists Take Aim at Wealth Inequality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ECONOMIC ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-04T01:46:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8290943-5328-5710-9a69-1fc9ddb4596d', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8290943-5328-5710-9a69-1fc9ddb4596d'}, {'abstract': 'Both teams’ previous elimination from playoff contention made for an unusual game where Philadelphia wanted to show it could run its offense and the Giants aimed to win another game for Coach Tom Coughlin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/sports/football/an-eagles-audition-tarnishes-a-giants-tribute-to-tom-coughlin.html', 'snippet': 'Both teams’ previous elimination from playoff contention made for an unusual game where Philadelphia wanted to show it could run its offense and the Giants aimed to win another game for Coach Tom Coughlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The Giants had one big edge over the Philadelphia Eagles entering Sunday’s season finale. Their head coach, Tom Coughlin, had been in the job for 12 years. Pat Shurmur, Philadelphia’s interim coach, had been in his job for all of five days.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/04subBLUE/04subBLUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/04/sports/04subBLUE/04subBLUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 838}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', '