of kindness and generosity are offset by cruelty, greed and corruption, and creativity is inspired by necessity because of the city’s broken infrastructure and the looming threat of ruin. Between these extremes, and usually to the background drone of a generator, exist the rich and textured lives of some 20 million people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Growth of Contemporary African Photography at LagosPhoto', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nwagbogu, Azu', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Press Photo Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-04T08:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': "By Finbarr O'Reilly", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Finbarr', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Reilly", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9093683-d9a6-5778-b43b-9ae958ddb622', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9093683-d9a6-5778-b43b-9ae958ddb622'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to Arthur C. Brooks, who wrote that we should be a nation “motivated by hope and opportunity, not one dominated by victimhood.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/opinion/a-culture-glorifying-victimhood.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to Arthur C. Brooks, who wrote that we should be a nation “motivated by hope and opportunity, not one dominated by victimhood.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Ed