d', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/28ddb601-0a05-56ee-a610-36c974792f16', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28ddb601-0a05-56ee-a610-36c974792f16'}, {'abstract': 'Antiterrorism efforts are threatening a cornerstone of democracy — the equality of all citizens before the law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/04/opinion/frances-diminished-liberties.html', 'snippet': 'Antiterrorism efforts are threatening a cornerstone of democracy — the equality of all citizens before the law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since President François Hollande of France declared a state of emergency after the terrorist attacks in Paris on Nov. 13, more than 2,700 police raids have been carried out. They have yielded very little that can be linked to terrorism, but have traumatized citizens and left havoc in their wake.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/opinion/04mon2web/04mon2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/04/opinion/04mon2web/04mon2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/opinion/04mon2web/04mon2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/opinion/04mon2web/04mon2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/04/opinion/04mon2web/04mon2web-thumbStandard.jpg'