n a hurricane on Oct. 1 with 33 mariners aboard while on a route to San Juan, P.R., from Jacksonville, Fla., ended about a month later with the discovery of its wreckage nearly three miles under the sea. On Sunday, investigators for the National Transportation Safety Board released photographs and video footage captured by remote-controlled underwater vehicles of the sunken ship that show a breach in its hull.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos Show El Faro’s Resting Place, but Sinking Remains Mystery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sonar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hurricane Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-04T19:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jean Rutter and Frances Robles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Frances', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8ccf481-ef74-53ee-8651-15349c62afe9', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8ccf481-ef74-53ee-8651-15349c62afe9'}, {'abstract': 'Destiny Garcia was charged with murder in the killings of the Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn, couple, whose bodies were f