ptation of Laurie Anderson’s film, “Heart of a Dog,” can be seen at the end of each day as part of the Midnight Moment program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since its inception in 2012, the Midnight Moment program has presented the work of prominent artists including Tracey Emin, Jesper Just and Andy Warhol in the unlikeliest of places: on several giant screens right in the middle of Times Square. Each month, Times Square Arts and the Times Square Advertising Coalition choose one artist whose work will be showcased daily over the course of a month in a three-minute video, beginning at 11:57 p.m. and finishing at midnight — an appropriately digestible format.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Pays Tribute to Her Dog — in Times Square', 'kicker': 'On View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, LAURIE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-04T20:41:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvia Rupani-Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rupani-Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87c29279-fde2-5873-91f4-6462156043ae', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87c29279-fde2-5873-91f4-6462156043ae'}, {'abstract': 'With only two field paleontologists, the Forest Service has turned for help to a small group of amateur fossil-hunters, many in their 70s and 80s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/05/science/dinosaurs-amateur-paleontology-pic