zations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-05T00:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a85114b-174d-5743-89da-c41ac3f3f007', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a85114b-174d-5743-89da-c41ac3f3f007'}, {'abstract': 'The experiment has riled many of the Indian capital’s elite even as its ability to reduce pollution remains unclear, with air quality still at “hazardous” levels Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/05/world/asia/streets-if-not-the-air-clear-out-as-delhi-tests-car-restrictions.html', 'snippet': 'The experiment has riled many of the Indian capital’s elite even as its ability to reduce pollution remains unclear, with air quality still at “hazardous” levels Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Traffic was flowing smoothly Monday morning on Outer Ring Road in South Delhi, usually jammed at that hour by subway construction and cars. An upscale market was dotted with free parking spaces. Monkeys ambled down one street in the colonial heart of the capital, easily dodging the few cars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/world/05delhi_web2/05delhi_web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/05/world/05delhi_web2/05delhi_web2-