 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nida Najar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Najar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc11c4c8-bdc5-5e93-b26b-a62ce6c2e4a2', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc11c4c8-bdc5-5e93-b26b-a62ce6c2e4a2'}, {'abstract': 'Islamic State militants attempted to capture an oil port along Libya’s coast, in fighting that left at least seven people dead and set fire to a storage tank of crude oil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/05/world/africa/libya-islamic-state-attacks-oil-port.html', 'snippet': 'Islamic State militants attempted to capture an oil port along Libya’s coast, in fighting that left at least seven people dead and set fire to a storage tank of crude oil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Islamic State militants attempted to capture an oil port along Libya’s coast early Monday, in fighting that left at least seven people dead and set fire to a storage tank of crude oil, according to witnesses. The militants began their assault on the Sidra oil port with suicide bomb attacks on a checkpoint, but by Monday afternoon, the offensive had been beaten back by guards. The Islamic State in Libya is regarded as one of the most dangerous affiliates of the extremist group outside of Iraq and Syria, and has gained strength in Libya by capitalizing on infighting among various armed factions. The attack on Monday was at least the second by the Islamic State on the Sidra port, and showed the determination of the group to expand its territory beyond its stronghold in the western Libyan town of Surt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya: Islamic State Attacks Oil Port', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; Libya: Islamic State Attacks Oil Port', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zway, Suliman Ali', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-05T00:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suliman Ali Zway', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suliman', 'middlename': 'Ali', 'lastname': 'Zway', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a9c9b04-b425-5442-8667-89a66b1dbc42', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a9c9b04-b425-5442-8667-89a66b1dbc42'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge found that he and a colleague had committed misconduct by waiting to turn over key evidence in a civil case about a police shooting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/05/us/illinois-new-trial-ordered-in-fatal-shooting-by-police.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge found that he and a colleague had committed misconduct by waiting to turn over key evidence in a civil case about a police shooting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawyer for the City of Chicago resigned Monday as a federal judge found that he and a colleague had committed misconduct by waiting to turn over key evidence in a civil case about a police shooting. The lawyer, Jordan Marsh, resigned on the same day Judge Edmond E. Chang of United States District Court threw out a jury’s verdict that cleared the officers of wrongdoing and ordered Chicago to pay the plaintiffs’ legal bills. Thomas Aumann, the other lawyer, resigned in August. The ruling involves a 2011 traffic stop that ended in the fatal shooting of Darius Pinex by officers who said radio traffic had led them to pull over his vehicle. The radio recordings were not turned over to lawyers for Mr. Pinex’s estate until the trial had started, and Judge Chang said Mr. Marsh “intentionally concealed” them. Also Monday, the acting chief of Chicago’s much-criticized Independent Police Review Authority announced staffing changes that she said were designed to build trust in the agency, which has rarely faulted officers for shootings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: City Lawyer Quits After Judge Finds Misconduct', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: City Lawyer Quits After Judge Finds Misconduct', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsh, Jordan E (1967- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chang, Edmond E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (Chicago, Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-05T00:50:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://