athizing with Saudi Arabia, a powerful ally, but also trying to avoid a conflict with Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/06/world/middleeast/kuwait-iran-feud-saudi-arabia.html', 'snippet': 'Many countries signaled that they would take a measured approach, sympathizing with Saudi Arabia, a powerful ally, but also trying to avoid a conflict with Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — For all the diplomatic dominoes that have fallen across the Middle East in recent days, with ambassadors from different countries flying home as a result of the explosive rift between Saudi Arabia and Iran, the map of allegiances has not significantly altered.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gulf States Guarding Their Interests in Saudi-Iran Rift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gulf States Guarding Their Interests in Saudi-Iran Rift ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nimr, Nimr al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kuwait', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-05T10:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dcb8ab7-3245-5b4d-864e-551db7cfc460', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dcb8ab7-3245-5b4d-864e-551db7cfc460'}, {'abstract': 'The absence of maternal guidance is a palpable force in the journeys of two young women in a world of unsavory characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/books/review/samantha-hunts-mr-splitfoot.html', 'snippet': 'The absence of maternal guidance is a palpable force in the journeys of two young women in a world of unsavory characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wonder if the best stories are those hardest to categorize. Bildungsroman or romance? Picaresque or metafiction? Stories change shape as one reads them. Understandings are loaded in, revised, discarded. Then, when the book is closed, a kind of spirit image remains in the mind, a revenant. Sometimes a reader knows that a lasting connection has been made only by the intensity of the effect, the memory and aftershock, after the book is back on the shelf.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/books/review/10MAGUIRE/10MAGUIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/books/review/10MAGUIRE/10MAGUIRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/books/review/10MAGUIRE/10MAGUIRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/books/review/10MAGUIRE/10MAGUIRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/books/review/10MAGUIRE/10MAGUIRE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'heig