article/3f874c0e-d977-51df-ab3b-1eaaf167de11'}, {'abstract': 'In a collaboration with Benjamin Millepied’s L.A. Dance Project, Gerard and Kelly explore themes of queer intimacy “within the legacies of modernist architecture.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/05/gerard-and-kelly-to-perform-at-schindler-house-and-glass-house/', 'snippet': 'In a collaboration with Benjamin Millepied’s L.A. Dance Project, Gerard and Kelly explore themes of queer intimacy “within the legacies of modernist architecture.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Architecture and performance art have gone together at least since Yves Klein’s “Leap Into the Void,” his 1960 photomontage that makes it look as if he is swan-diving from the ledge of an elegant mansard roof. Beginning this weekend, the dancers and visual artists Brennan Gerard and Ryan Kelly will use two of the country’s most beloved 20th-century houses – the Schindler House, designed by Rudolph M. Schindler in West Hollywood, Calif., and the Glass House, Philip Johnson’s masterpiece in New Canaan, Conn. – as walk-in texts for a performance work focusing on what they describe as “themes of queer intimacy and domestic space within the legacies of modernist architecture.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gerard and Kelly to Perform at Schindler House  and Glass House', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peformance Art Planned at 2 Famous Houses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 6, 'major': 