sons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cattle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-05T19:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucinda Holt and Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucinda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e409534-88b6-5d78-ba2c-b799077c92e9', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e409534-88b6-5d78-ba2c-b799077c92e9'}, {'abstract': 'Also, Biang moves to the East Village, Chinese dry-pot cooking at MaLa Project, and meatballs to take home at Maroni Hot Pots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/06/dining/thai-street-food-now-at-the-lucky-bee-on-the-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'Also, Biang moves to the East Village, Chinese dry-pot cooking at MaLa Project, and meatballs to take home at Maroni Hot Pots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lucky Bee Rupert Noffs and his business partner, the chef Matty Bennett, are taking a farm-to-table approach to Thai street food. It’s easy for Mr. Bennett, who was at the Fat Radish, a locavore spot. The setting, dominated by a big bar, is splashed with vibrant pink. “The pink was my idea,” said Mr. Noffs, “and I think it works.” In the front, snacks like salt-and-pepper chicken wings and oysters with nahm jim chile sauce are dispensed. The menu has crisp pork belly with palm sugar caramel and chile vinegar; grilled squid with sunchokes, coconut and shaved bottarga; and a green curry of vegetables with pickled mustard greens. The cocktail list features drinks made with honey: A dollar of each drink sold goes to the New York City Beekeepers Association. The partners hope to raise bees on the roof: 252 Broome Street (Ludlow Street), 917-262-0329, luckybeenyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/dining/06OFFTHEMENU/06OFFTHEMENU-thumbL