es.com/2016/01/06/upshot/why-the-government-owns-so-much-land-in-the-west.html', 'snippet': 'Understanding the dispute in Oregon requires a look at American history, and how geography, climate and politics shaped “the frontier.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States government owns 47 percent of all land in the West. In some states, including Oregon, Utah and Nevada, the majority of land is owned by the federal government. Of course, it used to own nearly all of it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Government Owns So Much Land in the West', 'kicker': 'Manifest Destiny', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why the Government Owns So Much Land in the West', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanger-Katz, Margot', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bui, Quoctrung', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bundy, Cliven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ranches', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T01:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quoctrung Bui and Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quoctrung', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bui', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d84948c-e03b-5274-b9cc-34088a279752', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d84948c-e03b-5274-b9cc-34088a279752'}, {'abstract': 'Reporters and editors at The Las Vegas Review-Journal were given guidelines for how the paper should cover its new owner, the billionaire Republican donor Sheldon Adelson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/06/business/media/las-vegas-news-staff-advised-on-covering-adelson.html', 'snippet': 'Reporters and editors at The Las Vegas Review-Journal were given guidelines for how the paper should cover its new owner, the billionaire Republican donor Sheldon Adelson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the billionaire casino mogul Sheldon Adelson acquired The Las Vegas Review-Journal last month, the newspaper’s reporters and editors have agonized over whether their coverage of Mr. Adelson and his business interests would be compromised. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/business/0105adelsonjpg/0105adelsonjpg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/05/business/0105adelsonjpg/0105adelsonjpg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/business/0105adelsonjpg/0105adelsonjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/business/0105adelsonjpg/0105adelsonjpg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/business/0105adelsonjpg/0105adelsonjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 