b4'}, {'abstract': 'The key role of party elites has evolved but has not fundamentally changed, an author of “The Party Decides” says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/upshot/donald-trump-is-also-an-outlier-in-political-science.html', 'snippet': 'The key role of party elites has evolved but has not fundamentally changed, an author of “The Party Decides” says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump has confounded politicians, pundits and political scientists as he runs a most unconventional — and so far successful — campaign to win the Republican presidential nomination. Here’s the way we think these things are supposed to play out: Party leaders shape and guide the nomination process. We call it the invisible primary, and it was described in an influential 2008 book, “The Party Decides.” I asked David Karol, a University of Maryland associate professor of political science and one of the book’s four authors, whether Mr. Trump’s rise reveals a fundamental shift in party control. He thinks not. Here’s our conversation, slightly edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/upshot/07UP-Vavreck/07UP-Vavreck-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/07/upshot/07UP-Vavreck/07UP-Vavreck-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/upshot/07UP-Vavreck/07UP-Vavreck-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/upshot/07UP-Vavreck/07UP-Vavreck-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's