Pakistan are close to a truce in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/06/1966-india-and-pakistan-near-truce/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: India and Pakistan are close to a truce in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TASHKENT, U.S.S.R. — India and Pakistan have virtually agreed on an agenda for their conference here and have made progress toward a nonaggression pact that may be signed in the next few days, authoritative diplomatic sources said today [Jan. 6]. The agreement was reportedly hammered out today during separate talks that Soviet Premier Alexei N. Kosygin held with Pakistani President Mohammed Ayub Khan and Indian Prime Minister Lal Bahadur Shastri. The two Asian leaders are also considering an agreement to withdraw occupation troops from both countries.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 7, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/blogs/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent-jumbo.png', 'height': 465, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/blogs/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent-superJumbo.png', 'height': 465, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/blogs/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/07/blogs/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent/07iht-oldjan07-tashkent-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'