'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T15:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9af7ec55-8698-59dd-927f-e56021f41a9a', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9af7ec55-8698-59dd-927f-e56021f41a9a'}, {'abstract': 'Will President Hollande’s plan to strip citizenship from terrorists with dual nationality destroy his country’s founding principles?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/opinion/france-forfeits-its-own-values.html', 'snippet': 'Will President Hollande’s plan to strip citizenship from terrorists with dual nationality destroy his country’s founding principles?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — IN French, the word “déchéance” has several meanings, all of them bleak. It can refer to the fall of a civilization, or the degradation of the social fabric. More formally, it means the forfeiture of a right or a possession — one’s citizenship, for example. All three meanings, carrying echoes of the country’s experience under Vichy, resonate in a political drama unfolding in France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Forfeits Its Own Values', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T15:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Zaretsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaretsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/74428407-c485-5a37-a538-08454de8864f', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74428407-c485-5a37-a538-08454de8864f'}, {'abstract': 'The action in California is the latest setback for the restaurant chain, which said it expected a drop of 14.6 percent in same-store sales for its fourth quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/business/chipotle-outbreak.html', 'snippet': 'The action in California is the latest setback for the restaurant chain, which said it expected a drop of 14.6 percent in same-store sales for its fourth quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chipotle Mexican Grill said on Wednesday that it had been served a federal grand jury subpoena as part of a criminal investigation seeking information about a norovirus outbreak at a California restaurant.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/business/07chipotle-web/07chipotle-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/07/business/07chipotle-web/07chipotle-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/business/07chipotle-web/07chipotle-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/business/07chipotle-web/07chipotle-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 20