subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T16:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe290b0-53a1-500d-95d4-a923c8e7f06e', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe290b0-53a1-500d-95d4-a923c8e7f06e'}, {'abstract': 'With a 10-0 run, Kansas City became the first team to start 1-5 but make the playoffs since the 1970 Bengals, but the Chiefs have not won a playoff game since 1993.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/sports/football/kansas-city-chiefs-ride-momentum-of-10-0-run-into-nfl-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'With a 10-0 run, Kansas City became the first team to start 1-5 but make the playoffs since the 1970 Bengals, but the Chiefs have not won a playoff game since 1993.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not that long ago, the Kansas City Chiefs’ season appeared to have gone badly awry. With a loss to the Vikings on Oct. 18, the Chiefs fell to 1-5. Their star running back, Jamaal Charles, was out for the year with a torn anterior cruciate ligament. Coach Andy Reid was under fire, notably for a puzzling decision to hand off to Charles at the end of regulation in Week 2 against Denver, which led to a fumble and a loss.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07CHIEFSweb1/07CHIEFSweb1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07CHIEFSweb1/07CHIEFSweb1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'su