, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T19:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6c92003-a3ca-5c0d-a8d5-69cf57eb92e5', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6c92003-a3ca-5c0d-a8d5-69cf57eb92e5'}, {'abstract': 'This drama about passing for a younger woman opens with its heroine’s workplace secret more or less intact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/arts/television/younger-ages-into-a-second-season-on-tv-land.html', 'snippet': 'This drama about passing for a younger woman opens with its heroine’s workplace secret more or less intact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For women stung by ageism in the workplace, “Younger,” the Darren Star series on TV Land, might at first have seemed like a lame joke. Not the part where Liza, a divorced 40-year-old with an Ivy League degree played by Sutton Foster, struggles to re-enter the publishing world after a long absence taken to raise her daughter — that rang all too true. Rather, the part where she hooks up with a 26-year-old tattoo artist who eyes her fresh face and killer body and assumes she’s in his demographic. Which sparks the notion that, with a bit of cosmetic tweaking and online purging, she can shave off enough years to begin anew. Right. If only job security were as simple as calling your hair stylist.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE7/10GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Younger’ Ages Into a Second Season on TV Land', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; Passing for Young, but Not Entirely', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Younger (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TV Land', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Sutton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Star, Darren', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T19:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e672f6a-ddd7-5fdc-96da-7fa9b185d8f6', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e672f6a-ddd7-5fdc-96da-7fa9b185d8f6'}, {'abstract': 'Trial is set for Feb. 23 for Mr. Marquez, who is accused of supplying weapons to the couple, Syed Rizwan Farook and Tashfeen Malik, who killed 14 people in San Bernardino.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/us/san-bernardino-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Trial is set for Feb. 23 for Mr. Marquez, who is accused of supplying weapons to the couple, Syed Rizwan Farook and Tashfeen Malik, who killed 14 people in San Bernardino.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIVERSIDE, Calif. — Enrique Marquez pleaded not guilty Wednesday on charges of supplying two assault weapons that Syed Rizwan Farook and Tashfeen Malik used to massacre 14 people at the Inland Regional Center in San Bernardino last month. Mr. Marquez, dressed in a white jumpsuit, his legs and hand shackled, spoke in a clear voice as he entered his plea on that charge, as well as on counts that he and Mr. Farook had conspired on an earlier terrorist plot that was not carried out. Answering a series of questions from the United States Magistrate, Sheri Pym, Mr. Marquez said he had been informed of his constitutional rights and read the indictment. The hearing for Mr. Marquez, who is 24 and was a longtime friend of Mr. Farook’s, lasted just over four minutes. Ms. Pym set the trial for Feb. 23.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/28/us/22marquez-web/22marquez-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 265, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/28/us/22marquez-web/22marquez-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 265, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/28/us/22marquez-web/22marquez-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/12/28/us/22marquez-web/22marquez-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/28/us/22marquez-web/22marquez-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enrique Marquez Pleads Not Guilty in San Bernardino Massacre Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Briefing | West; California: Not-Guilty Plea to Gun Charge in Massacre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marquez, Enrique (1991- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'San Bernardino, Calif, Shooting (2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farook, Syed Rizwan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malik, Tashfeen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T19:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe9f3171-9299-534c-beb0-672f19bfbadd', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe9f3171-9299-534c-beb0-672f19bfbadd'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Museum recently acquired five wooden masks from the 18th century and has surrounded them with art that fleshes out a rapturous religious tale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/arts/design/hindu-heroes-savored-through-fantastical-masks-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Museum recently acquired five wooden masks from the 18th century and has surrounded them with art that fleshes out a rapturous religious tale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a short step from religious ritual to theater, and barely any distance at all in the case of certain popular Hindu dramas of southern India. Performed during seasonal festivals, they are epic in length — they go on for hours, often through the night — and fantastic in character, telling the stories of gods who have the adventure-filled lives of superheroes. You get a vivid sense of this proto-“Star Wars” mood in “Encountering Vishnu: The Lion Avatar in Indian Temple Drama” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art. The Met recently acquired five large 18th-century wooden masks created for a play about the god Vishnu who, in the guise of the lion-man called Narasimha, visited earth to defeat an evil king and restore order to the universe. The masks are stupendous, and paintings and prints that the Met has placed around them flesh out a tale that, even today, can inspire devotional rapture under the stars. (metmuseum.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 982, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1865, 'width': 1787, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE5SUB/10GUIDE5SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hindu Heroes, Savored Through Fantastical Masks at the Met', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art; Dazzling Exploits of Hindu Heroes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Encountering Vishnu: The Lion Avatar in Indian Temple Drama (Exhibit)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T19:12:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fe9fda5-c5ab-5059-ac36-ee8f8194996a', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fe9fda5-c5ab-5059-ac36-ee8f8194996a'}, {'abstract': 'As part of its series “The Contenders,” MoMA is screening this film starring Patrick Wilson and Kurt Russell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/movies/bone-tomahawk-gets-another-look.html', 'snippet': 'As part of its series “The Contenders,” MoMA is screening this film starring Patrick Wilson and Kurt Russell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patrick Wilson had a memorable 2015 in Season 2 of “Fargo,” the much-admired, marvelously off-kilter FX television series, but he was also part of another unorthodox project last year, the horror western “Bone Tomahawk.” The movie received a limited theatrical run in October but deserves much more, and the Museum of Modern Art is doing its part by giving it a showing at 7:30 p.m. on Tuesday, Jan. 12, in a series it calls “The Contenders,” which spotlights films of significance from last year that went relatively unnoticed.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE8/10GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/