ame': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c001e0-bde5-5c56-a966-7ba0dcf83e98', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c001e0-bde5-5c56-a966-7ba0dcf83e98'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Opera features Franco Zeffirelli’s production of Puccini’s “Turandot,” and the Juilliard School holds its ChamberFest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/arts/music/big-opera-or-cozy-concert-take-your-pick.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Opera features Franco Zeffirelli’s production of Puccini’s “Turandot,” and the Juilliard School holds its ChamberFest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grand and intimate square off across 65th Street this week. At the Metropolitan Opera, Franco Zeffirelli’s gargantuan production of Puccini’s “Turandot” returns with the formidable soprano Nina Stemme in the title role. (She portrays Strauss’s Elektra in April.) The experienced Paolo Carignani conducts, Marco Berti is Calaf, and Anita Hartig is Liù. But the real star is the Zeffirelli spectacle, alternately cheesy and enchanting. (7:30 p.m., Monday, Jan. 11, and 8 p.m., Friday, Jan. 15; metopera.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't