he president to protect his signature domestic achievement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As its opening move in the newly convened Congress, the House voted Wednesday to repeal the Affordable Care Act, the 62nd such vote but the first time that a bill will make it to President Obama’s desk, forcing a rare veto to protect his signature domestic achievement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Votes to Send Bill to Repeal Health Law to Obama’s Desk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Bill Undoing Health Law Makes It to Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vetoes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T23:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed44eb17-8f95-5077-adf2-223fe02c0b10', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed44eb17-8f95-5077-adf2-223fe02c0b10'}, {'abstract': 'Griffey, who received a record 99.3 percent of the vote, would be the first player with a Mariners cap on his plaque. Piazza, who got in on his fourth try, is likely to represent the Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/sports/baseball/ken-griffey-jr-and-mike-piazza-voted-into-baseball-hall-of-fame.html', 'snippet': 'Griffey, who received a record 99.3 percent of the vote, would be the first player with a Mariners cap on his plaque. Piazza, who got in on his fourth try, is likely to represent the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ken Griffey Jr. and Mike Piazza, two of the most prolific sluggers of the high-scoring 1990s, were elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame on Wednesday. Griffey, who slammed 630 home runs, was elected on the first ballot with a record 99.3 percent of votes cast by members of the Baseball Writers’ Association of America. Piazza, whose 396 homers as a catcher are the most for anyone at the position, got in on his fourth try, with 83 percent.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 297, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 297}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1013, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/sports/07HALLweb/07HALLweb-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ken Griffey Jr. and Mike Piazza Trot Into Baseball Hall of Fame', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Sluggers Trot to Cooperstown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piazza, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffey, Ken Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonds, Barry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGwire, Mark', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T23:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8fe48dd-450c-5e45-b545-ccaabe38ba43', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8fe48dd-450c-5e45-b545-ccaabe38ba43'}, {'abstract': 'A defender of federal employees’ rights and safety decries the slow government response to the occupation of a national wildlife refuge.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/06/the-fear-factor-for-federal-workers-as-refuge-occupation-goes-unchallenged/', 'snippet': 'A defender of federal employees’ rights and safety decries the slow government response to the occupation of a national wildlife refuge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Ruch, who directs Public Employees for Environmental Responsibility, sent a fresh note about an under-appreciated risk that’s building as long as federal authorities don’t directly challenge the anti-government zealots who’ve taken over Oregon’s Malheur National Wildlife Refuge. The lack of response, while wise in many ways (as I wrote yesterday), could send a signal to other extremists that they can challenge the government with impunity. This puts federal employees at risk, particularly those in agencies that are a popular target in the West, particularly the Bureau of Land Management.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/opinion/RFDOregon/RFDOregon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear Factor Rising for Federal Workers as Refuge Occupation Goes Unchallenged', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malheur National Wildlife Refuge (Oregon)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-06T23:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7891d066-7972-5d45-8f86-92c5dab17f67', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7891d066-7972-5d45-8f86-92c5dab17f67'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cruz visited a Godfather’s Pizza in Spirit Lake and, when asked about gun rights, recounted a tale of a woman who had been pulled over while carrying a derringer in her boot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/06/ted-cr