ational Herald Tribune archives: Roosevelt creates a board to oversee arms production in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Roosevelt acted promptly today [Jan. 7] in furtherance of his pledge to Congress yesterday to defend democracy by sending ‘‘ever-increasing’’ numbers of warplanes, guns, tanks and ships to Great Britain, China and Greece. The action took the form of creating the Office of Production Management, whose duties, in brief, will be to speed up production of warplanes and all other essential war supplies in the interest not only of the United States but of Great Britain and all other countries which are resisting aggression by the Berlin-Rome-Tokio axis.\xa0—\xa0New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 8, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/blogs/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/08/blogs/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/blogs/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 716, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/blogs/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 716, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/blogs/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt/08iht-oldjan08-roosevelt-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75,