/2016/01/07/arts/television/american-horror-story-hotel-review.html', 'snippet': 'In which we finally figure out what this season is actually about: stagnation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was somewhere during this penultimate episode of the fifth season of “American Horror Story” that I finally realized what the season is actually about: stagnation. For all the creepiness that a hotel’s transience lends to a story, what about the people who never leave? The Liz Taylors, the Irises, stuck watching as their lives pass them by, or Sally and March, stuck as the living pass them by.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/arts/07HOTEL/07HOTEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 1