tml', 'snippet': 'The new GLC300 is drawn with softer lines than the GLK and is also roomier and 175 pounds lighter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MERCEDES-BENZ isn’t new to the midsize crossover market. Its angular GLK arrived in America in 2009. Its replacement does far more than swap the letter K for a C. The new GLC300 is drawn with softer lines, reminiscent of the long-nose C-Class sedan. And why not? They share architectures.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 311}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1063, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/05/multimedia/driven-mercedes-glc300/driven-mercedes-glc300-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Review: Mercedes GLC300 Is a Midsize Crossover With Few Faults', 'kicker': 'Driven', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mercedes GLC300: A Midsize Crossover With Few Faults', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-07T16:26:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8a35dd4-f692-5a29-8b9f-de2559058b2b', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8a35dd4-f692-5a29-8b9f-de2559058b2b'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Weller of Sadelle’s in SoHo sips a daily turmeric tonic first thing in the morning to compensate for her work diet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/t-magazine/food/ginger-turmeric-juice-recipe-melissa-weller.html', 'snippet': 'Melissa Weller of Sadelle’s in SoHo sips a daily turmeric tonic first thing in the morning to compensate for her work diet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A life of everything bagel sandwiches and warm sticky buns can take its toll. “I do a lot of baking and tasting of baked goods while I work, and I compensate by eating lots of vegetables and legumes, and drinking a lot of water,” says Melissa Weller, the celebrated baker at the popular SoHo restaurant Sadelle’s, a New York Times Critics’ Pick, reviewed by Pete Wells this week. With balance as her goal, there are times when the baker completely eliminates dairy and sugar (and alcohol) from her diet. “I will still taste what I am baking at work, but only small tastes,” she says. Her other line of defense? A daily turmeric tonic. “I go to this first thing in the morning when I wake up,” says Weller, who started making the drink about a year ago at home. (Sqirl’s Jessica Koslow also touts turmeric for its restorative properties.) But babka lovers, have no fear: There are no plans of adding this drink to the menu anytime soon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/t-magazine/07tmag-weller1/07tmag-weller1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/07/t-magazine/07tmag-weller1/07tmag-weller1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/t-magazine/07tmag-weller1/07tmag-weller1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/t-magazine/07tmag-weller1/07tmag-weller1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/07/t-magazine/07tmag-weller1/07tmag-weller1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/07/t-magazine/07tmag-weller1/07tmag-weller1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/0