rs-relives-a-perilous-forgotten-rescue.html', 'snippet': 'The film explores a maritime incident from 1952 that naval historians refer to as the greatest small-boat rescue in history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'QUINCY, MASS. — “The Finest Hours,” which opens Jan. 29, is very closely based on a real-life rescue that took place at sea in February 1952, when, during a nor’easter at least as fierce as the one immortalized in “The Perfect Storm,” not one but two oil tankers broke apart off the coast of Cape Cod. They were T2’s, ships hastily built of inferior metal during World War II and sometimes known as “serial sinkers” for their tendency to snap in half during cold weather.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/arts/10FINESTHRS3/10FINESTHRS3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Finest Hours’ Relives a Perilous, Forgotten Rescue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reliving a Perilous, Forgotten Rescue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillespie, Craig', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pine, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Affleck, Casey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape Cod (Mass)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Perfect Storm (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Finest Hours (Movie)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Finest Hours: The True Story of the US Coast Guard's Most Daring Sea Rescue (Book)", 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-07T17:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29174ba0-4480-57d7-b2dd-766332dec8b2', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29174ba0-4480-57d7-b2dd-766332dec8b2'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Stephen Petronio, who is beginning a $3 million campaign to establish a choreographic residency program in Pawling, N.Y., announced Thursday that he had received a gift from the artist Anish Kapoor.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/07/stephen-petronio-and-anish-kapoor-team-up-to-sell-art-for-dances-sake/', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Stephen Petronio, who is beginning a $3 million campaign to establish a choreographic residency program in Pawling, N.Y., announced Thursday that he had received a gift from the artist Anish Kapoor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once again the world of visual art, which creates durable works that can command astronomical prices, is coming to the aid of the world of performing arts, in which it is increasingly difficult to find the money to create and present works that last just until the curtain falls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephen Petronio and Anish Kapoor Team Up to Sell Art for Dance’s Sake', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petronio, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petronio, Stephen, Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catskills (NYS Area)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pawling (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-07T17:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/643f4900-0570-57b9-9d53-27c5d7e48f7a', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/643f4900-0570-57b9-9d53-27c5d7e48f7a'}, {'abstract': 'Corneliu Porumboiu, this film’s director, waits for dramatic events to arise instead of forcing the action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/08/movies/review-in-the-treasure-digging-for-something-of-value-in-romania.html', 'snippet': 'Corneliu Porumboiu, this film’s director, waits for dramatic events to arise instead of forcing the action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Costi, the Romanian Everyman at the center of “The Treasure,” leads a reasonably comfortable if not terribly exciting life. Played by Cuzin Toma, an actor with a melancholy, sensitive face and a gentle manner, Costi has an office job and a tidy, somewhat sterile apartment, where he lives with his wife, Raluca, and their young son, Alin (played by Mr. Toma’s real-life wife and son, Cristina and Nicodim). The boy likes to hear fairy tales at bedtime, and his father soon finds himself on an adventure that has all the markings of a modern fable.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08TREASURE/08TREASURE-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘The Treasure,’ Digging for Something of Value in Romania', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Digging for a Future  in Soil Unblessed  by Enchantment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porumboiu, Corneliu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toma, Cuzin (1977- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Treasure (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-07T17:04:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8587bf3-4d18-56d1-a088-3143c6298f6a', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8587bf3-4d18-56d1-a088-3143c6298f6a'}, {'abstract': 'An agreement, coming as the city moves to settle lawsuits over surveillance targeting Muslims, would restore some of the outside oversight that was eliminated after the Sept. 11 attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/08/nyregion/new-york-to-appoint-monitor-to-review-polices-counterterrorism-activity.html', 'snippet': 'An agreement, coming as the city moves to settle lawsuits over surveillance targeting Muslims, would restore some of the outside oversight that was eliminated after the Sept. 11 attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mayor will appoint an independent civilian to monitor the New York Police Department’s counterterrorism activities, lawyers said in court documents on Thursday as they moved to settle a pair of lawsuits over surveillance targeting Muslims in the decade after the Sept. 11 attacks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/nyregion/08SURVEILLANCE2/08SURVEILLANCE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/08/nyregion/08SURVEILLANCE2/08SURVEILLANCE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/nyregion/08SURVEILLANCE2/08SURVEILLANCE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/nyregion/08SURVEILLANCE2/08SURVEILLANCE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/nyregion/08SURVEILLANCE2/08SURVEILLANCE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/08/nyregion/08SURVEILLANCE2/08SURVEILLANCE2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth