1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11b254ca-6fd3-5fff-8050-85bf73219e0f', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11b254ca-6fd3-5fff-8050-85bf73219e0f'}, {'abstract': 'A new period room at the Metropolitan Museum of Art showcases 19th-century design, alongside an exhibition focused on furniture from the era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/08/arts/design/peeking-into-the-gilded-age-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'A new period room at the Metropolitan Museum of Art showcases 19th-century design, alongside an exhibition focused on furniture from the era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art recently unveiled a new period room, and it’s a beauty. Called the Worsham-Rockefeller Dressing Room, it’s a consummate expression of Aestheticism, a trans-Atlantic, 19th-century design movement that combined European Renaissance, Modern, Islamic and Japanese styles into luxurious objects and sumptuous environments for well-to-do hedonists. Having recently undergone conservation by the Met, the dressing room joins 19 other period rooms in the museum’s American Wing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08GILDEDJP1/08GILDEDJP1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08GILDEDJP1/08GILDEDJP1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08GILDEDJP1/08GILDEDJP1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08GILDEDJP1/08GILDEDJP1-superJumbo-v3.jpg