ng by combining art owned and borrowed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julie Ault’s art mediums are collaboration and accumulation. She was a co-founder in 1980 of Group Material, a collective that treated archival-style installations as walk-through art objects. She created a memorable 2013 solo show at Artists Space, “Macho Man: Tell It to My Heart,” entirely from her personal collection of work by other artists gathered over many years. In the 2014 Whitney Biennial, she further expanded on this method of expressive, highly individualized curating by combining art owned and borrowed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08AULTGALLERY1/08AULTGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08AULTGALLERY1/08AULTGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08AULTGALLERY1/08AULTGALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08AULTGALLERY1/08AULTGALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08AULTGALLERY1/08AULTGALLERY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08AULTGALLERY1/08AULTGALLERY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capti