a63'}, {'abstract': 'In “Inverted Birth,” slow-motion and reverse techniques are used to dramatic effect with a flood of water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/08/arts/design/bill-violas-new-video-project-is-a-rebirth-of-sorts.html', 'snippet': 'In “Inverted Birth,” slow-motion and reverse techniques are used to dramatic effect with a flood of water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Viola goes for big, cosmic themes, which he funnels into technically impressive video works of compelling, quasi-religious sincerity. The main event of this exhibition is an awesome video called “Inverted Birth.” The 15-foot-tall projection shows in slow motion and in reverse a man standing on a bare stage as he is subjected to a tremendous deluge of liquid. This is accompanied by the electronically amplified roar of pouring water.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08VIOLAGALLERY4/08VIOLAGALLERY4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08VIOLAGALLERY4/08VIOLAGALLERY4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1067}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08VIOLAGALLERY4/08VIOLAGALLERY4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08VIOLAGALLERY4/08VIOLAGALLERY4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1919, 'width': 1079, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/08/arts/08VIOLAGALLERY4/08VIOLAGALLERY4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi