Boy,” a new exhibition at the London College of Fashion, opens on the eve of the men’s shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomorrow, men’s shows will officially begin in London — and just in time comes an exhibition, “Mad About the Boy,” that puts it all in context. Held in the gallery of the London College of Fashion, the show examines the link between garments on the catwalk and the youth tropes they drew inspiration from, and vice versa. Silhouettes from designers including Raf Simons, J.W. Anderson and Christopher Shannon are shown alongside fashion, street and documentary images.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In London, an Exploration of Men’s Wear and Youth Culture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Raf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'J W Anderson (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-07T21:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hettie Judah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hettie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Judah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13822211-4809-5b90-8092-366c776a26db', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13822211-4809-5b90-8092-366c776a26db'}, {'abstract': "Above and beyond the Angel of Independence monument in the city's Paseo de la Reforma.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/tr