d 19 percent. The two men emerged from a field of 30 in an election that, while peaceful, involved logistical problems and prompted allegations of fraud. Candidates can appeal to the Constitutional Court, which has 15 days to review any appeals and validate the final results. The runoff is scheduled for Jan. 31. Sectarian violence between Christians and Muslims in the past several years has caused nearly a million people to flee their homes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Central African Republic: Runoff Is Set for Presidential Candidates', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; Central African Republic: Runoff Is Set for Presidential Candidates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dologuele, Anicet-Georges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Touadera, Faustin-Archange', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-08T02:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaux Benn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaux', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf50185-b507-5ce0-bdd3-0c7a74e0414f', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf50185-b507-5ce0-bdd3-0c7a74e0414f'}, {'abstract': 'The days on which alternate-side street-cleaning rules will be suspended in New York City in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/01/07/nyregion/alternate-side-parking-holidays-2016.html', 'snippet': 'The days on which alternate-side street-cleaning rules wi