enan.html', 'snippet': 'The 120-foot-tall structure, said to have cost $465,000, had been under construction for months when it began to attract attention online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZHUSHIGANG, China — Just two days after images of a giant gold-colored statue of Mao in the bare fields of Henan Province spread across the Internet, the statue was gone — torn down apparently on the orders of embarrassed local officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/06/world/06CHINAMAO01/06CHINAMAO01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Golden Mao Statue in China, Nearly Finished, Is Brought Down by Criticism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Outcry Helps Topple a Mao Statue 120 Feet Tall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tatlow, Didi Kirsten', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Henan Province (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zhushigang (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-08T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bd9ad6d-7c4c-5f41-9e8f-443af002a87d', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bd9ad6d-7c4c-5f41-9e8f-443af002a87d'}, {'abstract': 'Society is getting a free ride on our unrewarded contributions to the perpetuation of the human race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/payback-time-for-women.html', 'snippet': 'Society is getting a free ride on our unrewarded contributions to the perpetuation of the human race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A COUNTRY that gives every citizen enough cash to live on whether she needs it or not: It’s got to be either a fool’s paradise or a profligate Northern European nation. And lo, in November, the Finnish government proposed paying every adult 800 euros or about $870 a month. Fits of this seemingly irrational generosity, called a universal basic income or U.B.I., are becoming surprisingly common. The Swiss will vote in a referendum on basic income this year. The Dutch city of Utrecht will soon  start a basic-income pilot program. Canada’s ruling Liberal Party recently adopted a resolution calling for a similar experiment.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 659}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 933, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1865, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/opinion/sunday/10shulevitz/10shulevitz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': '