onal Herald Tribune archives: Ducks cause changes in anti-aircraft training in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMP UPTON, L.I. — Ducks, for the second time in less than a month, have been the cause of changes in anti-aircraft training here. The first time it was wild ducks, which interfered with firing of anti-aircraft batteries. Now, because of the nerves of market ducks on the south shore duck farms, anti-aircraft searchlights of the 198th Coast Artillery Regiment will be directed only north and west of the camp. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/blogs/09iht-oldjan09-camp/09iht-oldjan09-camp-articleLarge.png', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/09/blogs/09iht-oldjan09-camp/09iht-oldjan09-camp-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/blogs/09iht-oldjan09-camp/09iht-oldjan09-camp-jumbo.png', 'height': 403, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/blogs/09iht-oldjan09-camp/09iht-oldjan09-camp-superJumbo.png', 'height': 403, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/blogs/09iht-oldjan09-camp/09iht-oldjan09-camp-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/09/blogs/09iht-oldjan09-camp/09iht-oldjan09-camp-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':