organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c9ba35a-1d70-5ebb-a047-418f8085bf3b', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c9ba35a-1d70-5ebb-a047-418f8085bf3b'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel’s legacy in an age of gridlock.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/08/rahm-and-his-party/', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel’s legacy in an age of gridlock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall of Rahm Emanuel, seemingly a political\xa0dead man walking because of\xa0his alleged role in covering up the video showing Chicago cops shooting a black teenager, has united right and left in schadenfreude. The right is delighted because Emanuel is a prominent overclass Democrat, an enforcer for\xa0the last two Democratic presidents, the man who led the midterm “thumping” that undid George W. Bush’s congressional majorities in 2006, and the mayor of a city that’s a case study in one-party misgovernment. The left, meanwhile, is happy to see him fall because Emanuel is a prominent centrist Democrat, whose role in both the Clinton and Obama White Houses involved prodding his bosses to temper their liberalism and tack somewhat to the right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rahm and His Party', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American Free Trade Agreement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Part