'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b565844-ece7-5ea8-ad1a-5afa14c6c907', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b565844-ece7-5ea8-ad1a-5afa14c6c907'}, {'abstract': 'Rosanna Pansino, whose “The Nerdy Nummies Cookbook” is No. 5 on the food and fitness list, is a YouTube star with more than three million subscribers to her online baking show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Rosanna Pansino, whose “The Nerdy Nummies Cookbook” is No. 5 on the food and fitness list, is a YouTube star with more than three million subscribers to her online baking show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sugar and Spice: Every year around this time, when people are still recovering from the holidays and the main hardcover lists have settled into deep-freeze mode — a single new entry in the past four weeks! — it has become traditional for Inside the List to wander a little afield. Sometimes we reprint a list from years past. Sometimes we ask best-selling authors for their book-related wish lists or resolutions. This year, we bring you cookies: specifically, Rosanna Pansino’s atom cookies, from “The Nerdy Nummies Cookbook,” at No.\u202f5 in its second month on the food and fitness list (available online). Pansino belongs to the growing club of YouTube stars who have crossed over into publishing; her online baking show, also called “Nerdy Nummies,” has more than three million subscribers who watch her take goofy delight in treats like doughnut waffles. (These are, literally, store-bought glazed doughnuts, heated and pressed in a home waffle iron. I’m not sure that qualifies as baking, but it sounds amazing.) If you suspect that Pansino’s appeal has as much to do with charm and presentation as with the actual recipes, her book probably won’t change your mind. But she is charming, in her way. Here’s how she introduces those atom cookies, which are just six-pointed sugar cookies iced and decorated to resemble a science class’s atom model, with an M&M nucleus and candy pearl electrons: “Atoms are the building blocks of every type of matter in the universe — even you! My grandfather was a nuclear physicist, my uncle followed in his footsteps, and my dad’s old high school even had an atom on its emblem. I guess you could say we have an atomic bond. I decorated my atoms green, blue and purple, but you can make your atom cookies any color you want. Just remember: Never trust an atom .\u2008.\u2008. they make up everything!”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17list-image/17list-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 453, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17list-image/17list-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 453, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17list-image/17list-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17list-image/17list-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17list-image/17list-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}],