y braced for powerful forces: the swaggering yuppiedom of “Bonfire of the Vanities” and Oliver Stone’s “Wall Street” (both 1987); the AIDS epidemic and the crack wars; the graffiti boom and the golden age of New York hip-hop. For the photographer Janet Delaney, who visited regularly from the West Coast, between trips to Nicaragua, New York in the mid-1980s was a street theater where people wore their anxieties on their faces, a city that looked you in the eye. It was also a tough place to break into as an outsider, she said.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/nyregion/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/nyregion/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 593}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/nyregion/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1012, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/nyregion/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/nyregion/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/nyregion/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T/10ALBUMSS-slide-605T-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ra