ail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/fashion/10PARTY/10PARTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/fashion/10PARTY/10PARTY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Evening Hours | New Year’s Eve at the Metropolitan Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-08T23:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By BILL CUNNINGHAM', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CUNNINGHAM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a32f0a0d-f21f-5923-90fd-0289076f2647', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a32f0a0d-f21f-5923-90fd-0289076f2647'}, {'abstract': 'States not complying with federal requirements for extra safety features in driving licenses gain a two-year extension before residents must use a passport or other government ID to board a flight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/09/business/us-gives-states-2-more-years-to-meet-drivers-license-standards.html', 'snippet': 'States not complying with federal requirements for extra safety features in driving licenses gain a two-year extension before residents must use a passport or other government ID to board a flight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Homeland Security has given states an extra two years to comply with federal requirements to issue driving licenses with extra safety features, meaning that residents of noncompliant states will have until January 2018 before having to use a passport or other official identification to board a domestic flight.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Gives States 2 More Years to Meet Driver’s License Standards', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Government Gives States 2 Additional Years to Meet Driver&#8217;s License Standards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drivers Licenses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Conference of State Legislatures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:14:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d2149b7-3c0e-57ae-bf1f-18f442809ceb', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d2149b7-3c0e-57ae-bf1f-18f442809ceb'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrations in São Paulo, Rio de Janeiro and Belo Horizonte reflected resentment over efforts to cover budget shortfalls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/09/world/americas/brazil-protest-over-higher-bus-fares-erupt-in-3-cities.html', 'snippet': 'Demonstrations in São Paulo, Rio de Janeiro and Belo Horizonte reflected resentment over efforts to cover budget shortfalls.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Protests flared in the cities of São Paulo, Rio de Janeiro and Belo Horizonte on Friday night over increases in bus fares, reflecting resentment over efforts by the municipal authorities to cover budget shortfalls during Brazil’s most severe economic crisis in decades. Anti-riot police units clashed with protesters in downtown São Paulo. The unrest drew comparisons to the much larger demonstrations that shook cities across Brazil in 2013, which also crystallized over increases in bus fares. Some of the demonstrators in São Paulo destroyed buses, ransacked banking offices and threw rocks and bottles at the police, who used tear gas. Clashes also erupted between the police and protesters in downtown Rio de Janeiro. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: Protest Over Higher Bus Fares Erupt in 3 Cities', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Americas; Brazil: Protests Over Higher Bus Fares Erupt in 3 Cities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank':