o are a regular feature on television news programs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Cause of Crises? For Rio Governor, Life Incriminates Art ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cause of Crises? For Rio Governor, Life Incriminates Art ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:39:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9dc0a7d-f1b9-5107-a034-8412d559df8f', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9dc0a7d-f1b9-5107-a034-8412d559df8f'}, {'abstract': 'Head wraps were inventively stylish, and fur bonnets were a favorite. Men wore shearling coats, and one woman swirled in a pleated Chanel coat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/fashion/bill-cunningham-winter-flair.html', 'snippet': 'Head wraps were inventively stylish, and fur bonnets were a favorite. Men wore shearling coats, and one woman swirled in a pleated Chanel coat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The doggies on Fifth Avenue were snuggled into winter coats, and the fountain in Bryant Park was a cascade of icicles. Head wraps were inventively stylish, and fur bonnets were a favorite. Men wore shearling coats, and one woman swirled in a pleated Chanel coat. Cat-eye bags provided a touch of whimsy.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Winter Flair', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winter Flair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coats and Jackets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5acc6fa5-618b-5fa3-bcd4-e38bbd763ba6', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5acc6fa5-618b-5fa3-bcd4-e38bbd763ba6'}, {'abstract': 'Talking about Hillary Clinton and Benghazi, Ted Cruz notes that his 5-year-old daughter gets a spanking when she lies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/08/ted-cruzs-iowa-bus-tour-benghazi-and-the-benefits-of-spanking/', 'snippet': 'Talking about Hillary Clinton and Benghazi, Ted Cruz notes that his 5-year-old daughter gets a spanking when she lies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ted Cruz is on a six-day, 28-town swing through Iowa. These are\xa0the places, faces and culinary selections\xa0of 2016’s first proper bus tour.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/us/08firstdraft-cruzcharlescity/08firstdraft-cruzcharlescity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width