, 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:47:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2048eb5a-30fe-52be-a3cb-2d9696ce43f0', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2048eb5a-30fe-52be-a3cb-2d9696ce43f0'}, {'abstract': 'General José Guillermo García, who was minister of defense in El Salvador in the 1980s, was deported after an immigration judge found he assisted in torture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/09/us/florida-ex-leader-of-salvadoran-military-deported.html', 'snippet': 'General José Guillermo García, who was minister of defense in El Salvador in the 1980s, was deported after an immigration judge found he assisted in torture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The authorities have deported General José Guillermo García, who was minister of defense in El Salvador in the 1980s, after an immigration judge found that he had a role in human rights violations in that period, including in the 1980 slaying of Archbishop Óscar Arnulfo Romero while the prelate was saying Mass in San Salvador. In a decision in February 2014, the judge found that General García, a close ally of the United States during the Salvadoran civil war, should be deported for assisting “numerous acts of torture and extrajudicial killing while he was command,” a Department of Homeland Security news release said. An appeal by General García, 82, of the lower court ruling was denied on Dec. 8. He was arrested on Dec. 17 at his home in Florida, where he had been living for many years, and was flown to San Salvador on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Ex-Leader of Salvadoran Military Deported ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Ex-Leader of Salvadoran Military Deported ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Jose Guillermo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Salvador', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f5ea3ec-fd3d-566c-8d6a-41fc5ebbcc72', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f5ea3ec-fd3d-566c-8d6a-41fc5ebbcc72'}, {'abstract': 'Air-quality regulators have reached an agreement with the Southern California Gas Company to capture and burn off some of the natural gas escaping from a blown-out well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/09/us/california-gas-leaking-in-neighborhood-to-be-burned.html', 'snippet': 'Air-quality regulators have reached an agreement with the Southern California Gas Company to capture and burn off some of the natural gas escaping from a blown-out well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Air-quality regulators have reached an agreement with the Southern California Gas Company to capture and burn off some of the natural gas escaping from a blown-out well, which continues to pump tons of methane, a powerful greenhouse gas, into the air and has sickened residents in the nearby Los Angeles neighborhood of Porter Ranch. The gas company will take measures within 10 days to use carbon absorbers and thermal oxidizers to capture and burn off some of the gas, according to the regulators. Though regulators still do not know exactly how much gas is escaping, they acknowledged it would not be possible to capture all of it. The agreement requires the gas company to conduct extensive air-quality monitoring, and to pay for a study of the leak’s effect on residents’ health. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Gas Leaking in Neighborhood to Be Burned', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Gas Leaking in Neighborhood to Be Burned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern California Gas Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T00:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/247273e9-dfcd-5d34-bab3-30826b46de48', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247273e9-dfcd-5d34-bab3-30826b46de48'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty, a Dalmatian given to a firehouse that suffered heavy losses on Sept. 11, 2001, died on Tuesday after years of living among the firefighters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/09/nyregion/firehouse-loses-a-spotted-symbol-of-healing.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty, a Dalmatian given to a firehouse that suffered heavy losses on Sept. 11, 2001, died on Tuesday after years of living among the firefighters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 11, 2001, seven members of Ladder Company 20 on Lafayette Street in the NoLIta neighborhood of Manhattan were killed in the collapse of the World Trade Center, about a mile and a half away, along with seven members of Squad 18, which shared the firehouse at the time with the ladder company.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/nyregion/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/09/nyregion/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/nyregion/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/nyregion/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/nyregion/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1/09FIREHOUSEDOGweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'heig