N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Union City (NJ)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-09T20:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David L. Kirp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Kirp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2469cec-c094-57ee-b292-69ce8b1b5961', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2469cec-c094-57ee-b292-69ce8b1b5961'}, {'abstract': 'Washington won its division this season behind Kirk Cousins, after a wild-card loss in 2013 in which their star quarterback was injured sent the franchise into disarray.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/sports/football/back-in-postseason-the-washington-redskins-move-on-from-a-loss-that-lingered.html', 'snippet': 'Washington won its division this season behind Kirk Cousins, after a wild-card loss in 2013 in which their star quarterback was injured sent the franchise into disarray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASHBURN, Va. — For a long time, the Washington Redskins have been trying to exorcise the demons of their last playoff appearance. On Jan. 6, 2013, they were riding a seven-game winning streak, and Robert Griffin III, a rookie sensation and franchise quarterback in the making, was the N.F.L.’s hottest story. The Redskins even grabbed a 14-0 lead in their wild-card game against the Seattle Seahawks before a hobbled Griffin tore the anterior cruciate ligament in his right knee, and his team lost, 24-14.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10cousins/10cousins-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei