ense picked off four Brian Hoyer passes and recovered one of his two fumbles, while its offense capitalized on the miscues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/sports/football/kansas-city-chiefs-beat-houston-texans-wild-card.html', 'snippet': 'Kansas City followed its script to late season success: Its defense picked off four Brian Hoyer passes and recovered one of his two fumbles, while its offense capitalized on the miscues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — The last time the Kansas City Chiefs won a playoff game, Joe Montana was their quarterback, Michael Jordan wanted a tryout with the Chicago White Sox, and Sonic the Hedgehog was all the rage. The team’s owner, Clark Hunt, was 28 years old.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1279, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/sports/10CHIEFSTEXANS/10CHIEFSTEXANS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chiefs End 22-Year Run of Playoff Futility by Thrashing the Texans', 'kicker': 'Chiefs 30, Texans 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chiefs End 22-Year Run of Playoff Futility by Thrashing the Texans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-10T01:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b2d1260-e89f-559e-8a57-c5f9d1885916', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b2d1260-e89f-559e-8a57-c5f9d1885916'}, {'abstract': 'In Iowa City and Des Moines, Ms. Dunham made a feminist pitch to packed audiences of mostly young women about why they should vote for Mrs. Clinton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/10/us/politics/girls-creator-visits-iowa-on-tour-to-support-hillary-clinton.html', 'snippet': 'In Iowa City and Des Moines, Ms. Dunham made a feminist pitch to packed audiences of mostly young women about why they should vote for Mrs. Clinton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IOWA CITY — When Hannah Horvath, the lead character of the hit HBO series “Girls,” arrived in Iowa during the show’s fourth season, the Brooklyn transplant was struck by the quietude, the cheap real estate and the fresh produce that is pervasive in America’s heartland. The infatuation faded, however, and she soon quit and returned home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/10/us/10dunham-web1/10dunham-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Girls’ Creator Lena Dunham Visits Iowa on Tour to Support Hillary