d51df0-03de-590c-88a8-f368ed00f562', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcd51df0-03de-590c-88a8-f368ed00f562'}, {'abstract': 'On a potential game-winning kick against the Seahawks, Vikings kicker Blair Walsh was presented with a problem: The laces were facing him. He missed the 27-yarder, and Seattle escaped with a victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/11/sports/football/nfl-playoffs-seattle-seahawks-beat-minnesota-vikings.html', 'snippet': 'On a potential game-winning kick against the Seahawks, Vikings kicker Blair Walsh was presented with a problem: The laces were facing him. He missed the 27-yarder, and Seattle escaped with a victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — There is only one lace, threaded through 16 holes, on an official N.F.L. game ball. When a holder sets the ball for a kicker, the rule of thumb is “laces out” — meaning the holder should rotate the ball to put the lace on the side facing the goal posts. Something about the way that white strip meets the kicker’s foot can make the ball fly in unpredictable directions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1593, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/11/sports/11jpVIKING2/11jpVIKING2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Ball’s Lace Facing Wrong Way, Seahawks Win by a Thread', 'kicker': 'Seahawks 10, Vikings 9', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Ball&#8217;s Lace Facing Wrong Way, Seahawks Win by a Thread', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borzi, Pat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Vikings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Doug (1988- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peterson, Adrian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Russell (1988- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, Blair (1990- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-10T21:49:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f44dc62a-1ef2-57ff-8440-3c1d4c74ae4f', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f44dc62a-1ef2-57ff-8440-3c1d4c74ae4f'}, {'abstract': 'Until now, writes Iran’s foreign minister, Tehran has acted with restraint toward Riyadh’s provocations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/11/opinion/mohammad-javad-zarif-saudi-arabias-reckless-extremism.html', 'snippet': 'Until now, writes Iran’s foreign minister, Tehran has acted with restraint toward Riyadh’s provocations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE world will soon celebrate the implementation of the landmark agreement that resolves the unnecessary, albeit dangerous, crisis over Iran’s nuclear program. All parties hoped, and continue to believe, that the resolution of the nuclear issue would enable us to focus on the serious challenge of extremism that is ravaging our region — and the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mohammad Javad Zarif: Saudi Arabia’s Reckless Extremism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riyadh’s Reckless Extremism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zarif, Mohammad Javad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nimr, Nimr al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-10T21:49:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohammad Javad Zarif', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohammad', 'middlename'