in-great-britain/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Draft is likely to be voted in Great Britain in 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The debate on the second reading of the Military Service Bill opened in the House of Commons today [Jan. 11] with every indication that Mr. Asquith’s proposals for limited compulsory service will be adopted by a very large majority. After a meeting of the Irish Nationalists today, Mr. Redmond has announced in Parliament the withdrawal of Irish opposition to the Bill, and the Government’s only serious opponents are now a section of the Labor Party and a few Radicals. Even in regard to the attitude of organized labor, a settlement of differences seems probable.— The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 12, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Draft Is Likely In Great Britain', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Commons (Great Britain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T15:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf054a1e-e788-5354-8b35-c974b84b47ad', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf054a1e-e788-5354-8b35-c974b84b47ad'}, {'abstract': 'Ringling Bros. and Barnum & Bailey said it would phase out its elephants show earlier than planned, sending the animals to a conservation cente