ay at the group’s midwinter conference in Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt de la Peña’s illustrated children’s book, “Last Stop on Market Street,” about a boy’s reflections during a bus ride to a soup kitchen with his grandmother, won the John Newbery Medal for the most outstanding contribution to children’s literature, a rare honor for a picture book.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children’s Book Awards Honor Diversity', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Newbery and Caldecott Go to Diverse Laureates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LIBRARY ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T18:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Alter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17606477-64b2-51b7-af3d-abc5bceb488f', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17606477-64b2-51b7-af3d-abc5bceb488f'}, {'abstract': 'As human resource departments look to reward employees without paying more, the idea of team-building through offsite gatherings is growing in popularity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/business/hotels-company-retreats.html', 'snippet': 'As human resource departments look to reward employees without paying more, the idea of team-building through offsite gatherings is growing in popularity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joshua Reeves, the co-fou