y’s internal watchdog.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Human Traffickers Found to Exploit U.S. Visas and Data-Sharing Failures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Report Faults Agencies on Visas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'San Bernardino, Calif, Shooting (2015)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizenship and Immigration Services (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Office of Inspector General', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forced Labor', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T18:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ccafca-b939-5318-9d33-f86e278e4e7e', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ccafca-b939-5318-9d33-f86e278e4e7e'}, {'abstract': '“Bowie bonds” inspired a wave of esoteric asset-backed securities deals based on intellectual property.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/business/dealbook/how-david-bowie-changed-wall-street.html', 'snippet': '“Bowie bonds” inspired a wave of esoteric asset-backed securities deals based on intellectual property.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Bowie was known for his ability to reinvent himself. But he also helped inspire a pocket of Wall Street that tries to create money out of weird things like billboard rental income, cellphone tower lease payments and literary or film libraries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How David Bowie Changed Wall Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowie, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royalties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prudential Financial Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T19:08:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Moyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a99a7ace-0dbf-5264-a1ef-7066fd63213e', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a99a7ace-0dbf-5264-a1ef-7066fd63213e'}, {'abstract': 'Also, horseradish from Long Island; discussing and eating Jewish deli food; mint from the Pacific Northwest; a gin manual; and sausage from California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/dining/supercrown-coffee-roasters-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Also, horseradish from Long Island; discussing and eating Jewish deli food; mint from the Pacific Northwest; a gin manual; and sausage from California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Darleen Scherer, who founded Gorilla Coffee in Park Slope, Brooklyn, sold her interest last year and has gone on to open Supercrown Coffee Roasters, a combination cafe, retail shop and coffee roaster with a behemoth of a German roasting machine positioned in full view. The coffees include some from Indonesia, like Sulawesi, with rewarding depth and balance. And she has staked out some unusual territory in coffee drinks. There’s a decadent coffee milkshake made with Ample Hills ice cream, and once the weather warms, a Scandinavian-style blend of coffee and lemonade that may be an acquired taste. To eat, there are pastries from Brooklyn purveyors like Bien Cuit and bialys, onion and prosciutto, made by Roberta’s and topped with poached eggs: Supercrown Coffee Roasters, 8 Wilson Avenue (Flushing Avenue), Bushwick, Brooklyn, 347-295-3161; supercrown.coffee.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/dining/13BURNER3/13BURNER3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/13/dining/13BURNER3/13BURNER3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/dining/13BURNER3/13BURNER3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType'