 look at Pennsylvania Station’s past uncovers treasures in The Times’s photo archive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any chance to explore the history of old Pennsylvania Station in mid-Manhattan underscores the wealth of The Times’s photo and clipping archive. We’ve come to call it the “lively morgue” for a very good reason: Its holdings, numbering in the millions (though stored under precarious conditions in the basement of an abutting office building), don’t just illuminate the past but breathe life into it. They warrant a regular feature on Tumblr.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/insider/09insider-penn-03-babe/09insider-penn-03-babe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/09/insider/09insider-penn-03-babe/09insider-penn-03-babe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 692}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/insider/09insider-penn-03-babe/09insider-penn-03-babe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 888, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/insider/09insider-penn-03-babe/09insider-penn-03-babe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1776, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/09/insider/09insider-penn-03-babe/09insider-penn-03-babe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/09/insider/09insider-penn-03-babe/09insider-penn-03-babe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0,