ated buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of Detroit’s public schools closed Monday in the face of a “sickout” by teachers who protested what they called unsafe, crumbling, vermin-infested and inadequately staffed buildings, and the failure of state lawmakers to agree on a plan to rescue a system teetering on the edge of insolvency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sickout’ by Detroit Teachers Closes Most Public Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frustrated Detroit Teachers Stage &#8216;Sickout&#8217; That Closes Most Public Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T19:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70383b3c-b42e-521d-b211-a858bc9cfe4c', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70383b3c-b42e-521d-b211-a858bc9cfe4c'}, {'abstract': 'Adele’s “25” is still the top-selling album of the week, adding an additional 164,000 copies sold to its tally for a seventh week at No. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/11/adele-cedes-billboards-singles-chart-to-justin-bieber-after-10-weeks/',