ly interminable and intolerable.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 913}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1347, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12BOOKRAWLENCE/12BOOKRAWLENCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘City of Thorns,’ Ben Rawlence Tells a Refugee Camp’s Story', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Refugee Limbo: Desperation Amid the Dust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rawlence, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dadaab (Kenya)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "City of Thorns: Nine Lives in the World's Largest Refugee Camp (Book)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T21:54:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Senior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Senior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5b76e31-f400-5db3-93f5-c8250ac5a0b7', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5b76e31-f400-5db3-93f5-c8250ac5a0b7'}, {'abstract': 'Kirsten Dunst, Cate Blanchett and Kate Winslet all chose dangling accessories that were (or just looked) over a century old.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/11/t-magazine/fashion/vintage-earrings-golden-globes.html', 'snippet': 'Kirsten Dunst, Cate Blanchett and Kate Winslet all chose dangling accessories that were (or just looked) over a century old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several actresses chose to wear dangling earrings to last night’s Golden Globes, but the standout trend were the vintage (and vintage-inspired) pieces that brought Old Hollywood — in some cases, really old Hollywood — back to the red carpet. Kirsten Dunst chose Fred Leighton diamond pendant earrings that date from the 19th century, while Cate Blanchett matched her Givenchy fringe gown with a pair of Tiffany & Co. platinum diamond and pearl earrings from 1915. And Kate Winslet’s Neil Lane diamond earrings are a contemporary design heavily influenced by the Art Deco period.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None