94ed-59f9-5855-979d-c2c28440530f', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/804994ed-59f9-5855-979d-c2c28440530f'}, {'abstract': 'He helped transform the idea of the music video from a mere promotion to an art form in its own right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/arts/music/david-bowie-master-of-the-music-video.html', 'snippet': 'He helped transform the idea of the music video from a mere promotion to an art form in its own right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among many other things, David Bowie was a pioneer and maestro of the music video: From the start of his career, he understood the possibilities of a fledgling format, the ways in which music and image could conspire to tell a richer, more complicated story. Whether in a narrative or purely expressionist mode, he brought acute visual poetry to the screen, helping to transform the music video from an afterthought — a flat promotional tool — into its own challenging (and ever-changing) artistic medium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Bowie, Master of the Music Video', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowie, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rock, Mick (1948- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strange, Steve (1959-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-11T22:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c70ecf35-a405-59be-a52b-8a746c9291e9', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c70ecf35-a405-59be-a52b-8a746c9291e9'}, {'abstract': 'In Thomas Middleton and William Rowley’s 1622 Jacobean tragedy, at the Lucille Lortel, a young noblewoman needs a hit man.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/theater/review-the-changeling-where-murder-is-the-natural-solution.html', 'snippet': 'In Thomas Middleton and William Rowley’s 1622 Jacobean tragedy, at the Lucille Lortel, a young noblewoman needs a hit man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sensation slides into silliness in “The Changeling,” a 1622 tragedy — with generous dollops of comedy — by Thomas Middleton and William Rowley. The convoluted story grows more lurid and strained as the play hurtles toward its predictably bloody conclusion, but with a fine cast bringing sufficient heat to the panting plotlines, the Red Bull Theater and its artistic director, Jesse Berger, once again win admiration for presenting a rarely seen drama from the Jacobean era with highly caffeinated verve. (Their previous productions include Middleton’s “Women Beware Women” and “The Revenger’s Tragedy.”)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12CHANGELING1/12CHANGELING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12CHANGELING1/12CHANGELING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/12CHANGELING1/12CHANGELING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/arts/1