ool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 24 million children living in 22 countries affected by conflict are not in school, the United Nations said Monday. A report released by Unicef, the United Nations Children’s Fund, said that of roughly 109 million children of primary and secondary school age in these countries, almost one in four are not getting an education. The highest proportion was in South Sudan, where more than half the school-age children are not in school, followed by Niger, at 47 percent; Sudan, 41 percent; and Afghanistan, 40 percent. The impact of war and upheaval on childhood education is regarded as a long-term crisis by Unicef, which has frequently warned of the effects of trauma and illiteracy as children reach adulthood. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conflicts Keep 24 Million Children Out of School, Unicef Report Finds', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'United Nations; Conflicts Keep 24 Million Children Out of School, Unicef Report Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United Nations Children's Fund", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T02:38:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qua