/2016/01/12/sports/ncaafootball/alabama-crimson-tide-wins-national-championship.html', 'snippet': 'The Heisman Trophy winner Derrick Henry ran for 158 yards and three touchdowns, leading No. 2 Alabama past No. 1 Clemson for the College Football Playoff championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLENDALE, Ariz. — Nick Saban won his fourth national title in seven seasons on Monday night, and his fifth over all, with an Alabama team headlined by Derrick Henry, the second Tide player, after Mark Ingram Jr., to win the Heisman Trophy. The Heismans bookending Saban’s first and fourth titles since 2009 buttress the belief outside Tuscaloosa, Ala., that Saban is the beneficiary of bountiful talent. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama Wins Fourth National Championship in Seven Years', 'kicker': 'Alabama 45, Clemson 40', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'JUST CALL IT THE TIDAL GAME ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Football Playoff National Championship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clemson University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T05:19:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a08229f-d96a-53a5-bfc4-6d1c0977e034', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a08229f-d96a-53a5-bfc4-6d1c0977e034'}, {'abstract': 'At the Iowa Black and Brown Forum, a nationally televised event focused on minority issues, Mrs. Clinton broke with the Obama administration in arguing that raids are not an appropriate method of enforcing immigration laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/12/hillary-clinton-promises-not-to-be-deporter-in-chief/', 'snippet': 'At the Iowa Black and Brown Forum, a nationally televised event focused on minority issues, Mrs. Clinton broke with the Obama administration in arguing that raids are not an appropriate method of enforcing immigration laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under pressure to consolidate her support among Latinos as Senator Bernie Sanders of Vermont gains ground on her in Iowa, Hillary Clinton broke with the Obama administration on a key immigration provision on Monday night and promised not to be the “deporter in chief” if elected president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/us/politics/12firstdraft-clinton/12firstdraft-clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/12/us/politics/12firstdraft-clinton/12firstdraft-clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/us/politics/12firstdraft-clinton/12firstdraft-clinton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/us/politics/12firstdraft-clinton/12firstdraft-clinton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/us/politics/12firstdraft-clint