, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/185d06a0-d655-53d1-b090-5c5a9588c857', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/185d06a0-d655-53d1-b090-5c5a9588c857'}, {'abstract': 'New ads from Donald Trump and Ted Cruz are part of a tradition that began with a race-baiting 1988 spot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/opinion/campaign-stops/ads-from-donald-trump-and-ted-cruz-play-to-racist-fears.html', 'snippet': 'New ads from Donald Trump and Ted Cruz are part of a tradition that began with a race-baiting 1988 spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Donald J. Trump’s first television ad of the 2016 campaign, released last week, a photo of Hillary Clinton and President Obama flashes across the screen, followed by stark black-and-white images of the San Bernardino, Calif., attackers, Syed Rizwan Farook and Tashfeen Malik.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/10/opinion/emma-roller-headshot/emma-rollins-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i