{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/92120375-bc93-58a4-ab43-2d188b1f7978', 'word_count': 1401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92120375-bc93-58a4-ab43-2d188b1f7978'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas Republican lacks the Christian virtues many evangelical voters may expect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/opinion/the-brutalism-of-ted-cruz.html', 'snippet': 'The Texas Republican lacks the Christian virtues many evangelical voters may expect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1997, Michael Wayne Haley was arrested after stealing a calculator from Walmart. This was a crime that merited a maximum two-year prison term. But prosecutors incorrectly applied a habitual offender law. Neither the judge nor the defense lawyer caught the error and Haley was sentenced to 16 years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/opinion/12brooksWeb/12brooksWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag