se, on view at MoMA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The high-powered art dealer Larry Gagosian says he bought it. The royal family of Qatar says it bought the sculpture, too. And now they are facing off in court over who owns Picasso’s important plaster bust of his muse (and mistress) Marie-Thérèse Walter, a star of the Museum of Modern Art’s popular “Picasso Sculpture” show.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/09/11/arts/0911PICASSOJP5/0911PICASSOJP5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Picasso Bust at Center of Custody Battle Between Gagosian and Qatar Royal Family', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Picasso Bust Sells for Millions, but Did It Go to Two Buyers?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gagosian, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Widmaier-Picasso, Maya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T14:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cb85031-b8f8-5bed-bcd3-732011417e8d', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cb85031-b8f8-5bed-bcd3-732011417e8d'}, {'abstract': 'Pamela Tatge, the director of the Center for the Arts at Wesleyan University, is to take over beginning April 18.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/a-new-director-for-jacobs-pillow-dance-festival/', 'snippet': 'Pamela Tatge, the director of the Center for the Arts at Wesleyan University, is to take over beginning April 18.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival, nestled in the Berkshire Hills of western Massachusetts, has a new leader: Pamela Tatge, who is to take over as executive director beginning April 18. Previously, the position of executive and artistic director was held by Ella Baff. Ms. Tatge is the director of the Center for the Arts at Wesleyan University in Middletown, Conn., where, for the past 16 years, she has organized programming in dance, music, theater and the visual arts. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Director for Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jacobu2019s Pillow Festival Has a New Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Jacob's Pillow Dance Festival", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baff, Ella', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T14:52:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9661facb-915c-5951-ba64-07957d26e7b8', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9661facb-915c-5951-ba64-07957d26e7b8'}, {'abstract': 'With more than a billion dollars up for grabs in the Powerball jackpot this week, people flocked to Georgia, a state that actually participates in the lottery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/us/no-powerball-at-home-alabamians-cross-state-lines-in-search-of-a-golden-ticket.html', 'snippet': 'With more than a billion dollars up for grabs in the Powerball jackpot this week, people flocked to Georgia, a state that actually participates in the lottery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TALLAPOOSA, Ga. — There was not much in the world that was more important to many Alabamians in recent days than the national football champio