, 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework-slide-LKMK/12tmag-homework-slide-LKMK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework-slide-LKMK/12tmag-homework-slide-LKMK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marin Montagut’s Atelier in Normandy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T16:57:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1b70ca9a-3209-5d65-a119-b8f6f1757a78', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1b70ca9a-3209-5d65-a119-b8f6f1757a78'}, {'abstract': 'Marin Montagut, the illustrator of Bonjour City Map-Guides, takes T in and around his bucolic atelier in Normandy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/t-magazine/art/marin-montagut-normandy-tour.html', 'snippet': 'Marin Montagut, the illustrator of Bonjour City Map-Guides, takes T in and around his bucolic atelier in Normandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rarely without his navy and white marinière — or his robin’s-egg blue Vespa — the French illustrator-filmmaker-multimedia artist Marin Montagut has emerged as a darling of sorts in the Parisian cultural scene. Known first for his documentaries for the fashion paragon Inès de la Fressange, he’s earning attention today for weaving watercolors of his favorite fashionable addresses in Paris, London and New York into Bonjour City Map-Guides, a series of pocket-sized folding maps. And yet, the globetrotter produces much of his work about an hour from the City of Light in his creative home-away-from-home in Saint-Luc, Normandy — prepossessing as much for its design as for its bucolic environs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12tmag-homework1/12tmag-homework1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A French Watercolorist’s Countryside Escape', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Normandy (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T16:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsey Tramuta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tramuta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cb4ec18-6d04-53a0-ac3c-ee7738be3fa8', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cb4ec18-6d04-53a0-ac3c-ee7738be3fa8'}, {'abstract': 'When we needed a cover illustration for our annual 52 Places to Go issue, we turned to Rafael Lopez, a celebrated illustrator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/travel/52-places-to-go-art-rafael-lopez.html', 'snippet': 'When we needed a cover illustration for our annual 52 Places to Go issue, we turned to Rafael Lopez, a celebrated illustrator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we needed a cover illustration for our annual 52 Places to Go issue, we turned to Rafael Lopez, a celebrated illustrator. After all, our No. 1 pick this year is Mexico City, where Mr. Lopez is from and lives part-time. He’s also an extraordinary artist who’s created dynamic and colorful posters, murals and postage stamps. We were delighted with the results. To learn more, we asked Mr. Lopez a few questions about his inspiration, his life and his work. He sent his answers, which are below, edited for length and clarity, by email from San Miguel de Allende.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/11/travel/11PTG-illo/11PTG-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'su