 war in Syria?” a writer asks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/opinion/taking-action-in-syria.html', 'snippet': '“How much more suffering must we witness before world leaders take real action to end the war in Syria?” a writer asks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Action in Syria', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Action in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T18:21:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/00c08ac7-7dcc-5658-8e9e-0428d5f87b54', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00c08ac7-7dcc-5658-8e9e-0428d5f87b54'}, {'abstract': 'Dana Sherwood’s latest work involves leaving precisely chosen feasts out for Brazilian ocelots and Danish deer — and filming the results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/t-magazine/art/dana-sherwood-animal-art.html', 'snippet': 'Dana Sherwood’s latest work involves leaving precisely chosen feasts out for Brazilian ocelots and Danish deer — and filming the results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the artist Dana Sherwood’s apartment on the Upper West Side, her dog, Hera, answers the door, tail wagging. A lifelong equestrian who now competes in dressage, Sherwood is used to collaborating with animals — and connects with them on a fundamental level. “Dressage is all about understanding a horse through the feel of your body; it’s like inventing another language,” says Sherwood. “What I’m interested in lately is the difference between what we assume animals think and how they actually behave.” In her new solo show, “Crossing the Wild Line,” at Denny Gallery on the Lower East Side, Sherwood takes nature’s pulse by way of an unlikely combination of media: pastry, video and drawing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/12/t-magazine/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5/12mag-sherwood-slide-N3F5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Made by Tempting Animals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dressage (Equestrian Sport)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denny Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T18:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kat Herriman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herriman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d15e34c1-2925-5087-bdd1-334557498e29', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d15e34c1-2925-5087-bdd1-334557498e29'}, {'abstract': 'In his final State of the Union message, the president urged Americans to confront the challenges of the future by rejecting fear and embracing change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/us/politics/obama-state-of-the-union.html', 'snippet': 'In his final State of the Union message, the president urged Americans to confront the challenges of the future by rejecting fear and embracing change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Tuesday set forth an ambitious vision for America’s future but conceded his own failure to heal the political divisions holding back progress, calling it a lasting disappointment of his tenure.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headl