Mad Max” and “Martian” also make the Directors Guild list, but “Carol” is shut out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alejandro G. Iñárritu (“The Revenant”), Tom McCarthy (“Spotlight”), and Adam McKay (“The Big Short”) were among the feature film nominees chosen as the year’s best by the 15,000-member Directors Guild of America, whose final winners — to be announced at a ceremony on Feb. 6 — often hew closely to pictures that win an Academy Award. Since 2000, all but three Directors Guild winners (“Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon,” “Brokeback Mountain” and “Gravity”) went on to claim the best picture Oscar.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13artsbeat-inarritu/13artsbeat-inarritu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13artsbeat-inarritu/13artsbeat-inarritu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13artsbeat-inarritu/13artsbeat-inarritu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13artsbeat-inarritu/13artsbeat-inarritu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13artsbeat-inarritu/13artsbeat-inarritu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13artsbeat-inarritu/13artsbeat-inarritu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7