ive of the Edinburgh Festival Fringe Society.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/12/shona-mccarthy-new-head-of-edinburgh-fringe/', 'snippet': 'Shona McCarthy succeeds Kath Mainland as chief executive of the Edinburgh Festival Fringe Society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shona McCarthy, an arts leader and consultant, has been appointed chief executive of the Edinburgh Festival Fringe Society, the organization that oversees the annual Edinburgh Festival Fringe, the largest multi-arts festival in the world. Ms. McCarthy, who will take over in early March, assumes a post currently occupied by Kath Mainland, who has run the Society for seven years. Ms. Mainland announced in November that she was stepping down to become executive director of the Melbourne Festival.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shona McCarthy New Head of Edinburgh Fringe', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Top Executive for Edinburgh Fringe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Edinburgh Festival Fringe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mainland, Kath M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Shona', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T18:49:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0110790b-54bf-5f20-b40b-d494c4e8c828', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0110790b-54bf-5f20-b40b-d494c4e8c828'}, {'abstract': 'Anaheim, which took over regional supremacy las