Group has announced that Mr. Morris is to choreograph a full-length dance narrative, “Layla and Majnun,” based on a love story that has its origins in seventh-century Persia. It is to have its premiere in Berkeley, Calif., in September. The music, live as always with Mr. Morris, will involve Azerbaijani mugham, a complex combination of music and poetry, to be performed on both traditional and Western instruments by the Silk Road Ensemble with the father and daughter Azerbaijani vocalists Alim Qasimov and Fargana Qasimova. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1244, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/12MORRIS/12MORRIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width':