ew York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: Cruz’s Canadian Birth Could Matter in Iowa', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Policy Polling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T21:35:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c002f93-3d75-5a07-84b4-b76239810cc7', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c002f93-3d75-5a07-84b4-b76239810cc7'}, {'abstract': 'A corrupt onetime sheriff is brought back to life by a Frankenstein-style duo after he dies in this new series, raising the question of whether he will make amends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/arts/television/tv-review-second-chance-fox.html', 'snippet': 'A corrupt onetime sheriff is brought back to life by a Frankenstein-style duo after he dies in this new series, raising the question of whether he will make amends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Frankenstein genre and the buddy cop genre may seem a long way from each other, but “Second Chance,” which begins on Wednesday night on Fox, is born of both. And it’s aptly titled. The premiere has so much going on and is so absurd that you may be tempted not to return, but give it another try. Rewards await.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13SECOND-2/13SECOND-1452622977172-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In Fox’s ‘Second Chance,’ a Life Resurrected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Muscled Frankenstein at a Moral Crossroads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeKay, Tim (1963- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'va