'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-12T23:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Upshot Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Upshot Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/723b4cfb-1f5e-5b61-9e4b-737bf4c0ca45', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/723b4cfb-1f5e-5b61-9e4b-737bf4c0ca45'}, {'abstract': 'In returning to the presidential campaign trail for the first time since 2008, Chelsea Clinton focused on motherhood and attacked Senator Bernie Sanders over his health care and education proposals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/12/chelsea-clinton-again-her-mothers-surrogate-takes-up-the-fight-against-bernie-sanders/', 'snippet': 'In returning to the presidential campaign trail for the first time since 2008, Chelsea Clinton focused on motherhood and attacked Senator Bernie Sanders over his health care and education proposals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Again playing the part of candidate surrogate — though with a message now tailored to young parents like herself — Chelsea Clinton spoke of motherhood Tuesday on the New Hampshire trail while also amplifying her mother’s increasing attacks on Senator Bernie Sanders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chelsea Clinton, Again Her Mother’s Surrogate, Takes Up the Fight Against Bernie Sanders', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':