w.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/us/maryland-trial-in-freddie-gray-death-complicated-by-appeals-schedule.html', 'snippet': 'The trial of Officer Caesar R. Goodson Jr. has another scheduling obstacle, an appeals court set March 4 for oral arguments for another officer who is trying to avoid testifying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trial of Officer Caesar R. Goodson Jr. of the Baltimore police, charged with murder in the death of Freddie Gray, encountered another scheduling obstacle Tuesday when an appeals court set March 4 for oral arguments in the appeal of another officer who is trying to avoid testifying. On Monday, the Court of Special Appeals said the Goodson trial may not go forward until it hears the appeal of the other officer, William G. Porter, whose own trial on manslaughter charges ended in a deadlocked jury last month. The state considers Officer Porter its star witness in the Goodson case, but he is trying to assert his Fifth Amendment right not to incriminate himself. The legal wrangling could alter the schedules of four other officers facing charges in the death of Mr. Gray, a 25-year-old black man who sustained a fatal spinal cord injury in police custody in April. The death set off riots in Baltimore. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maryland: Trial in Freddie Gray Death Complicated by Appeals Schedule', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Mid-Atlantic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maryland: Trial in Freddie Gray Death Is Complicated by Appeals Schedule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodson, Caesar R Jr (1969- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Freddie (1989-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porter, William G (1989- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-13T00:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/503ed5ab-966f-53a6-9d3d-d52e15d99bba', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/503ed5ab-966f-53a6-9d3d-d52e15d99bba'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Margulies, a versatile character actor, performed in scores of supporting stage, film and television roles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/movies/david-margulies-mayor-in-ghostbusters-dies-at-78.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Margulies, a versatile character actor, performed in scores of supporting stage, film and television roles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Margulies, a versatile character actor who performed in scores of supporting stage, film and television roles but was most conspicuous as the common-sense mayor in “Ghostbusters” and as Tony Soprano’s sleazy lawyer, died on Monday at his home in Manhattan. He was 78.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13margulies-obit/13margulies-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13margulies-obit/13margulies-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/arts/13margulies-obit/13margulies-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 64