', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a20154e-d14d-5fff-98a0-f88b52459186', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a20154e-d14d-5fff-98a0-f88b52459186'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Changes are made to Italy’s forces in Albania in 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/1941-changes-to-the-italian-army/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Changes are made to Italy’s forces in Albania in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Two months after taking command of the Italian forces in Albania, Gen. Ubaldo Soddu has been relieved of active duty at his own request, it was announced here today [Jan. 13]. Ill health, necessitating a long rest and care, was given as the reason for his retirement. All that the military command vouchsafed today concerning the fighting in Albania was that there had been normal activity of patrols and artillery and that Italian planes had machine-gunned and shelled enemy troops and columns of trucks on the march. No word has as yet reached the Italian people officially to confirm the claims of further Greek successes, which foreign broadcasts have reported.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 14, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/blogs/13iht-oldjan13-italy/13iht-oldjan13-italy-jumbo.png', 'height': 470, 'width': 470, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/blogs/13iht-oldjan13-italy/13iht-oldjan13-italy-superJumbo.png', 'height': 470, 'width': 470, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':