ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfd7d34b-2b3d-5d88-b42d-fa1617d32385', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfd7d34b-2b3d-5d88-b42d-fa1617d32385'}, {'abstract': 'Jami Morse Heidegger brings decades of experience — and some of the highest-quality ingredients in the industry — to Retrouvé.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/13/t-magazine/fashion/retrouve-beauty-jami-morse-heidegger.html', 'snippet': 'Jami Morse Heidegger brings decades of experience — and some of the highest-quality ingredients in the industry — to Retrouvé.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When third-generation Kiehl’s heir Jami Morse Heidegger sold the family business to L’Oreal in 2000, she thought she was walking away from beauty for good. But the luxury of having time away ironically sucked her back in. “I had been traveling so much for work and had three young children at home at the time,” she recalls. “I wanted to take care of myself, but there wasn’t anything on the market that addressed all of my concerns. I wanted something that was anti-aging but with top-quality oils to address the dryness I felt living in California desert.” So, she enlisted her longtime chemist from Kiehl’s to help formulate several products to rejuvenate her own skin. The requirement: Create mixtures with the highest possible concentration of effective ingredients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/t-magazine/13tmag-retrouve1/13tmag-retrouve1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/13/t-magazine/13tmag-retrouve1/13tmag-retrouve1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/13/t-magazine/13tmag-retrouve1/13tmag-retrouve1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop