 LISA SANDERS, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SANDERS', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/98fea449-91c2-5b48-ab5e-02f6b334767c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/98fea449-91c2-5b48-ab5e-02f6b334767c'}, {'abstract': 'Paying tribute to my father and reflecting on a changing country during a four-day trek in the Himalayan foothills.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/travel/nepal-himalayas.html', 'snippet': 'Paying tribute to my father and reflecting on a changing country during a four-day trek in the Himalayan foothills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around the third hour on the third day of trekking uphill on a rocky trail in the rain, I felt a profound appreciation for the generous tolerance of my family. We had come to the foothills of the Himalayas by way of various story lines of my life, including President Kennedy’s 1961 inaugural address and my father’s death in 2014. These events led us to Nepal, and to a walk through the clouds.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/travel/17NEPAL1/17NEPAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Return to Nepal, in Memoriam', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Return to the Himalayas, in Memoriam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Himalayas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mountaineering', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T12:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anker Heegaard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anker', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heegaard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef6fca9b-9cd4-549b-870b-9daf4056c5a5', 'word_count': 2030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef6fca9b-9cd4-549b-870b-9daf4056c5a5'}, {'abstract': 'The apparent impartiality of photographs can conceal as much as it reveals — especially when the subject is violence or prejudice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/magazine/against-neutrality.html', 'snippet': 'The apparent impartiality of photographs can conceal as much as it reveals — especially when the subject is violence or prejudice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photograph and the words arrive simultaneously. They guarantee each other. You believe the words more because the photograph verifies them, and trust the photograph because you trust the words. Additionally, each puts further pressure on the interpretation: A war photograph can, for example, make a grim situation palatable, just as a story about a scandal can make the politician depicted look pathetic. But images, unlike words, are often presumed to be unbiased. The facticity of a photograph can conceal the craftiness of its content and selection.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17onphotography1/17mag-17onphotographynew-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17onphotography1/17mag-17onphotographynew-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17onphotography1/17mag-17onphotographynew-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17onphotography1/17mag-17onphotographynew-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17onphotography1/17mag-17onphotographyn