, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d73fc20a-9a86-5a5c-851a-10486276fb0f', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d73fc20a-9a86-5a5c-851a-10486276fb0f'}, {'abstract': 'GoPro surprised Wall Street with its earnings warning on Wednesday. Intel is on deck to report quarterly results on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/14/daily-report-tech-earnings-season-begins-with-a-warning/', 'snippet': 'GoPro surprised Wall Street with its earnings warning on Wednesday. Intel is on deck to report quarterly results on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tech earnings season got off to a rocky start on Wednesday with the surprise warning from GoPro, the maker of action cameras, that its quarterly results would be lower than expected by Wall Street analysts and that it had cut about 7 percent of its work force. A top executive also departed the company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Tech Earnings Season Begins With a Warning', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GoPro', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T14:34:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pui-Wing Tam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pui-wing', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49a4d7b7-b8ac-5d1c-b840-5d8be4a21a1b', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49a4d7b7-b8ac-5d1c-b840-5d8be4a21a1b'}, {'abstract': 'The bandwagon effect helps Donald Trump now but leaves him vulnerable if he loses a primary — and could make his supporters complacent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/upshot/everybody-loves-a-winner-so-what-happens-if-trump-loses.html', 'snippet': 'The bandwagon effect helps Donald Trump now but leaves him vulnerable if he loses a primary — and could make his supporters complacent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump misses no opportunity to remind us that he’s ahead in the polls for the Republican presidential nomination. During a rally in Claremont, N.H., last week, he said, “When people say, ‘Why do you always talk about the polls?’ I say, ‘Because I’m winning!’ Believe me, if I’m not winning, I don’t talk about them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1270, 'width': 1884, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/15UP-Bandwagon/15UP-Bandwagon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Everybody Loves a Winner. So What Happens if Trump Loses?', 'kicker': 'Political Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T14:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brendan Nyhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brendan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nyhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bffd3bad-5379-56bc-aa60-aa5053890fc3', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bffd3bad-5379-56bc-aa60-aa5053890fc3'}, {'abstract': 'Access to Amazon Instant Videos can be gained in many ways, including via game consoles and devices that connect to your TV set.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/technology/personaltech/amazon-prime-video-home-and-away.html', 'snippet': 'Access to Amazon Instant Videos can be gained in many ways, including via game consoles and devices that connect to your TV set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Is there a way to watch Amazon’s Instant Video on my television instead of my tablet? If I’m subscribed to Amazon Prime in the United States, can I watch the Prime Instant Video outside the country, like when I’m traveling overseas for work?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Prime Video, Home and Away', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets and Media Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple TV', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T14:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/dce5b3b6-8581-5fcd-a8c6-1e5a8899f5a0', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dce5b3b6-8581-5fcd-a8c6-1e5a8899f5a0'}, {'abstract': 'Of all this show’s perversions, the most surprising has been its penchant for happy endings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/14/arts/television/american-horror-story-hotel-finale.html', 'snippet': 'Of all this show’s perversions, the most surprising has been its penchant for happy endings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And so began the era of Iris and Liz Taylor. Our heroines have taken over the Cortez (though, didn’t The Countess leave it to Ramona at the end of the last episode?) and, flush with cash after liquidating their former employer’s art collection, do a little redecorating. There’s 400 thread-count Egyptian cotton! Complimentary champagne! Japanese toilets!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/arts/ahs/ahs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Horror Story’ Season 5 Finale: The Real Lady', 'kicker': 'American Horror Story', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Horror Story (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T14:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. A. Hanks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Hanks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/60096545-7a5c-598f-9907-2d761bb86a5d', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60096545-7a5c-598f-9907-2d761bb86a5d'}, {'abstract': 'The new film “Quo Vado?” is bigger than “Star Wars,” because it speaks to the country’s nostalgia for safe, secure careers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/opinion/quo-vado-italy-bigger-than-star-wars.html', 'snippet': 'The new film “Quo Vado?” is bigger than “Star Wars,” because it speaks to the country’s nostalgia for safe, secure careers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — A BALDING government clerk in his late 30s has one true love: “il posto fisso,” a job for life. He doesn’t want to compete in the labor market; he has no urge to move on. He doesn’t even want to earn more. Give him a desk, a chair and a 9-to-5 job in the “pubblica amministrazione,” and he’s happy. Clocking in late, chatting with colleagues, accepting small bribes from taxpayers (most favored: quail), a regular salary — that’s life!', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/opinion/15severgniniWeb/15severgniniWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/opinion/15severgniniWeb/15severgniniWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/opinion/15severgniniWeb/15severgniniWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/opinion/15severgniniWeb/15severgniniWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1134, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/opinion/15severgniniWeb/15severgniniWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thu