'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T15:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'subsection_name': 'Insider Events', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francesca Donner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francesca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/252336a0-878d-580f-adb1-7325c773de5f', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/252336a0-878d-580f-adb1-7325c773de5f'}, {'abstract': 'The transfer of 10 lower-level Yemeni detainees, which took place on Wednesday, was the largest single resettlement of prisoners in the yearslong effort to close the prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/us/politics/guantanamo-bay-prison-transfer.html', 'snippet': 'The transfer of 10 lower-level Yemeni detainees, which took place on Wednesday, was the largest single resettlement of prisoners in the yearslong effort to close the prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Pentagon on Thursday announced that it had transferred 10 lower-level Yemeni detainees from the Guantánamo Bay prison to Oman. The departure of the unusually large group of prisoners — each of whom spent about 14 years in custody — reduced the prison population to 93, the first time it has been in double digits since the Bush administration began bringing Afghanistan war prisoners to the naval base in January 2002.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/us/15gitmo-web/15gitmo-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guantánamo Population Drops to 93 after 10 Prisoners Go to Oman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '10 Detainees Sent to Oman From Prison in Cuba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T15:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cha