s&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00a63fea-995e-571c-a5b3-536b0aa1cc4f', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00a63fea-995e-571c-a5b3-536b0aa1cc4f'}, {'abstract': 'The two events will bring plenty of international performers to the city, including Lakou Mizik and Pedro Sá Moraes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/arts/music/globalfest-and-brazilian-explorative-music-come-to-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The two events will bring plenty of international performers to the city, including Lakou Mizik and Pedro Sá Moraes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Association of Performing Arts Presenters convention is the January thaw for music in New York — an audition for the presenters, a potential binge for the rest of us. It brings Globalfest, where 12 international performers are showcased in one building over five hours: among them this year, the New York debut of the Haitian group Lakou Mizik; deep Delta blues from the Music Maker Blues Revue; raspy-voiced and Arab-influenced Mexican cabaret from Astrid Hadad; the Arabic-flamenco-jazz reunion of the oud player Simon Shaheen’s ensemble Zafir; and Fendika, with its own twist on Ethiopian funk. (7 p.m., Sunday, Jan. 17, Webster Hall, globalfest.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Globalfest and Brazilian Explorative Music Come to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; Welcoming the World  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of Performing Arts Presenters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Globalfest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T18:08:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a351ede7-631e-562f-885b-410244cb9692', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a351ede7-631e-562f-885b-410244cb9692'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s implicit criticism of the idea during his State of the Union speech “degrades the presidency,” according to Mr. Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/14/no-comment-necessary-paul-ryan-attacks-obama-for-criticizing-muslim-ban/', 'snippet': 'The president’s implicit criticism of the idea during his State of the Union speech “degrades the presidency,” according to Mr. Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his State of the Union address on Tuesday, President Obama referred to people “promising to restore past glory if we just got some group or idea that was threatening America under control,” an implicit criticism of Donald Trump and his call for a temporary ban on Muslims entering the United States. In an interview with USA Today on Wednesday, Paul Ryan said he also opposed such a ban. But he lambasted the president for bringing the issue up in his speech.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Comment Necessary: Paul Ryan Attacks Obama For Criticizing Muslim Ban', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T18:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cae7c4bc-b0c1-5a60-8f1e-5df2cdd5e7ac', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cae7c4bc-b0c1-5a60-8f1e-5df2cdd5e7ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Museum of Modern Art is bringing his work to light with “All That Jack (Cole),” a two-week film and lecture series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/arts/dance/moma-highlights-work-of-the-choreographer-jack-cole.html', 'snippet': 'The Museum of Modern Art is bringing his work to light with “All That Jack (Cole),” a two-week film and lecture series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Jack Cole has flown under the radar of American dance history. A pioneer of theatrical jazz onstage and on the screen — and a performance coach to Rita Hayworth and Marilyn Monroe — he influenced the likes of Jerome Robbins, Alvin Ailey and Bob Fosse, yet we don’t hear about him much. Beginning on Wednesday, Jan. 20, the Museum of Modern Art is bringing Cole’s work to light with “All That Jack (Cole),” a two-week film and lecture series organized with the dance critic Debra Levine, a Cole scholar.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE6/17GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE6/17GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE6/17GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/arts/17GUIDE6/17GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'su