read looks ready to levitate. Called noni toki, it is matzo-thin, a blistered expanse 14 inches across, the edges uplifted as if in supplication. At Taste of Samarkand, this is achieved by slapping and patting dough around the inverted underbelly of a kazan, a high-sloped Uzbek frying pan akin to a Chinese wok, then baking it over the stove until hard and crisp.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taste of Samarkand Is a Silk Road Oasis in Queens', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Silk Road Oasis in Queens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle Village (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taste of Samarkand (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T18:22:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f2b9ec9-b730-5127-9395-6e7aed7cdd55', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f2b9ec9-b730-5127-9395-6e7aed7cdd55'}, {'abstract': 'Faced with attacks from Ted Cruz and Donald Trump, Mr. Rubio has pushed stiffer policies, while still supporting a change in the law to offer a path to citizenship to illegal immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/us/politics/marco-rubio-immigration.html', 'snippet': 'Faced with attacks from Ted Cruz and Donald Trump, Mr. Rubio has pushed stiffer policies, while still supporting a change in the law to offer a path to citizenship to illegal immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — A Latin singing duo had just finished warming up the crowd for Senator Marco Rubio on Sunday here when he looked out from the stage and asked if he might offer a few words in Spanish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/us/15rubioimmig/15rubioimmig-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pulled in 2 Directions, Marco Rubio Toughens on Immigration, a Little', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving to Right, Rubio Takes Harder Line on Immigration as Rivals Attack ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T18:24:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d163dc-a697-54b0-8e67-b335a4e474d5', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d163dc-a697-54b0-8e67-b335a4e474d5'}, {'abstract': 'Always wrong, never daunted.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/14/strangely-self-confident-permahawks/', 'snippet': 'Always wrong, never daunted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An odd thing about permahawks — people who have been demanding, year after year, that the Fed raise rates now now now. (The same is true, actually, about the overlapping group warning nonstop about fiscal crisis.) They are, by and large, free-market acolytes who insist that markets know best; yet they also insist that we ignore financial markets that have been telling us that inflation is quiescent and the U.S. government is solvent. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strangely Self-Confident Permahawks', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T18:43:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f2d0fa3-5065-5cdc-a2ee-bb2165e876eb', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f2d0fa3-5065-5cdc-a2ee-bb2165e876eb'}, {'abstract': 'Detainees in pretrial detention centers will be forbidden to use slang known as “fenya,” but there was no immediate indication of how the authorities intended to enforce the rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/world/europe/russia-bans-foul-language-in-some-prisons-no-word-on-enforcement.html', 'snippet': 'Detainees in pretrial detention centers will be forbidden to use slang known as “fenya,” but there was no immediate indication of how the authorities intended to enforce the rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia’s prison system, the successor to the notoriously harsh gulag, has issued an edict that would have shocked even the victims of Stalin’s purges: From now on, officials say, some prisoners will be forbidden to swear.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/world/15GULAG1/15GULAG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/world/15