reasingly comfortable with the idea of the billionaire businessman being their presidential nominee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/us/politics/14firstdraft-trump5/14firstdraft-trump5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump’s Popularity Hits New Heights in Latest National Poll', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T22:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e50ae11b-5d21-5353-995a-cdca761d5c9d', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e50ae11b-5d21-5353-995a-cdca761d5c9d'}, {'abstract': 'Lucy and Jorge Orta’s “Antarctica World Passport Delivery Bureau,” which follows the pair’s expedition to the South Pole, offers visitors a (symbolic) universal citizenship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/14/t-magazine/art/lucy-jorge-orta-antarctica-art.html', 'snippet': 'Lucy and Jorge Orta’s “Antarctica World Passport Delivery Bureau,” which follows the pair’s expedition to the South Pole, offers visitors a (symbolic) universal citizenship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than five decades, the South Pole has remained free of any one nation’s rule; rather, under the Antarctic Treaty, which includes signatures from 53 nations, Antarctic territory is a demilitarized, nuclear-free, neutral zone. Or is it? “Antarctic Flag,” a work by the artists Lucy and Jorge Orta that was first unveiled during their 2007 expedition to Antarctica, stands as a symbolic bricolage of the territory’s supporting nations and their shared values — but also raises the question of whether peaceful coexistence there is sustainable. The partners and artistic duo, also referred to as Studio Orta, based in France and internationally recognized for their socially mindful practice, are all too aware of potential danger in the region. Come 2048, a 1991 agreement protecting what lurks beneath the ice there — oil, coal and kimberlite (thus, maybe, diamonds) — will be open for review, and it’s unclear to what lengths some nations might compete to have sole ownership.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/t-magazine/14tmag-ortas/14tmag-ortas-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Antarctic Art Project, Complete With Fake Passports', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Passports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lombard, Jane, Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T22:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc3b5c9f-3cc5-5a69-8232-77b195563c0d', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc3b5c9f-3cc5-5a69-8232-77b195563c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Puccini’s Mimì and Turandot each have received a multilayered interpretation as Franco Zeffirelli’s productions of these works have returned to the Metropolitan Opera with new casts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/arts/music/review-in-turandot-and-la-boheme-a-new-depth-of-emotion.html', 'snippet': 'Puccini’s Mimì and Turandot each have received a multilayered interpretation as Franco Zeffirelli’s productions of these works have returned to the Metropolitan Opera with new casts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The frail seamstress Mimì and the fierce princess Turandot are two opposite poles of Puccinian womanhood, and both are characters that can seem one-dimensional. But each have received a multilayered interpretation as Franco Zeffirelli’s lavish productions of “T