 trees, seascapes and roadsides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lovers, friends, the smell of the sea, the warmth of the sun on the nape of your neck: Zane Zhou’s photographs, redolent of summertime nostalgia, are a reminder of the powerful, universal intimacy a photographer can create with an unknown viewer. Both aspects of Zhou’s artistic background — he studied painting in Shanghai before moving to New York to pursue fashion photography at the School of Visual Arts in 2013 — are evident in his photo pairs, which juxtapose dreamy, moody images of young men against perfectly composed trees, seascapes and roadsides. “These photographs capture the ephemeral journey of the golden moments of summer and the ways we experience and spend our youth,” Zhou says. (And if you can’t get enough of the young photographer’s work, check out his contributions for T.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreamy, Sexy Photos of Sun-Drenched Summer Afternoons', 'kicker': 'Viewfinder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of Visual Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T22:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carter Love', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Love', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05540136-9198-5974-b9a0-bd085137560f', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05540136-9198-5974-b9a0-bd085137560f'}, {'abstract': 'While not a splashy choice for head coach, McAdoo, the team’s offensive coordinator for the last two years, is not a continuation of the Tom Coughlin era, either.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/sports/football/new-york-giants-hire-ben-mcadoo-a-coughlin-assistant-but-his-own-man.html', 'snippet': 'While not a splashy choice for head coach, McAdoo, the team’s offensive coordinator for the last two years, is not a continuation of the Tom Coughlin era, either.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Giants’ pool of candidates to replace Tom Coughlin was short on pizazz from the beginning. Half the candidates were brainy tacticians in headsets, the football equivalent of Sheldon from “The Big Bang Theory.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/sports/15GIANTS/15GIANTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ben McAdoo Is Replacing, Not Replicating, His Boss With the Giants', 'kicker': 'On Pro Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Replacing, Not Replicating, His Boss With the Giants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAdoo, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Mike (1963- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T22:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3703c9ad-6442-5dfa-9e5e-a4ba759fbe20', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3703c9ad-6442-5dfa-9e5e-a4ba759fbe20'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bay has moderately scaled back his extreme-cinema approach for the story about the attack on the American diplomatic mission in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/movies/review-in-michael-bays-13-hours-the-secret-soldiers-of-benghazi-clarity-isnt-the-objective.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bay has moderately scaled back his extreme-cinema approach for the story about the attack on the American diplomatic mission in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slipped into “13 Hours: The Secret Soldiers of Benghazi,” among the torrential bullets and convulsive mayhem, is a protracted advertisement for a Mercedes-Benz S.U.V. A dramatization of the 2012 attack on the American diplomatic mission in Libya that resulted in the death of four Americans, including Ambassador J. Christopher Stevens, the movie is a pummeling slog — 45 minutes of setup and an eternity of relentless combat. So it’s a relief when the director Michael Bay, amid this bleak fusillade, provides a little zigzagging action-movie-style relief. You can’t help but admire how well the truck holds up with its wheels aflame, like a 21st-century chariot of fire.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15THIRTEENSUB/15THIRTEENSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In Michael Bay’s ‘13 Hours: The Secret Soldiers of Benghazi,’ Clarity Isn’t the Objective', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blowing Stuff Up Without Offering Clarity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '13 Hours: The Secret Soldiers of Benghazi (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krasinski, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-14T22:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a31dd7dc-c189-57c3-9130-f02430cfe609', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a31dd7dc-c189-57c3-9130-f02430cfe609'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Kelly, a longtime stand-up comic, discusses her role on a new FX show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/arts/television/martha-kelly-in-baskets-funny-if-youre-ok-with-that.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Kelly, a longtime stand-up comic, discusses her role on a new FX show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha Kelly isn’t sure why Zach Galifianakis called her “out of the blue” a couple of years ago and asked her to star in his new FX comedy, “Baskets,” which debuts Thursday, Jan. 21. But she’s 