n and loss in her first New York solo exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/arts/design/zineb-sedira-present-tense-at-the-taymour-grahne-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Sedira explores the idea of cultural gain and loss in her first New York solo exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zineb Sedira was born in Paris in 1963 to Algerian immigrants, and has lived in London since the 1980s. Widely exhibited in Europe, she now has a very fine solo of recent work, “Zineb Sedira: Present Tense,” at Taymour Grahne. The idea of cultural gain and loss, and the complications both entail, is a constant theme in her art. A substantial part of this exhibition, organized by Sam Bardaouil and Till Fellrath, is devoted to a multipart project on the subject of lighthouses built under French colonial rule along the North African coastline, and still in use, weather-battered and outdated.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15SEDIRAGALLERY1/15SEDIRAGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15SEDIRAGALLERY1/15SEDIRAGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15SEDIRAGALLERY1/15SEDIRAGALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 515, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15SEDIRAGALLERY1/15SEDIRAGALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 515, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/ar