deologue whose campaign for the 2000 Republican presidential nomination was laced with harsh anti-immigrant rhetoric and other bombastic foretastes of Mr. Trump’s own run this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/opinion/14clinesWEB2/14clinesWEB2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Pat Buchanan Has Come to Be More Than Another Trump ‘Wacko’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2000', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buchanan, Patrick J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T00:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f50be13a-a182-5fe4-9855-70b970eae28e', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f50be13a-a182-5fe4-9855-70b970eae28e'}, {'abstract': 'This solo show, from the Norwegian company Findlay//Sandsmark and part of the Coil festival, conjures apocalyptic imagery before imparting glimpses of hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/arts/dance/review-in-o-death-creation-stirs-amid-the-specter-of-imminent-death.html', 'snippet': 'This solo show, from the Norwegian company Findlay//Sandsmark and part of the Coil festival, conjures apocalyptic imagery before imparting glimpses of hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finding your seat at “o’ death” requires some groping in the dark. Perhaps audience members, fumbling in the faint glow of an usher’s flashlight, are meant to identify with the dancer who eventually comes into view, scrambling on the floor of the nearly lightless room. That would be Marit Sandsmark, the lone performer in this postapocalyptic work by the Norwegian company Findlay//Sandsmark, which had its United States premiere at Ideal Glass Gallery in the East Village on Tuesday. (Ms. Sandsmark choreographed the show; Iver Findlay, her husband and a Wooster Group alum, directed and designed it.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15ODEATH/15ODEATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15ODEATH/15ODEATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15ODEATH/15ODEATH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/15ODEATH/15ODEATH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':