': 'RE: BRAIN SURGERY', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 735}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1631, 'width': 1331, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17thread-cover1/17mag-17thread-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 1.3.16 Issue', 'kicker': 'The Thread', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 1.3.16 Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T11:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ebcdc30-9048-595c-9d5c-f97368447954', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ebcdc30-9048-595c-9d5c-f97368447954'}, {'abstract': 'Desperate attempts to track down an Internet swindler in person.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/magazine/to-catch-a-scammer-in-madrid.html', 'snippet': 'Desperate attempts to track down an Internet swindler in person.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some years ago, while house-sitting outside Rome, I was supposed to be working on a school paper. Instead I spent a lot of time surfing the Internet. One day I found an eBay auction for the kind of semiprofessional camera I coveted. The starting-bid amount was one-fifth the retail price. A few days later, just shortly before the end of the auction, no one had placed a bid. It was my first auction, and my heart started pounding as I prepared to bid my savings on this camera. I typed in the amount, took a deep breath, hit ‘‘bid now’’ and closed my eyes. When I opened them again, nothing had happened.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 844}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1457, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/magazine/17lives/17mag-17lives-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Catch a Scammer in Madrid', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Camera Trap ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bauerlein, Laura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T11:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Anna Mazzobel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzobel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/501ba73b-2155-5d57-b8fa-8c8dbaa43da6', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/501ba73b-2155-5d57-b8fa-8c8dbaa43da6'}, {'abstract': 'The Louis Vuitton exhibition “Volez, Voguez, Voyagez” in Paris is a trip through time — and design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/travel/louis-vuitton-paris.html', 'snippet': 'The Louis Vuitton exhibition “Volez, Voguez, Voyagez” in Paris is a trip through time — and design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, Louis Vuitton is a luxury fashion label, a status symbol that usually hangs from a shoulder or elegantly dangles from a wrist by way of a leather logoed handbag. But rewind to 1835, and the name belonged to a man who left his home at the age of 14 and began walking 280 miles from eastern France to Paris. Upon arriving two years later, he worked as a box maker and packer before starting his own company in 1854, designing ergonomic trunks — or “specialty packing for fashion” as it was advertised — for the wandering elite.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/travel/15intransit-vuitton8/15intransit-vuitton1-1452809157368-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/travel/15intransit-vuitton8/15intransit-vuitton1-1452809157368-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/travel/15intransit-vuitton8/15intransit-vuitton1-1452809157368-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/travel/15intransit-vuitton8/15intransit-vuitton1-1452809157368-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/tr