uff from the vague there to the present here is made possible by container ship. The San Francisco-based artist Martin Machado has an unusual firsthand perspective on this tool of globalization: He spends several months of the year working on container ships, on routes that have taken him through the Suez Canal and to ports in cities as far-flung as Honolulu; New York; Dubai; Karachi, Pakistan; Shanghai; and Singapore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Art on the Open Seas', 'kicker': 'Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Matson Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T12:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Bonnie Tsui', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Bonnie', 'lastname': 'Tsui', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcccc411-02b8-5019-8a14-886d7d531dd7', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcccc411-02b8-5019-8a14-886d7d531dd7'}, {'abstract': 'In this Poetry Pairing, Lily Cao’s poem “Memento” appears with a 2012 article, “It’s Not Me, It’s You,” by Alex Williams.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/poetry-pairing-memento/', 'snippet': 'In this Poetry Pairing, Lily Cao’s poem “Memento” appears with a 2012 article, “It’s Not Me, It’s You,” by Alex Williams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month we again feature the work of a young poet alongside a New York Times article. Here, Lily Cao’s poem “Memento” appears with a 2012 article, “