', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walmart, whose supercenters once transformed the way Americans shop, announced on Friday that it would close a record number of stores in the United States and overseas, as it fights to hold its ground in a retail landscape under siege by the behemoth Amazon.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/business/16walmart-web1/16walmart-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Walmart to Close 269 Stores as Retailers Struggle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walmart to Close 269 Stores Worldwide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T15:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d18916b-2cde-505c-9ee6-f5ff7b5270ce', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d18916b-2cde-505c-9ee6-f5ff7b5270ce'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GHETTOSIDE: A True Story of Murder in America, by Jill Leovy. (Spiegel & Grau, $16.) As a reporter for The Los Angeles Times, Leovy witnessed firsthand the impact of America’s staggering murder rates. Focusing here on one Los Angeles case, she delves into the “plague of black homicides,” including the fraught relationship between the police and civilians and the justice system’s failure to protect black citizens. (African-American men account for nearly 40 percent of the country’s murder victims.)', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T15:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joumana Khatib', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joumana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khatib', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84e8eacf-b1b1-55e9-bc81-aff2fb7584cb', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84e8eacf-b1b1-55e9-bc81-aff2fb7584cb'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY NAME IS LUCY BARTON, by Elizabeth Strout. (Random House, $26.) A writer and her estranged mother attempt to reconnect during a brief visit in a Pulitzer Prize winner’s exquisite novel of careful words and vibrating silences.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent Books of Particular Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T15:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/248cc90a-2bf3-509d-a3b4-5e607b0d114f', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/248cc90a-2bf3-509d-a3b4-5e607b0d114f'}, {'abstract': 'Novels of recent years have brought the issue of refugees to wider attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/books/review/the-facts-of-refugee-life-in-fiction.html', 'snippet': 'Novels of recent years have brought the issue of refugees to wider attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, we review several books about global migration and fractured borders, including Ben Rawlence’s “City of Thorns: Nine Lives in the World’s Largest Refugee Camp.” Rawlence’s book is nonfiction, but acclaimed and popular novels of recent years have brought the issue of refugees to wider attention by placing sympathetic fictional characters in situations much (sometimes very much) like real life.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/0117-BKS-OPENBOOK/0117-BKS-OpenBook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/0117-BKS-OPENBOOK/0117-BKS-OpenBook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/0117-BKS-OPENBOOK/0117-BKS-OpenBook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/0117-BKS-OPENBOOK/0117-BKS-OpenBook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/0117-BKS-OPENBOOK/0117-BKS-OpenBook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'th