he East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Afonso de Albuquerque died 500 years ago, after spending a dozen years terrorizing coastal cities from Yemen to Malaysia. He enriched thousands of men and killed tens of thousands more. Despite never commanding more than a few dozen ships, he built one of the first modern intercontinental empires. And this was just the beginning: The next step, he said, was to sail up the Red Sea, destroy Mecca, Medina and the Prophet Muhammad’s body and liberate the Holy Land. Perhaps, he mused, he could destroy Islam altogether.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Conquerors: How Portugal Forged the First Global Empire,’ by Roger Crowley', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ships and Guns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowley, Roger (1951- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Conquerors: How Portugal Forged the First Global Empire (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T16:35:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c93de92-fa60-5cdb-b08b-4630751f1aef', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c93de92-fa60-5cdb-b08b-4630751f1aef'}, {'abstract': 'A look at unfree labor and its link to environmental damage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/books/review/blood-and-earth-by-kevin-bales.html', 'snippet': 'A look at unfree labor and its link to environmental damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin Bales argues in “Blood and Earth” that ending “modern slavery” could make a big difference in the \xadplanet’s health. “If slavery were a country,” he \xadasserts, “it would have the third-largest CO2 emissions on the planet.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/books/review/17-PURDY/17-PURDY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Blood and Earth,’ by Kevin Bales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backs Bent and Broken ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None