locations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Archie's Waeside (Le Mars, Iowa, Restaurant)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Smitty's Tenderloin Shop (Des Moines, Iowa, Restaurant)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-15T18:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/66f71294-399c-5a94-9371-5ecd27b6610b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/66f71294-399c-5a94-9371-5ecd27b6610b'}, {'abstract': 'The dining landscape in the state has far more to offer than local chains and dishes worthy of state fairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/dining/iowa-caucus-restaurants.html', 'snippet': 'The dining landscape in the state has far more to offer than local chains and dishes worthy of state fairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LE MARS, Iowa — To get to Archie’s Waeside, the James Beard Award-winning steakhouse here that has been run by the same family for three generations, you drive past a branch of the ubiquitous Pizza Ranch chain, cross over a set of railroad tracks and inch down an unlit road toward a low-slung and scantly marked building hard by an R.V. dump.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '\u200bAnother Reason to Caucus in Iowa: The Restaurants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Iowa Food Caucus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', '