rnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In crucial ways, the charismatic conductor Yannick Nézet-Séguin, now in his fourth season as music director of the Philadelphia Orchestra, is excelling in the job. The players seem energized by his leadership. The orchestra sounded terrific on Thursday at Carnegie Hall, in a concert highlighted by an uncommonly sensitive performance of Beethoven’s Fourth Piano Concerto, with the pianist Jan Lisiecki.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/16/arts/16PHILORCHESTRA1/16PHILORCHESTRA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'h