 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4860a86f-0090-51a7-a51f-b3a01f380bdb', 'word_count': 1278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4860a86f-0090-51a7-a51f-b3a01f380bdb'}, {'abstract': 'Jawbone, the start-up that makes wearable devices, became the latest private company to raise money at a lower valuation than before.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/15/jawbone-raises-165-million-at-half-its-last-valuation/', 'snippet': 'Jawbone, the start-up that makes wearable devices, became the latest private company to raise money at a lower valuation than before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jawbone, the once-hot wearable technology start-up, said on Friday that it had raised $165 million in funding at a valuation of $1.5 billion, or roughly half the amount that the company was valued at as recently as 2014, continuing a burgeoning trend of start-ups raising money at lower values than before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jawbone Raises $165 Million at Half Its Last Valuation', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jawbone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-16T01:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Isaac and Katie Benner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79074427-030e-58f4-b4b1-7f2a128edba2', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79074427-030e-58f4-b4b1-7f2a128edba2'}, {'abstract': 'The girl, Natalia Jimenez, fell five stories and was pronounced dead at a Manhattan hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/16/nyregion/girl-15-killed-in-fall-from-rooftop-in-hells-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'The girl, Natalia Jimenez, fell five stories and was pronounced dead at a Manhattan hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 15-year-old girl died on Friday afternoon after she tried to jump from one rooftop to another in Midtown Manhattan and fell five stories, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Girl, 15, Killed in Fall From Rooftop in Hell’s Kitchen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girl, 15, Dies After Fall From Midtown Roof', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remnick, Noah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jimenez, Natalia (d 2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rojas, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-16T01:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas and Noah Remnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Remnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8012b457-ec4e-5a9e-9fdf-9a74e12a120d', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8012b457-ec4e-5a9e-9fdf-9a74e12a120d'}, {'abstract': 'One man connected with the armed takeover of a federal wildlife refuge in Oregon was arrested, and a second was held in the disappearance of a vehicle, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/16/us/oregon-police-arrest-two-tied-to-standoff-at-refuge.html', 'snippet': 'One man connected with the armed takeover of a federal wildlife refuge in Oregon was arrested, and a second was held in the disappearance of a vehicle, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One man connected with the armed takeover of a federal wildlife refuge in rural Oregon was arrested, and a second was held in the disappearance of a vehicle from the refuge, the authorities said Friday. Both arrests were made without incident and far from the refuge itself. Kenneth Medenbach, 62, was arrested Friday at a grocery in Burns on probable cause for unauthorized use of a motor vehicle that the police said was the property of the Malheur National Wildlife Refuge, about 30 miles away. Brian Cavalier, who identified himself as “Fluffy Unicorn,” and as a bodyguard of the militant group’s leader, Ammon Bundy, was arrested earlier in the week in Buckeye, Ariz., on a criminal warrant during the investigation of a suspicious vehicle. He was later released by a judge. A Buckeye police spokesman on Friday said Arizona law prevented disclosure of arrest warrant details. Protesters have occupied the refuge headquarters buildings since Jan. 2. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oregon: Police Arrest Two Tied to Standoff at Refuge', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Northwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oregon: Police Arrest Two Tied to Standoff at Refuge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medenbach, Kenneth (1953- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cavalier, Brian (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malheur National Wildlife Refuge (Oregon)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-16T01:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/77909999-ed16-5bdf-8a0d-3e271836f556', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77909999-ed16-5bdf-8a0d-3e271836f556'}, {'abstract': 'Several people were taken to hospitals after possibly being exposed to lead paint dust in a House office building, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/16/us/workers-sickened-at-house-office-building.html', 'snippet': 'Several people were taken to hospitals after possibly being exposed to lead paint dust in a House office building, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several people were taken to hospitals on Friday after possibly being exposed to lead paint dust in a House office building, the authorities said. Officials said that overnight construction at the Longworth House Office Building may have released the harmful substance in the kitchen area of the cafeteria, according to the House sergeant at arms. The area was not being used for food preparation. Ten cafeteria employees were evaluated, and most were taken to hospitals with “minor injuries,” a Fire Department official said. A favorite of House staff members, the cafeteria will remain closed while tests are conducted. The area around the Capitol was largely empty on Friday, with Congress in recess. ', 