ion of the Day for Saturday, January 16, 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/16/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, January 16, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We may win an Oscar now and then, but an Oscar is not going to fundamentally change how Hollywood does business. I’m not talking about Hollywood stars. I’m talking about executives. We’re not in the room.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-16T06:24:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ec1b68-d744-52a1-be8f-9766e9f90d1b', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ec1b68-d744-52a1-be8f-9766e9f90d1b'}, {'abstract': 'Voters were expected to give Ms. Tsai’s Democratic Progressive Party control of the legislature, giving her broad authority to push her policies in office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/world/asia/taiwan-elections.html', 'snippet': 'Voters were expected to give Ms. Tsai’s Democratic Progressive Party control of the legislature, giving her broad authority to push her policies in office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAIPEI, Taiwan — Tsai Ing-wen was elected Taiwan’s president on Saturday, becoming the first woman to win the office. Voters gave her Democratic Progressive Party, which is skeptical of closer ties with China, control of Taiwan’s legislature for the first time, giving her broad authority to enact her policies in office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image