om/2016/01/17/world/asia/taiwan-china-singer-chou-tzu-yu.html', 'snippet': 'The videotaped apology from the singer, Chou Tzu-yu, with the K-pop band Twice, was addressed in a victory speech by Taiwan’s president-elect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A teenage singer made headlines in China and on her home island of Taiwan this weekend, but not for the winsome K-pop music that she hoped would attract fans. Instead, a glum, shaken apology after a controversy over a flag landed the singer, Chou Tzu-yu, in the maw of tensions between China and Taiwan, just as the island voted to elect an independence-leaning president on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singer’s Apology for Waving Taiwan Flag Stirs Backlash of Its Own', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chou Tzu-yu', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-16T18:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley and Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4be3e02-1294-5185-b767-0be0f457dac1', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4be3e02-1294-5185-b767-0be0f457dac1'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement to 