 he planned to begin a journey to Syria to fight with ISIS, and that the other assisted him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department charged two Virginia men on Saturday with terrorism-related offenses, one day after F.B.I. agents arrested one of them at an airport where officials believe he was planning to begin a journey to Syria to fight with the Islamic State.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia Man Is Accused of Trying to Join ISIS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia Man Is Accused of Trying to Join ISIS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farrokh, Joseph Hassan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elhassan, Mahmoud Amin Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T00:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f15000b0-54f3-5298-9a1c-7bfa9f77f898', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f15000b0-54f3-5298-9a1c-7bfa9f77f898'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Belichick, the New England coach, and his quarterback Tom Brady have now won 22 postseason games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/sports/football/patriots-defeat-chiefs-to-advance-to-afc-championship-game.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Belichick, the New England coach, and his quarterback Tom Brady have now won 22 postseason games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — Two days before the first anniversary of the game that spawned a polemic controversy over deflated footballs, the New England Patriots and their fans gathered for the first playoff game since that contretemps shrouded the franchise for nearly nine months. The atmosphere was festive, with the home side clearly happy to host another mid-January postseason game. But there was also an edge in the air.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/sports/17afc/17afc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/sports/17afc/17afc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/sports/17afc/17afc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/sports/17afc/17afc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1157, 'width': 1840, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/sports/17afc/17afc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/sports/17afc/17afc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw