ef work. In an interview at the offices of the committee, 100 East Forty-second Street, Mr. Troper said that 1,500,000 Jews were absolutely destitute in Poland and many of them were living in walled-up ghettos which they were not allowed to leave even during the day. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-poland/18iht-oldjan18-poland-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1941: Relief Director Tells Plight of Jews in Europe', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T12:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef11ba4f-70cd-5f29-9e75-0ddfd86b5842', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef11ba4f-70cd-5f29-9e75-0ddfd86b5842'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Insurgents surrender to the new military leader after a bloody uprising in Nigeria in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/1966-nigerian-rebels-surrender/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Insurgents surrender to the new military leader after a bloody uprising in Nigeria in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAGOS — The leader of Nigeria’s bloody weekend uprising today [Jan. 17] surrendered his forces to the West African republic’s new military ruler, Maj. Gen. Johnson Aguiyi Ironsi. The peaceful surrender appeared to end the threat of further violence in the country and consolidated Gen. Ironsi’s position as the new strongman of Nigeria. When dissident Nigerian Army leaders rebelled Saturday, the country’s civilian government handed over administration of the country to Gen. Ironsi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria-jumbo-v5.png', 'height': 748, 'width': 495, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria-superJumbo-v5.png', 'height': 748, 'width': 495, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria/18iht-oldjan18-nigeria-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Nigerian Rebels Surrender', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T14:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None},