 Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Men's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3840769a-96ad-58a7-b480-2f561a3fe386', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3840769a-96ad-58a7-b480-2f561a3fe386'}, {'abstract': 'The fall 2016 men’s collections included Bottega Veneta, Salvatore Ferragamo, Neil Barrett and Versace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/fashion/mens-style/zegna-ralph-lauren-milan-mens-fashion-fall-2016.html', 'snippet': 'The fall 2016 men’s collections included Bottega Veneta, Salvatore Ferragamo, Neil Barrett and Versace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — Horizontal is not the only direction for market expansion in the rag trade. Increasingly, designer ambitions are turning vertical. Considered in global terms, the population of the One Percent amounts to a nationality of its own, a new reality duly reflected in Stefano Pilati’s Ermenegildo Zegna collection for men, titled Ermenegildo Zegna Couture.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/18Milan-01/18Milan-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Milan, Ermenegildo Zegna and Ralph Lauren Zero In on the One Percent', 'kicker': 'Fashion Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ambitions Turn Vertical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ermenegildo Zegna Holditalia SpA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauren, Ralph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Men's Fashion Week", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferragamo, Salvatore, Italia SpA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costume National', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jil Sander AG', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T15:23:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Men’s Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/087cba9e-8ab9-583f-bd16-b91e9d5a323a', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/087cba9e-8ab9-583f-bd16-b91e9d5a323a'}, {'abstract': 'The Berlusconi years were tough on men’s fashion in Italy. But now there seems to be a return to traditional sartorial values.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/14/fashion/for-italian-men-a-return-to-elegance.html', 'snippet': 'The Berlusconi years were tough on men’s fashion in Italy. But now there seems to be a return to traditional sartorial values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was vulgarity and not elegance that ruled the day in Italy when Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi was simultaneously running the country and staging “bunga bunga” bacchanals. Mr. Berlusconi was hell on traditional Italian cultural values, his years in office a prolonged populist takedown of the high-minded intellectual and aesthetic achievements that defined Italian architecture, art, industrial design and, not least, its fashion for much of the 20th century.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/17/fashion/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1/14-ITALIAN-STYLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '