'_id': 'nyt://article/a533137f-5ea3-524e-85f4-30176b9fd6b2', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a533137f-5ea3-524e-85f4-30176b9fd6b2'}, {'abstract': 'This event, part of the Coil festival, was a fusion of history and theory as performers paid tribute to a luminary of modern dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/arts/dance/review-in-excavation-site-martha-graham-usa-a-bond-is-shared.html', 'snippet': 'This event, part of the Coil festival, was a fusion of history and theory as performers paid tribute to a luminary of modern dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To Michael Kliën, choreography is more than a dance on a stage, but something akin to an archaeological dig. In “Excavation Site: Martha Graham U.S.A.,” that Austrian choreographer, with the dramaturge Steve Valk, organized a one-time event as part of the Coil festival in which 24 dancers — all but one associated with the Martha Graham Dance Company — investigated their shared bond with that luminary of modern dance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18GRAHAM/18GRAHAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Excavation Site: Martha Graham U.S.A.,’ a Bond Is Shared', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Are They Linked to a Luminary? Graham Aficionados Tell by Showing   ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coil Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Graham, Martha, Dance Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Excavation Site: Martha Graham USA (Dance)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Performance Space 122', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T22:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc226051-cd5b-5a8a-b72b-a558ba96ad10', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc226051-cd5b-5a8a-b72b-a558ba96ad10'}, {'abstract': 'In Anna Moench’s play a woman gives up her job to accompany her husband to a seminary, where she must learn to be a docile homemaker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/theater/review-in-in-quietness-a-high-powered-wife-makes-sacrifices-for-her-husbands-religious-zeal.html', 'snippet': 'In Anna Moench’s play a woman gives up her job to accompany her husband to a seminary, where she must learn to be a docile homemaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Anna Moench’s promising, frustrating “In Quietness,” produced by Dutch Kills at Walkerspace, a high-flying consultant leaves her job, her friends and her urban life to follow her husband to a seminary. At the outset of the play, Max (Kate MacCluggage) is burning up the frequent-flier miles and piling up the bonuses when she arrives home to find her husband, Paul (Blake DeLong), sitting in the dark. He confesses to an affair with a woman in his weekly Bible study group, relating that an accident has now left her in the hospital, unresponsive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 609, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 609}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1009, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2017, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18INQUIET/18INQUIET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘In Quietness,’ a High-Powered Wife Makes Sacrifices for Her Husband’s Religious Zeal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gamely Donning an Apron  for an Evangelical Husband  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'In Quietness (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moench, Anna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dutch Kills Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Danya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T22:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/84084a1e-bf1e-50de-bf70-77bab1bf756f', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84084a1e-bf1e-50de-bf70-77bab1bf756f'}, {'abstract': 'This evening of dance pieces, overseen by Rashaun Mitchell and Silas Riener, purported to explore collisions of abstraction and representation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/arts/dance/horizon-events-inspired-by-the-parameters-of-a-ps1-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'This evening of dance pieces, overseen by Rashaun Mitchell and Silas Riener, purported to explore collisions of abstraction and representation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because Rashaun Mitchell and Silas Riener are superlative dancers, a dancegoer wants them only to appear in work worthy of them, or in choreography that’s at least remotely important. In their most recent show — the premiere performances of “Horizon Events,” on Friday through Sunday at MoMA PS1 in Long Island City, Queens — they gave mere glimpses of what they and their five companion dancers can do.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2043, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/arts/18HORIZON/18HORIZON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'