and Ronn McFarlane.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: With Two Star Lutenists, Boston Early Music Festival Comes to the Morgan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lyricism Redoubled in a Lively Two-Way Conversation   ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Early Music Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Dette, Paul", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McFarlane, Ronn (1953- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Library & Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T22:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfe70547-96fe-54bf-89e7-49807e57e964', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfe70547-96fe-54bf-89e7-49807e57e964'}, {'abstract': 'After New England secured a fifth straight A.F.C. title game berth Saturday, Bill Belichick praised his players for staying committed. “It’s what we’re here for, is to win,” he said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/sports/football/patriots-singular-devotion-to-winning-produces-another-winning-run.html', 'snippet': 'After New England secured a fifth straight A.F.C. title game berth Saturday, Bill Belichick praised his players for staying committed. “It’s what we’re here for, is to win,” he said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — After the Patriots’ 27-20 victory Saturday over the previously scorching Kansas City Chiefs, New England’s coach, Bill Belichick, was asked how he felt about sharing a piece of football history: The Patriots, like the Oakland Raiders from 1973 to 1977, were headed to their fifth consecutive A.F.C. championship game.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/sports/18rhoden-web/18rhoden-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patriots’ Winning Philosophy: Keep the Focus on Winning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patriots&#8217; Winning Philosophy: Keep the Focus on Winning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-17T22:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc105c6-40c6-59ff-9928-778b9d52e0d6', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc105c6-40c6-59ff-9928-778b9d52e0d6'}, {'abstract': 'This group, which achieved fame on the PBS series “Where in the World Is Carmen Sandiego?,” performed loose-jointed, post-Motown styles infused with jazz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/arts/music/review-rockapella-sings-nostalgic-a-cappella-at-feinsteins-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'This group, which achieved fame on the PBS series “Where in the World Is Carmen Sandiego?,” performed loose-jointed, post-Motown styles infused with jazz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is it about a cappella pop groups that makes their spirit so playful? As Rockapella, an influential ensemble since the early 1990s, performed a sleek set of oldies at Feinstein’s/54 Below on Friday, the show became the musical equivalent of watching the members of a basketball team happily toss a ball around. Camaraderie and comedy go together; there’s something essentially lighthearted about human voices imitating instruments.', 'print_sectio