ity for a night out. The bullets missed him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justifiable Homicides, Taken Off the Books, Alter a Murder Tally ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justifiable Homicides, Taken Off the Books, Alter a Murder Tally ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bratton, William J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-18T01:19:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f87bc54-acac-5949-8931-b0c4777efa32', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f87bc54-acac-5949-8931-b0c4777efa32'}, {'abstract': 'The Inner Harbor project, in which a developer has received millions in public money, has started a debate about the obligations of builders to give residents meaningful aid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/nyregion/syracuse-sues-major-developer-over-local-hiring-and-tax-breaks.html', 'snippet': 'The Inner Harbor project, in which a developer has received millions in public money, has started a debate about the obligations of builders to give residents meaningful aid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The project known as Syracuse’s Inner Harbor looked like a feast for a starving city, the harbinger of the long-awaited turnarou