Golden State’s recent losses and defensive troubles could make it vulnerable to the Cavaliers, who have won nine of their last 10 games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/sports/basketball/nba-game-of-the-week-warriors-at-cavaliers.html', 'snippet': 'Despite its stellar record, Golden State’s recent losses and defensive troubles could make it vulnerable to the Cavaliers, who have won nine of their last 10 games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every week, The New York Times will choose one essential game to watch, highlighting hot teams, winning and losing streaks and statistical intrigue in the N.B.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Game of the Week: Warriors at Cavaliers ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Game of the Week: Warriors at Cavaliers ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden State Warriors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Cavaliers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-18T03:47:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonah Engel Bromwich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': 'Engel', 'lastname': 'Bromwich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/179cf04d-84aa-5b0e-bcfc-91089b309512', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/179cf04d-84aa-5b0e-bcfc-91089b309512'}, {'abstract': 'It’s tempting to think of “Billions” as a natural companion to the Oscar nominee “The Big Short,” but it most resembles “The Revenant.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/17/arts/television/billions-season-1-premiere-episode-1-review.html', 'snippet': 'It’s tempting to think of “Billions” as a natural companion to the Oscar nominee “The Big Short,” but it most resembles “The Revenant.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Oscar nominations announced this week, it’s tempting to think of Showtime’s “Billions” as a natural companion to “The Big Short,” Adam McKay’s Best Picture-nominated film about the financial shenanigans that cratered the economy in 2008. After all, this is a show about a United States Attorney attempting to prosecute just the sort of hedge fund giant who made a fortune exploiting a system that McKay exposes as fraudulent. Adding to that impression is the presence of Andrew Ross Sorkin, the founding editor of DealBook for The New York Times, who created the show with the longtime screenwriting partners Brian Koppelman and David Levien (“Rounders,” “Ocean’s Thirteen”) and who brings a level of Wall Street credibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/17BILLIONS-RECAP/17BILLIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/17BILLIONS-RECAP/17BILLIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/17BILLIONS-RECAP/17BILLIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/17BILLIONS-RECAP/17BILLIONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/arts/17BILLIONS-RECAP/17BILLIONS-RECAP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subT