d the skylight and the cold, cloudless morning. An investigator read from his clipboard: 61-year-old white male discharged from a Detroit hospital last night was found at home, shirtless, in a wheelchair, a .38-caliber handgun in his right hand. On his chest was a burn that appeared to be an exact match of the gun’s barrel. Carl Schmidt, the medical examiner, wiped the contact wound with a wet sponge.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 858}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 716, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1681, 'width': 1175, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/magazine/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder/24mag-necrobiome-placeholder-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Living Dead', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Living Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Peter Andrey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Justice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-18T12:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Andrey Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'Andrey', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ea30091-a966-5fc0-9832-a992dc6836c3', 'word_count': 2728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ea30091-a966-5fc0-9832-a992dc6836c3'}, {'abstract': 'The Egyptian author Ali Salem used humor — and all of its contradictions — to inspire peace in his country. Can other writers do the same?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/magazine/blessed-are-the-comedians.html', 'snippet': 'The Egyptian author Ali Salem used humor — and all of its contradictions — to inspire peace in his country. Can other writers do the same?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Middle East watchers, who are accustomed to reports of shootings and explosions, learning about a banned or suppressed book might be the closest thing to receiving good news. Suppression of a book, after all, is a perverse acknowledgment that literature holds the power to subvert the status quo — and without a single shot fired. If books that imagine peace are still able to put fear in the hearts of warmongers, isn’t it a sign that there’s some hope for us?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1409, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/14/magazine/14mag-alisalem-1/14mag-alisalem-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blessed Are the Comedians', 'kicker': 'Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-18T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Avi Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Avi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/826ae1e6-beb8-505e-b1fa-77e7cb48551f', 'word_count': 2383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/826ae1e6-beb8-505e-b1fa-77e7cb48551f'}, {'abstract': 'A study finds that pharmaceutical companies have cut drug prices in response to political pressure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/upshot/even-talking-about-reducing-drug-prices-can-reduce-drug-prices.html', 'snippet': 'A study finds that pharmaceutical companies have cut drug prices in response to political pressure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Both Bernie Sanders and Hillary Clinton are pushing for lower prescription drug prices as part of their campaigns. Debates about whether and how to reduce drug prices aren’t new. But they rarely lead to legislative success.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/18UP-Healthpay/18UP-Healthpay-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/15/upshot/18UP-Healthpay/18UP-Healthpay-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumb