nt': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e821d44-d475-5014-af46-0b021cc733ed'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Untouchables back Indira Gandhi in India in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/18/1966-untouchables-back-gandhi/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Untouchables back Indira Gandhi in India in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Mrs. Indira Gandhi today [Jan. 18] won the support of 80 Congress party members representing India’s untouchables in her bid to become India’s first woman prime minister. The result was a heavy blow to her chief opponent, Morarji Desai, former finance minister. He had been counting heavily on the support of the untouchables. Their support gave Mrs. Gandhi, 48, an apparently overwhelming lead in tomorrow’s election. Technically it is for leader of the Congress party, but since the party controls Parliament, its leader automatically becomes prime minister. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 19, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-indira/18iht-oldjan18-indira-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-indira/18iht-oldjan18-indira-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-indira/18iht-oldjan18-indira-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 897, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/blogs/18iht-oldjan18-indira/18iht-oldjan18-indira-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1794, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 