, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/nyregion/19NEEDIESTLEWIS/19NEEDIESTLEWIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/19/nyregion/19NEEDIESTLEWIS/19NEEDIESTLEWIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/nyregion/19NEEDIESTLEWIS/19NEEDIESTLEWIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Woman’s Mission: Teaching Her Children to Stay ‘Full of Hope’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Woman’s Mission: Teaching Her Children to Stay ‘Full of Hope’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rojas, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federation of Protestant Welfare Agencies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T03:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38c48bef-0180-5b7b-bbe2-4ee0dc48d3b4', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38c48bef-0180-5b7b-bbe2-4ee0dc48d3b4'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Nikola Gruevski submitted his resignation on Friday as part of an agreement forged by Johannes Hahn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/world/europe/macedonia-elections-scheduled-but-opposition-threatens-boycott.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Nikola Gruevski submitted his resignation on Friday as part of an agreement forged by Johannes Hahn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Macedonia’s governing coalition is moving forward with a European Union-brokered plan for elections in April even though the opposition has threatened to boycott the vote, which would be run by a caretaker government. Johannes Hahn, the European Union commissioner who took the leading role in the negotiations for ending the political crisis in the Balkan country, said he would have preferred a consensual solution regarding the date of the elections. Prime Minister Nikola Gruevski submitted his resignation on Friday as part of an agreement forged by Mr. Hahn. That agreement sought to end a political crisis that erupted last February over a wiretapping scandal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Macedonia: Elections Scheduled, but Opposition Threatens Boycott', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe; Macedonia: Elections Scheduled, but Opposition Threatens Boycott', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Macedonia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gruevski, Nikola (1970- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T03:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aleksandar Dimishkovski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aleksandar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dimishkovski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/467ed093-8d7b-5318-b6df-107e64687cb7', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/467ed093-8d7b-5318-b6df-107e64687cb7'}, {'abstract': 'The scale of a tuberculosis outbreak in rural Perry County widened Monday when state officials said that 47 residents last week tested positive for the bacterial infection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/us/alabama-more-test-positive-for-tuberculosis.html', 'snippet': 'The scale of a tuberculosis outbreak in rural Perry County widened Monday when state officials said that 47 residents last week tested positive for the bacterial infection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scale of a tuberculosis outbreak in rural Perry County widened Monday when state officials said that 47 residents last week tested positive for the bacterial infection. Those people, who are suspected of having an asymptomatic infection, will receive additional health care services as the authorities try to stop an outbreak that has now sickened or infected 73 people in and near Perry County since January 2014. In Perry County, which has fewer than 10,000 residents, three people have died. State officials previously said that the outbreak, which has mostly affected African-Americans, was concentrated in the county seat of Marion, and that Marion’s tuberculosis incidence rate was worse than those recorded in many developing countries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama: More Test Positive for Tuberculosis', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama: More Test Positive for Tuberculosis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuberculosis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Perry County (Ala)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marion (Ala)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T03:22:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f9255ec-662c-5866-92b0-761bb0a89744', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f9255ec-662c-5866-92b0-761bb0a89744'}, {'abstract': 'The man, whom Belgian and Moroccan news sources identified as Gelel Attar, is of Belgian and Moroccan background, as were most of those who participated in the attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/world/africa/morocco-belgian-linked-to-leader-of-the-paris-attacks-is-arrested.html', 'snippet': 'The man, whom Belgian and Moroccan news sources identified as Gelel Attar, is of Belgian and Moroccan background, as were most of those who participated in the attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moroccan officials announced Monday that they had detained a Belgian man thought to be a close friend of one of the leaders of the attacks in Paris on Nov. 13. The man, whom Belgian and Moroccan news sources identified as Gelel Attar, is of Belgian and Moroccan background, as were most of those who participated in the attacks. Mr. Attar was sentenced in absentia at a trial last summer in Belgium to five years in prison for involvement in a terrorist network. Two of the Paris attackers were also sentenced in absentia in that trial: Abdelhamid Abaaoud, who helped organize the attacks, and Chakib Akrouh, one of the attackers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morocco: Belgian Linked to Leader of the Paris Attacks Is Arrested', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; Morocco: Belgian Linked to Leader of the Paris Attacks Is Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Alissa Johannsen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Attar, Gelel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Attacks (November 2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morocco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T03:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d28bd289-65d5-5576-8319-25265a3f5c03', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d28bd289-65d5-5576-8319-25265a3f5c03'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jonas was a prominent Canadian newspaper columnist whose controversial book about Israeli counterterrorists was the basis of the 2005 film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/books/george-jonas-whose-book-was-the-basis-of-the-film-munich-dies-at-80.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jonas was a prominent Canadian newspaper columnist whose controversial book about Israeli counterterrorists was the basis of the 2005 film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Jonas, a prominent Canadian newspaper columnist whose controversial book about Israeli counterterrorists was the basis of the 2005 film “Munich,” directed by Steven Spielberg, died on Jan. 10 in Toronto. He was 80.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/