 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c191d4c5-ce83-5bec-9399-5c9d62622ff3', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c191d4c5-ce83-5bec-9399-5c9d62622ff3'}, {'abstract': 'Legislation planned for Senate introduction would interfere with regulation of big banks and businesses and limit protections for ordinary Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/opinion/deregulating-corporate-america.html', 'snippet': 'Legislation planned for Senate introduction would interfere with regulation of big banks and businesses and limit protections for ordinary Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you think Congress is hopelessly divided on party lines on every issue, think again. When it comes to regulating — more precisely, deregulating — corporate America, Republicans and Democrats are all too eager to find common ground.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/opinion/EDregulation/EDregulation-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/18/opinion/EDregulation/EDregulation-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/opinion/EDregulation/EDregulation-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/opinion/EDregulation/EDregulation-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/18/opinion/EDregulation/EDregulation-thumbStanda