rge': 'images/2016/01/19/us/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/us/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/us/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1466, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/us/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/19/us/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/us/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb/20CHRISTIEMARRIAGEweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Christie Offers a Key to Marital Success: Fight in a Walk-In Closet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie, in Book, Offers a Key to Marital Success, if Not Bliss: Fight in a Closet ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Mary Pat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Matt (Journalist)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "American Governor: Chris Christie's Bridge to Redemption (Book)", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T10:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/770d8d77-d2e7-59aa-94c5-e8ec629979ed', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/770d8d77-d2e7-59aa-94c5-e8ec629979ed'}, {'abstract': 'Two new books by very different authors agree that the buffoonery on the right is bad not just for conservatism but for America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/books/review/why-the-right-went-wrong-and-too-dumb-to-fail.html', 'snippet': 'Two new books by very different authors agree that the buffoonery on the right is bad not just for conservatism but for America.', 'lead_paragraph': ' “May you live in interesting times” is said to be a Chinese curse. The same kind of curse may apply to people who support interesting parties. There is no doubt that the Republicans are more interesting than the Democrats at the moment — their rhetoric is more incendiary, their divisions more profound, their behavior more outlandish. But the very antics that encourage people to tune in to the presidential debates also discourage them from pulling the voting lever: Hillary Clinton’s chances of winning the White House in November seem to be getting higher largely because she is a safe pair of hands. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24WOOLDRIDGEJP1/24WOOLDRIDGEjp01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Why the Right Went Wrong’ and ‘Too Dumb to Fail’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Why the Right Went Wrong’ and ‘Too Dumb to Fail’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dionne, E J Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Matt K (1975- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Why the Right Went Wrong: Conservatism - From Goldwater to the Tea Party and Beyond (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Too Dumb to Fail: How the GOP Betrayed the Reagan Revolution to Win Elections (and How It Can Reclaim Its Conservative Roots) (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T10:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adrian Wooldridge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adrian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wooldridge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b10d28-27b8-5701-ade6-d8b4aadf93e2', 'word_count': 1446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b10d28-27b8-5701-ade6-d8b4aadf93e2'}, {'abstract': 'A senior official of the Khyber tribal region said the attacker had detonated an explosive vest at a militia checkpoint just outside the northern city of Peshawar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/world/asia/peshawar-blast-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'A senior official of the Khyber tribal region said the attacker had detonated an explosive vest at a militia checkpoint just outside the northern city of Peshawar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan — An explosion, said to be a suicide bombing, at a militia checkpoint just outside this Pakistani city killed eight people and wounded at least 11 on Tuesday morning, a senior official of the Khyber tribal region said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Explosion, Said to Be Suicide Bombing, Kills 8 in Northwest Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Asia; Pakistan: Explosion Kills 8 People at Checkpoint in Khyber Region', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Ismail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (Pakistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peshawar (Pakistan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T10:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ismail Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/693aecc0-ac6a-5bcb-9ff3-eca2758686b8', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/693aecc0-ac6a-5bcb-9ff3-eca2758686b8'}, {'abstract': '“Dark Money” argues that the Koch brothers and a small number of allied plutocrats have essentially hijacked American democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/books/review/dark-money-by-jane-mayer.html', 'snippet': '“Dark Money” argues that the Koch brothers and a small number of allied plutocrats have essentially hijacked American democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nineteen eighty was a year of hope for conservatives in America, but it was a hope diminished by decades of consistent failure at the grass roots. Republicans hadn’t controlled either chamber of Congress, or a majority in state legislatures, for a quarter-century. Most governors were Democrats, as had been true since 1970. Not only was the Republican Party overmatched at winning elections, but those with the strongest ideological convictions — “movement conservatives,” as they liked to call themselves — were a faint voice even within Republican ranks.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1532, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB/0124-BKS-Cover-WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'h