London office in 2013 amid an insider trading investigation by authorities in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/business/dealbook/point72-steven-cohens-firm-reopens-office-in-london.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cohen’s former firm, SAC Capital Advisors, closed its London office in 2013 amid an insider trading investigation by authorities in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Steven A. Cohen, the billionaire investor, has returned to London, less than three years after his former firm, SAC Capital Advisors, closed its office in London amid an insider trading investigation by authorities in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Point72, Steven Cohen’s Firm, Reopens Office in London', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Point72 Asset Management LP', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T13:20:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47776406-fa74-57fc-a22a-11c251fbcc51', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47776406-fa74-57fc-a22a-11c251fbcc51'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: French hostages are welcomed back in Paris in 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/1916-france-welcomes-hostages/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: French hostages are welcomed back in Paris in 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris gave an enthusiastic welcome yesterday evening to the ten French hostages, mayors and prominent residents in the invaded departments taken prisoners early in the war, upon their arrival at the Gare de Lyon at 7.25. A great crowd assembled outside the station and the platform was lined with friends and relatives and many deputies and government officials. As the train steamed into the station, the crowd raised a great cry of ‘‘Vive la France!’’\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 20, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1916: France Welcomes Hostages', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T13:25:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c58621e4-8cc3-5204-99df-a6a958c67d2f', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c58621e4-8cc3-5204-99df-a6a958c67d2f'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Jenner will write the book, tentatively scheduled to be released in the spring of 2017, with the Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist Buzz Bissinger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/books/caitlyn-jenner-to-publish-a-memoir-about-her-transformation.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Jenner will write the book, tentatively scheduled to be released in the spring of 2017, with the Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist Buzz Bissinger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caitlyn Jenner — the reality TV star and prominent transgender activist — will publish a memoir about her highly public transformation from the Olympic track star and motivational speaker Bruce Jenner into a glamorous transgender woman, Caitlyn Marie Jenner.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 917}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1120, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/arts/20JENNERweb/20JENNERweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width':