37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4ee34f1-6d2e-52a4-a76f-2b0d235e718c', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4ee34f1-6d2e-52a4-a76f-2b0d235e718c'}, {'abstract': 'The producer and N.W.A. member says the film was heavily promoted to Academy voters, but he worried the subject of gangsta rap would be an issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/movies/ice-cube-and-the-obstacles-facing-compton.html', 'snippet': 'The producer and N.W.A. member says the film was heavily promoted to Academy voters, but he worried the subject of gangsta rap would be an issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s do a throwback Tuesday to last week, a few days before the Oscar nominations were announced, unleashing a torrent of fury over the omission of black actors and films about black characters. The prospects for “Straight Outta Compton,” directed by F. Gary Gray, looked bright: many forecast it would receive a best picture nomination (it did not). Ice Cube, a producer on the film, which depicts the rise of his group, N.W.A., met with the Bagger at the Roosevelt Hotel in Hollywood. He talked about his son O’Shea Jackson Jr., who plays Cube in the film, the therapeutic value of gangsta rap, and what would be lost if “Compton” did not get a nomination. Here are excerpts from the conversation:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 768}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/19ICE-CUBE/19ICE-CUBE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ice Cube and the Obstacles Facing ‘Compton’', 'kicker': 'The Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ice Cube (1969- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Straight Outta Compton (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T17:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role':