2ae718266e'}, {'abstract': 'The court refused in October to address the issue of what prosecutors need to prove to obtain convictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/business/supreme-court-agrees-to-hear-insider-trading-case.html', 'snippet': 'The court refused in October to address the issue of what prosecutors need to prove to obtain convictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Tuesday agreed to resolve a dispute about what prosecutors need to prove to obtain insider trading convictions. The question has divided federal appeals courts, and the justices declined to address it in October.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Will Hear a California Insider Trading Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Will Hear a California Insider Trading Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salman, Bassam (1957- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verrilli, Donald B Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T18:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41d44dc8-5e16-511c-ad2c-2d274e14321b', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41d44dc8-5e16-511c-ad2c-2d274e14321b'}, {'abstract': 'The presidential candidate will not be at the World Economic Forum. But the force behind his unlikely campaign for the White House will be a focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/business/dealbook/why-donald-trumps-shadow-looms-over-davos.html', 'snippet': 'The presidential candidate will not be at the World Economic Forum. But the force behind his unlikely campaign for the White House will be a focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump’s presence will be felt at the World Economic Forum this year, even though he isn’t actually expected to attend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Donald Trump’s Shadow Looms Over Davos', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T18:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a17f2b9-5291-5670-8ced-2bc884596b9b', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a17f2b9-5291-5670-8ced-2bc884596b9b'}, {'abstract': 'The plot of the Headlands Gamble, set in a series of secluded Marin County towns, revolves around the fictional mystery of a missing racehorse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/19/t-magazine/travel/headlands-gamble-first-person-travel.html', 'snippet': 'The plot of the Headlands Gamble, set in a series of secluded Marin County towns, revolves around the fictional mystery of a missing racehorse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to imagine a more intriguing description of a weekend escape than “like being the detective in Twin Peaks,” which is how Gabe Smedresman likes to advertise his latest offering, the Headlands Gamble. Smedresman calls himself a producer of “mixed-reality entertainment” — his prior projects include the pseudo-stock-market game Pretweeting (a way to make the most of the Times Newswire API) and the Hearst Collection, “a real-life maze in which people who enter try to steal works of art without tripping laser alarms,” reported the journalist Harold Goldberg in 2013. The Headlands Gamble pulls together these key themes as the inaugural trip of First Person Travel, Smedresman’s new “immersed-narrative travel agency.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/t-magazine/19tmag-headlands/19tmag-headlands-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/19/t-magazine/19tmag-headlands/19tmag-headlands-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/t-magazine/19tmag-headlands/19tmag-headlands-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/t-magazine/19tmag-headlands/19tmag-headlands-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't