 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c831e574-4e36-5f72-82fb-ba73e8602955', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c831e574-4e36-5f72-82fb-ba73e8602955'}, {'abstract': 'From its caviar-filled eggs to its chocolate cake with sesame ganache, the upscale Chinese restaurant in the Waldorf Astoria offers sophisticated surprises.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/dining/la-chine-review.html', 'snippet': 'From its caviar-filled eggs to its chocolate cake with sesame ganache, the upscale Chinese restaurant in the Waldorf Astoria offers sophisticated surprises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a nest of dried grass and feathery moss sat an eggshell, its top neatly lopped off. Caviar and a crinkle of gold leaf shone just inside the rim. Underneath were layers of custard and hairy crab, a seasonal freshwater treat from China whose taste is a lot more seductive than its name. The rich, smooth pleasure in each spoonful almost made my head pop.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Imagination Worth the Added Price at Midtown’s La Chine', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Investment in Imaginative Chinese Cooking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waldorf Astoria Hotels and Resorts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Chine (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-19T19:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname