dcc8-2f49-568a-9e96-8d33afca4ef5'}, {'abstract': 'The Congressional Budget Office reported that deficits, in decline for six years, will begin expanding again sooner than expected, posing tricky questions for presidential candidates of both parties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/business/economy/falling-deficit-to-reverse-course-in-2016-as-us-ages.html', 'snippet': 'The Congressional Budget Office reported that deficits, in decline for six years, will begin expanding again sooner than expected, posing tricky questions for presidential candidates of both parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A six-year trend of declining federal budget deficits will end this year, sooner than expected, the nonpartisan Congressional Budget Office reported on Tuesday — a development that injects new questions into the presidential race for candidates proposing trillions of dollars in new tax cuts or spending.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Falling Deficit to Reverse Course in 2016 as U.S. Ages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falling Deficit to Reverse Course in ’16 as U.S. Ages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Budget', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bipartisan Policy Center', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T00:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/926f4c63-e164-54ca-bf47-902904049e96', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/926f4c63-e164-54ca-bf47-902904049e96'}, {'abstract': 'Twelve young Palestinians killed over three months in clashes with Israelis were from a West Bank town known as the hotbed of the latest wave of stabbings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/world/middleeast/anger-in-a-palestinian-town-feeds-a-cycle-of-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Twelve young Palestinians killed over three months in clashes with Israelis were from a West Bank town known as the hotbed of the latest wave of stabbings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SA’IR, West Bank — Raed Jaradat was 22, an accounting student from a well-to-do family here, already working part time with his father in his stone quarry and construction business. After Dania Ersheid, 17, was shot and killed by Israeli soldiers who said she had pulled a knife at the Ibrahimi Mosque in Hebron, a version disputed by Palestinians, Mr. Jaradat wrote an angry post on Facebook: “Imagine if this were your sister!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/world/20HEBRON-web1/20HEBRON-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/20/world/20HEBRON-web1/20HEBRON-web1-a