-RM5I/20160119-lens-meg-slide-RM5I-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tuff Enough’ in New Orleans’s Queer Community', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T07:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8a1ea925-3273-5ba2-ac59-679320eb081c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8a1ea925-3273-5ba2-ac59-679320eb081c'}, {'abstract': 'A collaborative portrait project of New Orleans’s queer community began with Meg Turner’s realization that history books and galleries didn’t reflect the people and lives she knew.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/tuff-enough-in-new-orleanss-queer-community/', 'snippet': 'A collaborative portrait project of New Orleans’s queer community began with Meg Turner’s realization that history books and galleries didn’t reflect the people and lives she knew.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between-ness is an idea that gives us pause. As human beings, we have evolved to put virtually everything we see, hear and experience into neat boxes, carefully labeled and stored away. Places, tastes and people that deviate make us squirm and, like toddlers, we try to cram those square blocks into round holes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tuff Enough’ in New Orleans’s Queer Community', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Meg (Photographer)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T08:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Naughton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Naughton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57c13e19-8896-5f01-9301-7b5aa401b5a7', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57c13e19-8896-5f01-9301-7b5aa401b5a7'}, {'abstract': 'A day before a planned meeting with Chinese officials, a senior State Department envoy urged Beijing to do more to curb the North’s nuclear ambitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/world/asia/north-korea-nuclear-china.html', 'snippet': 'A day before a planned meeting with Chinese officials, a senior State Department envoy urged Beijing to do more to curb the North’s nuclear ambitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The United States and its allies will bolster sanctions and go on the defensive against North Korea in ways that China may not like if Beijing fails to lend greater support to efforts to curb the North’s nuclear ambitions, a top American diplomat said here on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/world/21korea/21korea-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Weighs Tighter Sanctions on North Korea if China Fails to Act', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Asia; North Korea: U.S. Presses China to Curb Ally’s Nuclear Program', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Tests', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinken, Antony J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T08:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0486467e-d69c-5b9d-978c-a7e5e190853c', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0486467e-d69c-5b9d-978c-a7e5e190853c'}, {'abstract': 'What if the eras of the E.U., high growth in China, expensive oil and newly independent nations’ economic foundations are all over?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/opinion/what-if.html', 'snippet': 'What if the eras of the E.U., high growth in China, expensive oil and newly independent nations’ economic foundations are all over?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZURICH — Just get me talking about the world today and I can pretty well ruin any dinner party. I don’t mean to, but I find it hard not to look around and wonder whether the recent turmoil in international markets isn’t just the product of tremors but rather of seismic shifts in the foundational pillars of the global system, with highly unpredictable consequences.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What If?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What  If?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T08:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5c1f9d9-5713-5a53-80d6-d86929db8d12', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5c1f9d9-5713-5a53-80d6-d86929db8d12'}, {'abstract': 'The Eagles’ music survives Mr. Frey’s death as it did the band’s breakup.', 'web_url': 'https://www