ardino, Calif, Shooting (2015)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristol, William', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T08:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab730a73-8cd0-53d3-b9cf-f8a43e3bc5d7', 'word_count': 1401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab730a73-8cd0-53d3-b9cf-f8a43e3bc5d7'}, {'abstract': 'The Iran case showed that the use of diplomacy was the best course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/opinion/mr-obamas-wise-call-on-a-prisoner-swap.html', 'snippet': 'The Iran case showed that the use of diplomacy was the best course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was inevitable that the prisoner exchange with Iran would be questioned as soon as it was announced — and not just by Republicans who mechanically assail anything President Obama does. The notion of making concessions to a hostile adversary to secure the release of one’s fellow citizens has always been controversial, pitting the innate longing to win their freedom against the risk that handing over money or releasing prisoners in exchange will only encourage the captors to seize more. This dilemma has bedeviled many presidents and governments through history, with no simple or single answer. In this case, President Obama did the right thing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1483, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/opinion/20wed2sub/20wed2sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Obama’s Wise Call on a Prisoner Swap', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Obama’s Wise Call on a Prisoner Swap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foley, James (1973-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T08:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/17e35e3c-f72f-59b3-8146-07fad14f04f3', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17e35e3c-f72f-59b3-8146-07fad14f04f3'}, {'abstract': 'The company expects fourth-quarter earnings to fall by about half, before a vote next week on its deal to acquire BG Group. Oil prices were down nearly 7 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/business/energy-environment/shell-q4-earnings-oil-prices.html', 'snippet': 'The company expects fourth-quarter earnings to fall by about half, before a vote next week on its deal to acquire BG Group. Oil prices were down nearly 7 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In the latest sign of industry damage from the plummeting price of oil, Royal Dutch Shell said on Wednesday that it expected its profit for the fourth quarter of 2015 to be about half of what it was in the comparable period a year earlier.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/business/21Shell/21Shell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/business/21Shell/21Shell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, '