. But how?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/supporting-a-teen-with-a-friend-in-need/', 'snippet': 'When your son stays up through the night to text with a buddy who is falling apart, you need to step in. But how?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not unusual for teenagers to need adult guidance on caring for their friends who have problems. Though teens are often characterized as being persistently self-centered, or for girls in particular, mean, anyone who spends a lot of time with adolescents can tell you that those stereotypes aren’t fair. Teenagers are devoted to their friends and, more often than not, they will sacrifice their time and comfort to buoy a friend who is sinking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/health/motherlode_teen/motherlode_teen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/19/health/motherlode_teen/motherlode_teen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 494}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/health/motherlode_teen/motherlode_teen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/health/motherlode_teen/motherlode_teen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1687, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/19/health/motherlode_teen/motherlode_teen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/19/health/motherlode_teen/motherlode_teen-thumbSt