 in operas are tacked on: divertissements unrelated to the story. In the premiere of “Quicksand,” an opera-novel told in the form of a mystery by the composer Robert Ashley (who died in 2014), the choreographer Steve Paxton abides by that approach; his movement may color the text, but it doesn’t describe it. He’s keeping the choreography, in his words, “low-key.” Mr. Ashley met Mr. Paxton in the 1960s, and though they worked together, “Quicksand” — a merging of music, light and dance — is considered their only major collaboration.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24GUIDE10/24GUIDE10-thumbLarge.jpg', 