': 'nyt://slideshow/60805150-faed-5d51-87e8-e3c939b6af5a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/60805150-faed-5d51-87e8-e3c939b6af5a'}, {'abstract': 'The festival, founded by the late conductor Lorin Maazel, announced this week that it is canceling most of this summer’s offerings due to financial difficulties.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/castleton-festival-to-go-on-hiatus/', 'snippet': 'The festival, founded by the late conductor Lorin Maazel, announced this week that it is canceling most of this summer’s offerings due to financial difficulties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Castleton Festival, which the conductor Lorin Maazel founded in 2009 on his estate in rural Virginia, announced this week that it is canceling most of this summer’s offerings in what festival officials described as a “temporary hiatus” brought on by financial difficulties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Castleton Festival to Go on Hiatus', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vienna State Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T20:44:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1959439-e312-5e45-96f8-430c4aa94459', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1959439-e312-5e45-96f8-430c4aa94459'}, {'abstract': 'After stops at the Brooklyn Academy of Music and in Seattle, the ailing choreographer’s company will focus on intimate works and education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/arts/dance/sending-the-trisha-brown-legacy-back-into-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'After stops at the Brooklyn Academy of Music and in Seattle, the ailing choreographer’s company will focus on intimate works and education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once upon a time, a choreographer made dances, and extraordinary ones at that. Her works, full of wit and rigor, unfolded on rooftops and rafts and even on the sides of buildings as well as in lofts and galleries, and later on proscenium stages. And then she couldn’t make them anymore.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 605}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2030, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24TRISHA1/24TRISHA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sending the Trisha Brown Legacy Back Into the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sending a Legacy Back Into the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Trisha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown, Trisha, Dance Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Trisha Brown: In Plain Site (Dance)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Proscenium Works, 1979-2011 (Dance)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T20:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/837d5e64-ddab-5258-b701-d65ce7292291', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/837d5e64-ddab-5258-b701-d65ce7292291'}, {'abstract': 'From what you sip to how often you exfoliate, Kristina Holey believes both internal and external wellness work together for a great complexion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/20/t-magazine/how-to-fix-winter-skin-kristina-holey.html', 'snippet': 'From what you sip to how often you exfoliate, Kristina Holey believes both internal and external wellness work together for a great complexion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cult facialist Kristina Holey, whose holistic approach to skincare favors healthy habits (eating well, exercising, sleeping) over a medicine cabinet full of topical antidotes, might be the beauty industry’s worst nightmare. Her modus operandi — that there is no universal rule for the skin, and each person requires a unique regimen — rejects the idea of any products touted as a quick fix cure-all. Yet it is this long-term strategy towards skincare that has seen Holey become San Francisco’s most sought-after facialist (she opened her own skincare center in June), with clients also clamoring to see her in Los Angeles and New York, where she works out of the West Village boutique Calliope.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/20/t-magazine/12tmag-holey01/12tmag-holey01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Tips for Curing Winter Skin, From a Cult Facialist', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holey, Kristina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calliope (Manhattan, NY, Retailer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-20T20:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Olivia Fleming', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Olivia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fleming', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd3370e-f4bc-5fce-8417-56131a6371ea', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd3370e-f4bc-5fce-8417-56131a6371ea'}, {'abstract': 'Descriptions of female singers can be narrow, with purity a recurrent concept. But that’s not how the artists see it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/arts/music/early-music-ensembles-praised-as-pure-but-seeking-more.html', 'snippet': 'Descriptions of female singers can be narrow, with purity a recurrent concept. But that’s not how the artists see it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the female vocal quartet Anonymous 4 retired last month, it left behind a discography spanning a thousand years of music. But the core of its repertory was medieval music in which, in plainchant passages, the four women’s voices seemed to melt together into one silky, unison line.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/arts/24PURITY1/24PURITY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Early-Music Ensembles: Praised as Pure, but Seeking More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Praised as Pure, but Seeking More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': '