 America mini-series, written by Tom Rob Smith and directed by Jakob Verbruggen, is a loopy mix of romance and conspiracy thriller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard not to care about a character played by Ben Whishaw, an actor whose nimble intensity has enlivened roles from Richard II, in “The Hollow Crown” cycle, to Q in the Bond movies. But during BBC America’s “London Spy,” a five-episode mini-series (beginning on Thursday) that’s a loopy mix of love story and conspiracy thriller, you may find yourself managing it for long stretches.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 276}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 287, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 287, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21SPY/21SPY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'c