 dacha just outside Moscow. He spent enough of his final hours unattended to give a vindictive alternative historian some wiggle room.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 890, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 890}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 691, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1381, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/arts/21BOOKGOLDBERG/21BOOKGOLDBERG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Yid,’ Paul Goldberg’s First Novel, Taunts Stalin', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stalin Purge Wrapped in a Yiddish Yarn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'