s.com/2016/01/21/nyregion/filing-says-success-academy-network-discriminated-against-students-with-disabilities.html', 'snippet': 'Parents of 13 current and former students of Success Academy filed a complaint against the charter school network with the federal Department of Education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents of 13 current and former students of Success Academy filed a complaint with the Office of Civil Rights with the federal Education Department on Wednesday, accusing the charter school network of discriminating against students with disabilities by denying them accommodations and in some cases pushing them out.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Filing Alleges Bias at Success Academy Network Against Students With Disabilities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filing Alleges School Group Discriminates ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Success Academy Charter Schools', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T02:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d7ddd9-bab2-5f6e-9bd4-06ff182fc75e', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d7ddd9-bab2-5f6e-9bd4-06ff182fc75e'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly half the people in the country are now facing hunger, the main food aid agency of the United Nations said Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/world/africa/central-african-republic-hunger-threatens-population-un-warns.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly half the people in the country are now facing hunger, the main food aid agency of the United Nations said Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nearly 2.5 million people in the Central African Republic — half the population — are now facing hunger, double the figure from a year ago, the main food aid agency of the United Nations said Wednesday. The agency, the World Food Program, attributed the increase to years of conflict and insecurity that have kept people from tending their fields and livestock, exacerbated by a poor harvest. “This is not the run-of-the-mill emergency,” Guy Adoua, the agency’s deputy director for the country, said in a statement. “People are left with nothing.” The agency called for an emergency cash infusion of $41 million from donor countries to deal with the crisis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Central African Republic: Hunger Threatens Population, U.N. Warns', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; Central African Republic: Hunger Threatens Population, U.N. Warns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Famine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malnutrition', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World