I was the guest speaker at the American Civil Liberties Union of Michigan’s annual dinner. Before I spoke, the group called to the stage a longtime investigative journalist who had done tremendous work bringing the Flint water crisis to light. His name was Curt Guyette. He, in turn, recognized the scientists, doctors, politician, lawyers and activists who had helped in that quest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/opinion/22blowWeb1/22blowWeb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Poisoning of Flint’s Water', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flint (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lead', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Richard Dale', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T08:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles M. Blow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ace5dc5-67f3-507f-9194-4743a19c2bce', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ace5dc5-67f3-507f-9194-4743a19c2bce'}, {'abstract': 'In recent years, the Supreme Court has waved the First Amendment banner ever higher to undermine long-accepted governmental regulatory authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/opinion/scalias-putsch-at-the-supreme-court.html', 'snippet': 'In recent years, the Supreme Court has waved the First Amendment banner ever higher to undermine long-accepted governmental regulatory authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN his vitriolic dissent last June from the Supreme Court’s same-sex marriage decision, Justice Antonin Scalia accused the majority of having carried out a “judicial putsch.” Justice Scalia should know. He and his four conservative colleagues were then in the process of executing one themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scalia’s Putsch at the Supreme Court', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Teachers Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALITO, SAMUEL A JR', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breyer, Stephen G', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carvin, Michael A', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T08:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5295f24b-cbaf-595c-98fe-0cf3208eb243', 'word_count': 1485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5295f24b-cbaf-595c-98fe-0cf3208eb243'}, {'abstract': 'The justices properly ruled that companies can’t avoid class actions by buying off individual plaintiffs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/opinion/an-important-win-in-the-supreme-court-for-class-actions.html', 'snippet': 'The justices properly ruled that companies can’t avoid class actions by buying off individual plaintiffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, the Supreme Court gave an important victory to regular Americans, ruling that companies may not avoid class-action lawsuits by offering to buy off the individual plaintiffs before they can establish a class of similarly harmed people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 742}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 828, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 969, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21thu1/21thu1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Important Win in the Supreme Court for Class Actions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Important Win for Class Actions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Campbell-Ewald', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsburg, Ruth Bader', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T08:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8486654b-339d-504d-a809-674efc5622a7', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8486654b-339d-504d-a809-674efc5622a7'}, {'abstract': 'We need to leverage populist frustration into constructive postelection policy. It’s been done before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/opinion/america-the-unfair.html', 'snippet': 'We need to leverage populist frustration into constructive postelection policy. It’s been done before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump and Bernie Sanders don’t agree on much. Nor do the Black Lives Matter movement, the Occupy Wall Street protests and the armed ranchers who seized public lands in Oregon. But in the insurgent presidential campaigns and in social activism across the spectrum, a common thread is people angry at the way this country is no longer working for many ordinary citizens.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 597}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1019, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular/kristof-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1862, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America the Unfair?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America the Unfair?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flint (Mich)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T08:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0cc8e70-5a67-5e2a-bb5f-a59a34bd5708', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0cc8e70-5a67-5e2a-bb5f-a59a34bd5708'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans talk about their commitment to the poor. So why haven’t we heard the party’s candidates talk about the crisis in Flint, Mich.?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/opinion/republicans-ignore-a-poisoned-city.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans talk about their commitment to the poor. So why haven’t we heard the party’s candidates talk about the crisis in Flint, Mich.?', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVER since I became a conservative as a teenager growing up in the city of Flint, Mich., I’ve heard again and again from Republican leaders about their commitment to minorities and the poor. Even today, we are told that conservative solutions exist for persistent poverty, for joblessness, for the masses of people, like those in my hometown, who live lives of quiet despair. House Speaker Paul Ryan has been especially eloquent on this point. If only Republicans would get a chance to prove it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21latimer/21latimer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 525, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21latimer/21latimer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 525}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21latimer/21latimer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21latimer/21latimer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1209, 'width': 1383, 's