old them hostage.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/works-sighted-ursula-le-guin-on-the-oregon-occupation/', 'snippet': '“Ammon Bundy and his bullyboys aren’t trying to free federal lands,” the novelist and longtime Oregon resident wrote, “but to hold them hostage.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ursula Le Guin, the author of the famous “Earthsea”\xa0series and a longtime Oregon resident, was displeased with The Oregonian’s coverage of the armed occupation of the Malheur National Wildlife Refuge. In a letter to the editor of the paper, she wrote:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Works Sighted: Ursula Le Guin on the Oregon Occupation', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malheur National Wildlife Refuge (Oregon)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T16:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6886c962-2c1f-538f-a433-7bba0d476d04', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6886c962-2c1f-538f-a433-7bba0d476d04'}, {'abstract': 'Conservative intellectuals fear Mr. Trump will spell the end of conservatism, while the cadre in Washington fears Mr. Cruz will build a new party machine and bypass them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/us/politics/donald-trump-ted-cruz-republican-establishment.html', 'snippet': 'Conservative intellectuals fear Mr. Trump will spell the end of conservatism, while the cadre in Washington fears Mr. Cruz will build a new party machine and bypass the