 of the artist’s work reflects a postwar mood of absurdity.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Enrico Baj” at Luxembourg & Dayan is a hoot and an eye-opener. Surveying about 16 years of works in several modes, the exhibition reintroduces the Italian artist Enrico Baj (1924-2003) to New York after an absence of three or four decades. This townhouse gallery is overflowing with his works, which confirms quite emphatically that there is more to postwar Italian art than the relatively pure abstraction of artists like Lucio Fontana, Piero Manzoni and Alberto Burri.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 734}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1675, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22BAJALTGALLERY2/22BAJALTGALLERY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Italian Artist Enrico Baj at Luxembourg & Dayan', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Italian Artist Enrico Baj at Luxembourg &amp; Dayan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Luxembourg & Dayan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baj, Enrico (1924-2003)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T21:18:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb639ba-32ad-5ec2-a777-4f119d0a72ca', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb639ba-32ad-5ec2-a777-4f119d0a72ca'}, {'abstract': 'The actors, starring in “The Free World” at this year’s festival, share thoughts on making the most of Park City — and some “Making a Murderer” theories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/21/t-magazine/entertainment/elisabeth-moss-boyd-holbrook-sundance-tips.html', 'snippet': 'The actors, starring in “The Free World” at this year’s festival, share thoughts on making the most of Park City — and some “Making a Murderer” theories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the most anticipated titles in competition at the 2016 Sundance Film Festival, kicking off today and running through Jan. 31 in Park City, Utah, is “The Free World,” an atmospheric drama from first-time filmmaker Jason Lew. The film stars Boyd Holbrook as a man wrongfully imprisoned for a grisly crime he didn’t commit who, upon his release, meets an equally scarred woman (played by Elisabeth Moss of “Mad Men”) who again turns his life upside down. The two actors and friends are no strangers to Sundance — Holbrook first attended in 2011 with the drama “Higher Ground,” directed by Vera Farmiga, and Moss made her first trip in 2013 for the Sundance Channel series “Top of the Lake.” Here, they share a few things they’ve learned along the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance1/21tmag-sundance-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance1/21tmag-sundance-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance1/21tmag-sundance-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance1/21tmag-sundance-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance1/21tmag-sundance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance1/21tmag-sundance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-sundance