, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/062d1702-489a-5abb-b266-22351aa551d8', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/062d1702-489a-5abb-b266-22351aa551d8'}, {'abstract': 'The company that reorganized New York City Opera presents its first production, starring Kristin Sampson, at the Rose Theater at Jazz at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/arts/music/review-tosca-from-nyco-renaissance-puts-a-grand-ambition-to-the-test.html', 'snippet': 'The company that reorganized New York City Opera presents its first production, starring Kristin Sampson, at the Rose Theater at Jazz at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seldom has so much ridden on a single production of Puccini’s “Tosca.” After months of legal wrangling over the fate of the New York City Opera, which filed for bankruptcy protection in late 2013, a group called NYCO Renaissance won approval for its plan to reorganize the company. It began the effort Wednesday night with the opening of a six-performance run of “Tosca” at the Rose Theater at Jazz at Lincoln Center.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22RENAISSANCE1/22RENAISSANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22RENAISSANCE1/22RENAISSANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22RENAISSANCE1/22RENAISSANCE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'