tra-large knits and coats with long, trailing sleeves. But perhaps the most practical interpretation of volume is evident in slouchy pants — which this season have been cut wide through the legs. At Rick Owens, the baggy style (complete with cargo pockets) resembled that of a ’90s raver. Christophe Lemaire deftly balanced his creased-front trousers with tailored coats, while Dries Van Noten paired a double-breasted blazer with generous trousers. And at Gosha Rubchinskiy, sweatpants — worn high, à la Al Bundy — came with a tucked in T-shirt and military shirt. Finally, we may just see the demise of the bare ankle in 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-threes-01/21tmag-threes-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-threes-01/21tmag-threes-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-threes-01/21tmag-threes-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-threes-01/21tmag-threes-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-threes-01/21tmag-threes-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/21/t-magazine/21tmag-threes-01/21tmag-threes-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail