ted States, citing one report of the handle breaking and a baby being injured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Britax Child Safety is recalling about 71,000 child car seats in the United States because the carrying handle may break, allowing the infant carrier to be dropped, the company reported on Thursday in a regulatory filing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britax Car Seats Recalled After Handle Breaks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Car Seats for Infants Are Recalled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Britax Child Safety Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Car Seats', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-21T22:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc7769fd-1823-52ec-87ea-9b855c1ed5a2', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc7769fd-1823-52ec-87ea-9b855c1ed5a2'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Wheeldon’s take on Shakespeare’s play, a co-production of the Royal Ballet and the National Ballet of Canada, comes to the Kennedy Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/arts/dance/review-dark-suspicions-in-jumps-and-gestures-in-the-winters-tale.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Wheeldon’s take on Shakespeare’s play, a co-production of the Royal Ballet and the National Ballet of Canada, comes to the Kennedy Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Christopher Wheeldon’s “The Winter’s Tale” — the first ballet to dramatize that Shakespeare play — achieves an extraordinary amount. Movingly, over three acts, it takes us on a great arc of emotion and experience, capturing the play’s themes of death and regeneration, hostility and reconciliation. When it takes liberties with aspects of the story, it does so persuasively. Its five leading roles — three for women, two for men — are marvelously distinct, while never seeming like copies of other roles in the repertory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22WHELDON/22WHELDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22WHELDON/22WHELDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22WHELDON/22WHELDON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22WHELDON/22WHELDON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22WHELDON/22WHELDON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22WHELDON/22WHELDON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight