5edf7'}, {'abstract': 'Exquisitely drafted playing cards from the 15th and 16th centuries — most of them from Germany — are on display at the Cloisters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/arts/design/with-these-cards-every-hands-a-winner.html', 'snippet': 'Exquisitely drafted playing cards from the 15th and 16th centuries — most of them from Germany — are on display at the Cloisters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PICK up a deck of cards. Shuffle, cut, deal. Now, take a look at your hand. It may be a winner or a loser. That’s up to chance. But it is a dead certainty that the visual spectacle will be dull. Diamonds, clubs, spades and hearts are the same from deck to deck, printed uniformly. The king, queen and jack wear more or less the same costume. Boring.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22PLAYING1/22PLAYING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 945, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22PLAYING1/22PLAYING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 945}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22PLAYING1/22PLAYING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22PLAYING1/22PLAYING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1949, 'width': 1238, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22PLAYING1/22PLAYING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/22/ar