ks, from the traditional to the modern to the odd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is still a divide in the contemporary art world’s recent embrace of ceramics and glass. You will find, for the most part, many traditional wares at the New York Ceramics and Glass Fair, now in its 17th incarnation. And yet, among 30 vendors, there is a great range of work here, from sophisticated haut-craft and modernist vessels to objects that will please the seeker of oddities. There are also a handful of lectures with juicy titles like “Demolition Man: Peter Voulkos, 1950-1970” and “Ming Goes Bling and the Slightly Satirical Aroma of Eucalyptus.” Here are some highlights.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22CERAMICS1/22CERAMICS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22CERAMICS1/22CERAMICS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 493}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22CERAMICS1/22CERAMICS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22CERAMICS1/22CERAMICS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1684, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22CERAMICS1/22CERAMICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/22CERAMICS1/22CERAMICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':