 'lead_paragraph': 'The lack of female African-American dancers in ballet companies is a subject that both frustrates and galvanizes Denise Saunders Thompson, the chairwoman and executive director of the International Association of Blacks in Dance, an organization that’s been around for 25 years.  On Sunday, in conjunction with the association’s annual conference in Denver, Ms. Thompson is holding auditions  for minority women seeking contracts with American companies — the group’s first such event. Ballet Memphis, Pennsylvania Ballet, San Francisco Ballet and Washington Ballet, among others, are sending representatives. Training institutions, including the Pacific Northwest Ballet School and the School of American Ballet, will also attend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/23AUDITION/23AUDITION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/23AUDITION/23AUDITION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/23AUDITION/23AUDITION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/23AUDITION/23AUDITION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/arts/23AUDITION/23AUDITION-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance to Dance for Minority Ballerinas', 'kicker': None, 