e/4d14767b-2314-5084-bd3c-10210d312421'}, {'abstract': 'The two countries are digging in for a battle that will continue regardless of any peace deal: the fight against the Islamic State extremist group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/world/middleeast/russia-and-us-while-pushing-for-peace-talks-jockey-for-position-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The two countries are digging in for a battle that will continue regardless of any peace deal: the fight against the Islamic State extremist group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The Russian military is expanding its footprint in Syria, setting up operations at an airfield in a northeastern, mostly Kurdish province across the country from its main coastal base. In an adjacent province, locals say the United States is intensifying its aid to Kurdish militias, even taking over a small agricultural airport; Pentagon officials denied this. And some Syrian fighters say Russia has reached out to Sunni tribes, offering to help them fight the Islamic State extremist group in the east after similar American efforts failed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia and U.S., While Pushing for Peace Talks, Jockey for Position in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia and U.S., While Pushing Peace Talks, Compete for Allies in Syria ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 