rders was among the casualties.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Multiple airstrikes on a town in northern Yemen on Thursday killed at least 18 people, including civilian rescuers and an ambulance driver working at a hospital supported by Doctors Without Borders, according to a statement by the group and the hospital director. At least three hospitals supported by Doctors Without Borders have been destroyed or damaged since October in the war between Houthi rebels and government forces backed by Saudi Arabia. Muhammed Hajr, the director of the Jumhuriya Hospital in Saada Province, said that the ambulance had just picked up people wounded in an airstrike in the Dhayan district when another airstrike destroyed the ambulance, killing everyone inside. Other airstrikes killed at least 12 people who arrived to help, Mr. Hajr said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen: Airstrikes Kill 18, Including a Hospital Worker', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Yemen: Airstrikes Kill 18, Including a Hospital Worker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almosawa, Shuaib', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T02:34:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shuaib Almosawa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shuaib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almosawa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c61446e-e25f-5fb0-b7e4-ae335612db49', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c61446e-e25f-5fb0-b7e4-ae335612db49'}, {'abstract': 'J.T. Miller, the Rangers’ first-round draft pick in 2011, has been “more assertive and more physical” this season. He has 10 goals and 12 assists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/sports/hockey/at-22-rangers-forward-is-already-having-a-signature-season.html', 'snippet': 'J.T. Miller, the Rangers’ first-round draft pick in 2011, has been “more assertive and more physical” this season. He has 10 goals and 12 assists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. — J. T. Miller may be only 22, but he has already had a wealth of experience with the Rangers, who made him a first-round draft pick in 2011.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/sports/22-Y-RANGERS/22-Y-RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/sports/22-Y-RANGERS/22-Y-RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/sports/22-Y-RANGERS/22-Y-RANGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/sports/22-Y-RANGERS/22-Y-RANGERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1580, 'width': 1137, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/sport