t pay fines or participate in a blood drive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/us/alabama-judge-censured-for-coercing-blood-donors.html', 'snippet': 'A Circuit Court judge was censured Thursday after he was accused last year of threatening defendants with jail time if they did not pay fines or participate in a blood drive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Circuit Court judge was censured Thursday after he was accused last year of threatening defendants with jail time if they did not pay fines or participate in a blood drive. Judge Marvin Wiggins, whose jurisdiction includes five impoverished counties, accepted the punishment as part of a settlement with the State Judicial Inquiry Commission. More than 40 defendants donated blood after Judge Wiggins told them, “Consider that as a discount rather than putting you in jail, if you do not have any money.” The judge’s supporters said he had chosen his words poorly and that he did not intend to jail anyone, but critics like the state commission said his comments “were so coercive as to be reprehensible and inexcusable.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama: Judge Censured for Coercing Blood Donors', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama: Judge Censured for Coercing Blood Donors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood Donation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiggins, Marvin (Judge)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T04:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'fi