e': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14ed713a-3f13-5130-8fd8-70d7087bf07c', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14ed713a-3f13-5130-8fd8-70d7087bf07c'}, {'abstract': 'Victor Dragonetti’s street scenes are colorful, and complex, with an air of mystery that evokes different responses from viewers.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/magic-and-mystery-on-sao-paulos-streets/', 'snippet': 'Victor Dragonetti’s street scenes are colorful, and complex, with an air of mystery that evokes different responses from viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you ever get cynical about photography, go talk to Victor Dragonetti. O.K., just going to where he lives – São Paulo – will lift anyone’s spirits given the weather in the Northeast. But this young photographer’s enthusiasm about photography is not just heartwarming, but also infectious. His smile is enough to remind you of the moment when you realized that taking pictures was magical.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Magic and Mystery on São Paulo’s Streets', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dragonetti, Victor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sao Paulo (Brazil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T08:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c515eb1-0373-521e-83d9-44877602aa27', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c515eb1-0373-521e-83d9-44877602aa27'}, {'abstract': 'The prime minister brings his youthful appeal and optimistic messages to the World Economic Forum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/business/dealbook/justin-trudeau-carries-his-look-to-canada-image-to-davos.html', 'snippet': 'The prime minister brings his youthful appeal and optimistic messages to the World Economic Forum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — The Davos man who attends the World Economic Forum here each year is a member of the global elite — say, a banker or a politician — whose status is reinforced by an exclusive white badge that gives him access to V.I.P. lounges away from the masses at this alpine resort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/business/db-davosjustin-web1/db-davosjustin-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/business/db-davosjustin-web1/db-davosjustin-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/business/db-davosjustin-web1/db-davosjustin-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/business/db-davosjustin-web1/db-davosjustin-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1520, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/busine