nt': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cff6892c-18c1-5000-a43c-6ad074a35967'}, {'abstract': 'The philosopher and author of “The Rebel” recognized that killing was, at times, unavoidable.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/making-peace-with-violence/', 'snippet': 'The philosopher and author of “The Rebel” recognized that killing was, at times, unavoidable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixty years ago today, Albert Camus gave the speech of his life. It was a speech, in fact, that nearly cost him his life, as well as one that failed in its goal of saving the lives of countless civilians, Arabs and French alike, caught in the vise of terrorism employed by both sides in Algeria’s war of independence. The reasoning behind the speech, as well as the reasons Camus gave it, cast important light on the “war on terror” now being fought in the West.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21stoneWeb1/21stoneWeb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21stoneWeb1/21stoneWeb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21stoneWeb1/21stoneWeb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21stoneWeb1/21stoneWeb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/opinion/21stoneWeb1/21stoneWeb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 