ging thoughts and sexual wanderings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/books/review/this-should-be-written-in-the-present-tense-by-helle-helle.html', 'snippet': 'A novel tracks a young woman’s ranging thoughts and sexual wanderings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last 20 years, Helle Helle’s novels and short stories have made her a star in her native Denmark, where she regularly receives awards and acclaim. Denmark is also where, according to her biography, Helle “lives in a forest.” What a fittingly magical dwelling for Helle, who — judging from her first novel to be translated into English, “This Should Be \xadWritten in the Present Tense” — has enchanting gifts as a storyteller.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘This Should Be Written in the Present Tense,’ by Helle Helle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Danish Girl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Helle, Helle (1965- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aitken, Martin (Translator)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'This Should Be Written in the Present Tense (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T09:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Russell Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': 'Russell', 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/86e11f33-edf8-5c63-9408-36ef45f3d065', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86e11f33-edf8-5c63-9408-36ef45f3d065'}, {'abstract': 'As government’s role has grown, power has increasingly shifted from the states to the federal domain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/books/review/liberty-and-coercion-by-gary-gerstle.html', 'snippet': 'As government’s role has grown, power has increasingly shifted from the states to the federal domain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between 1913 and 1920, Americans amended the federal Constitution four times. Each amendment solidified a major reform: the direct election of senators, the first federal income tax, votes for women, the banning of alcohol nationwide. Taken together, they reflected the progressive view that the Constitution was a living document, able to be adapted to and updated for the nation’s needs. A century ago, most Americans seemed to agree that new circumstances required new tools, and that the federal government would have a key role to play in meeting the challenges of the modern age.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24GAGE/0124-BKS-Gage-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24GAGE/0124-BKS-Gage-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 573}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24GAGE/0124-BKS-Gage-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 978, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24GAGE/0124-BKS-Gage-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24GAGE/24GA