e three Americans who flew there from Iran on Sunday to return home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Rezaian, the Washington Post reporter who was among the American citizens freed by Iran last weekend in a prisoner deal, left an American military hospital in Germany on Friday bound for the United States, accompanied by his wife and mother aboard his boss’s personal jetliner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1796, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/world/REZAIAN/REZAIAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jason Rezaian Travels to U.S. on Washington Post Owner’s Plane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freed Reporter Returns to U.S. on Boss&#8217;s Private Jet ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rezaian, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T12:35:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/060186c7-4bab-5342-a4e0-158bb4b54cbb', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/060186c7-4bab-5342-a4e0-158bb4b54cbb'}, {'abstract': 'It’s called “research rapture” — the moment you slip the bonds of the present and follow a detail into the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/books/review/under-no-certain-search-terms.html', 'snippet': 'It’s called “research rapture” — the moment you slip the bonds of the present and follow a detail into the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’re writing a book based on archival research and you have two children who come home from school at 3, no matter how much you love libraries, you become grateful for Google. For three years, I sat down most mornings at my dining room table in my slippers and read newspapers printed in the 1870s. No need to travel to distant archives, or spend fruitless hours turning the wrong pages. I could open a browser, punch in a range of dates and a few search terms, and within seconds have a presorted queue of articles, every one of which was relevant. I could feel confident that when it came to coverage of, let’s say, an embassy of Japanese statesmen arriving in San Francisco in 1872, I hadn’t missed a single mention. I blessed the librarians who had digitized their holdings, and got to work.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 468, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 936, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/books/review/24AUTHORSNOTE/0124-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Under No Certain Search Terms ', 'kicker': 'Author’s No