9-b384-5ba2-bcb2-7daee77f5344'}, {'abstract': 'The gilded bronze Baptistery doors with their 28 panels have been replaced with a replicas made by a team of artisans using the materials and techniques mastered centuries ago in a Renaissance workshop.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/22/replicas-of-ghiberti-doors-to-be-unveiled-in-florence/', 'snippet': 'The gilded bronze Baptistery doors with their 28 panels have been replaced with a replicas made by a team of artisans using the materials and techniques mastered centuries ago in a Renaissance workshop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — For nearly 600 years, Lorenzo Ghiberti’s panels depicting scenes from the life of Christ on the north doors of the Baptistery in Florence were exposed to the elements and other vicissitudes of time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Replicas of Ghiberti Doors to Be Unveiled in Florence', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T14:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8936f5ba-aad3-5169-9a11-38c51d11658e', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8936f5ba-aad3-5169-9a11-38c51d11658e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Page is hardly the first Silicon Valley chief with a case of intellectual wanderlust, but to a rare degree he has made his company a reflection of his personal fascinations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/technology/larry-page-google-founder-is-still-innovator-in-chief.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Page is hardly the first Silicon Valley chief with a case of intellectual wanderlust, but to a rare degree he has made his company a reflection of his personal fascinations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years ago, Charles Chase, an engineer who manages Lockheed Martin’s nuclear fusion program, was sitting on a white leather couch at Google’s Solve for X conference when a man he had never met knelt down to talk to him.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/business/24page-illo-web1/24page-illo-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Larry Page’s Obsessions Became Google’s Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Innovator in Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alphabet Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T14:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conor Dougherty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Conor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dougherty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e0de331-00b9-561f-a6d8-83dc9c228a8b', 'word_count': 2497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e0de331-00b9-561f-a6d8-83dc9c228a8b'}, {'abstract': 'The program includes Ethan and Joel Coen’s “Fargo,” “Raising Arizona” and “No Country for Old Men,” as well as their newest, “Hail, Caesar!”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/movies/film-forum-presents-a-15-film-coen-brothers-retrospective.html', 'snippet': 'The program includes Ethan and Joel Coen’s “Fargo,” “Raising Arizona” and “No Country for Old Men,” as well as their newest, “Hail, Caesar!”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s high time. On the eve of their latest opus, the sibling writers-directors Ethan and Joel Coen are receiving a 15-film retrospective at Film Forum, encompassing their first feature, the neo-noir “Blood Simple” (1984), and their new “Hail, Caesar!,” a satire of studio-system Hollywood, on Feb. 4 (it opens in other theater