ure might also limit Congress’s own ability to require the government to embrace good governance values.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/23/business/dealbook/the-price-of-requiring-regulators-to-do-more-cost-benefit-analysis.html', 'snippet': 'A proposed measure might also limit Congress’s own ability to require the government to embrace good governance values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bipartisan, if mildly conservative, group of senators has indicated that it will introduce legislation intended to increase the rule-making requirements on Wall Street regulators like the Securities and Exchange Commission and the Consumer Financial Protection Board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Price of Requiring Regulators to Do More Cost-Benefit Analysis', 'kicker': 'Another View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T16:48:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Zaring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60eb9d94-f2a5-5712-9220-9e1b1a14acc5', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60eb9d94-f2a5-5712-9220-9e1b1a14acc5'}, {'abstract': 'Donald J. Trump has regained momentum in Iowa two weeks before the state’s caucuses, and many voters cite his bravado and willingness to assail political correctness, more than his policy proposals, as the main reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/22/donald-trump-challenging-political-correctness-strikes-a-chord/', 'snippet': 'Donald J. Trump has regained momentum in Iowa two weeks before the state’s caucuses, and many voters cite his bravado and willingness to assail political correctness, more than his policy proposals, as the main reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a rally in Iowa this week, Donald J. Trump explained in bold terms and broad brush strokes the many ways he would improve the United States as president: building a wall, rebuilding the military, beating China on trade. When a protester chimed in to question how the Republican would do the things that he promised, Mr. Trump decided that instead of removing the man from the audience, he would respond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/us/22firstdraft-Trump2/22firstdraft-Trump2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/22/us/22firstdraft-Trump2/22firstdraft-Trump2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/us/22firstdraft-Trump2/22firstdraft-Trump2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/22/us/22firstdraft-Trump2/22firstdraft-Trump2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1307, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio