d Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T17:52:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By William D. Cohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/268f2b78-223e-55df-b393-d9973c2ad611', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/268f2b78-223e-55df-b393-d9973c2ad611'}, {'abstract': 'Ezra Nawi has become a symbol in the battle between advocacy groups on opposite sides of Israel’s political spectrum, and the debate over the nature of Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/23/world/middleeast/arrest-of-leftist-israeli-activist-ezra-nawi-underlines-political-split.html', 'snippet': 'Ezra Nawi has become a symbol in the battle between advocacy groups on opposite sides of Israel’s political spectrum, and the debate over the nature of Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Ezra Nawi, an Israeli Jewish plumber, has a long history as a left-wing activist helping Palestinians in their struggle against Israel’s occupation of the West Bank. Now he is under arrest in Israel, after a right-wing activist surreptitiously filmed him bragging about exposing Arab brokers who tried to sell Palestinian land to Jewish settlers. Such sales are a capital crime under Palestinian law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/world/23ISRAEL/23