 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffed062e-b1e1-592f-a9df-03079bb037b4', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffed062e-b1e1-592f-a9df-03079bb037b4'}, {'abstract': 'A Pennsylvania appeals court dismissed some serious criminal charges against three administrators over their handling of the Sandusky child molestation scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/23/sports/ncaafootball/some-charges-against-former-penn-state-officials-thrown-out.html', 'snippet': 'A Pennsylvania appeals court dismissed some serious criminal charges against three administrators over their handling of the Sandusky child molestation scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pennsylvania appeals court on Friday threw out some of the more serious criminal charges against three high-ranking former Penn State administrators whose handling of the Jerry Sandusky child molestation scandal continues to be a flash point for the state’s flagship university.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Charges Against Former Penn State Officials Thrown Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Several Charges Dropped Against Former Officials in Penn State Abuse Case ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spanier, Graham B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schultz, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curley, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T19:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0a9bb2-5785-5cc7-83c6-e8bc1f5cff51', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0a9bb2-5785-5cc7-83c6-e8bc1f5cff51'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Rowley unwinds by doing “extreme activities” — working out, go-kart racing, sledding — with her husband and their two daughters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/nyregion/how-cynthia-rowley-fashion-designer-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Rowley unwinds by doing “extreme activities” — working out, go-kart racing, sledding — with her husband and their two daughters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To judge from the society pages, the fashion designer Cynthia Rowley and her husband, Bill Powers, seem to be out on the town six days a week. But on the seventh day, the couple downshifts (slightly) into the rhythms of family life. Which is to say, “We do extreme activities,” said Ms. Rowley, 57, for whom family means her husband, a 48-year-old writer and art dealer, and two school-age daughters, Kit and Gigi. If your idea of unwinding is racing go-karts or singing Iggy Pop songs, then let them be your relaxation counselors. If not, try to hang on until the rocket returns to home base, a house in the West Village.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE3/24ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei