ed from the Superman myth is that the Man of Steel has a mild-mannered alter ego, Clark Kent, who few suspect has any connection to that heroic crusader. A similar relationship exists between the drag actor, singer and pianist John Epperson and his brilliant, brassy creation Lypsinka, one of the greatest creatures to emerge from the New York club scene.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: John Epperson Steps Out, Leaving the Diva at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaving the Diva at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Feinstein's/54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Music Venue)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epperson, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T23:05:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee3c96c7-82b1-55b3-93ce-d95a6caf9bd6', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee3c96c7-82b1-55b3-93ce-d95a6caf9bd6'}, {'abstract': 'The cat family doesn’t change its colors but the fashion world is in a playful mood with one of its most popular patterns: the leopard print.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/fashion/bill-cunningham-spotted.html', 'snippet': 'The cat family doesn’t change its colors but the fashion world is in a playful mood with one of its most popular patterns: the leopard print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cat family doesn’t change its colorsbut the fashion world is in a playful mood with one of its most popular patterns: the leopard print. It’s intriguing to see all the variations of black and gray, some of them with an overlay of subtle color. One wearer highlighted her coat with creative details, such as a gold-bronze envelope bag; a necklace that blended with the coat, and a color cast of pale pink and aqua; and leopard-print fingerless gloves. Perhaps surprisingly, this fashion lover works in investment banking; her personal style of dress is her hobby.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Spotted', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spotted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coats and Jackets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T23:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c3a6f40-40ae-55d1-8b9d-8b4b25228fc5', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c3a6f40-40ae-55d1-8b9d-8b4b25228fc5'}, {'abstract': 'A loose interpretation of Sophocles that features a live pig, this show at New York Live Arts in Chelsea also includes “Elektra Cabaret.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/23/arts/dance/review-elektra-runs-wild-with-ann-liv-young.html', 'snippet': 'A loose interpretation of Sophocles that features a live pig, this show at New York Live Arts in Chelsea also includes “Elektra Cabaret.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to imagine Ann Liv Young and company doing what they did on Wednesday night more than once, let alone eight times, the length of their run at New York Live Arts in Chelsea. The brutal rawness and immediacy that we’ve come to expect from Ms. Young, a divisive performer and choreographer, reaches new heights — or newly disturbing depths — in her “Elektra,” which had its United States premiere alongside its even rowdier companion piece, “Elektra Cabaret.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/arts/23ELEKTRA/23ELEKTRA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Elektra’ Runs Wild, With Ann Liv Young', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Performers Have It Tough; the Pig Has It Easy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Elektra (Dance)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Ann Liv', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-22T23:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a36030d-e0c5-54ec-9b4c-35871710211c', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a36030d-e0c5-54ec-9b4c-35871710211c'}, {'abstract': 'Presented at Montclair State University, this piece by the Dutch composer Michel van der Aa adapts a hard-to-classify work by the Portuguese writer Fernando Pessoa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/23/arts/music/review-the-book-of-disquiet-opera-as-one-man-with-films.html', 'snippet': 'Presented at Montclair State University, this piece by the Dutch composer Michel van der Aa adapts a hard-to-classify work by the Portuguese writer Fernando Pessoa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTCLAIR, N.J. — O.K., opera lovers, try this one on for size: No one sings live. The only two vocal numbers are rendered on film by a Portuguese fado singer. The lone figure onstage, apart from the small orchestra, speaks throughout. The drama is all internal and mostly philosophical.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'