onn-undaunted-by-uneven-start-its-not-march-yet.html', 'snippet': 'The Huskies, 13-5 with a key matchup with Georgetown looming, won the national championship in 2014 after an indifferent regular season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STORRS, Conn. — In the $40 million basketball practice center at UConn, there are subtle and more obvious reminders of the Huskies’ most recent men’s basketball glory: a giant banner commemorating the 2014 national championship team, and the folding chairs scattered throughout the gym taken from that year’s Final Four.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/sports/23UCONNweb1/23UCONNweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'UConn Undaunted by Uneven Start (It’s Not March Yet)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'UConn Undaunted by Uneven Start (It&#8217;s Not March Yet)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Seth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ollie, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-23T01:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44be986a-87a2-5087-9e01-94a67b8df2b5', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44be986a-87a2-5087-9e01-94a67b8df2b5'}, {'abstract': 'The Litvinenko killing was old school. Russia is now relying on character assassination online to attack opponents with impunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/23/opinion/who-needs-assassins-when-youve-got-hackers.html', 'snippet': 'The Litvinenko killing was old school. Russia is now relying on character assassination online to attack opponents with impunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moscow — A BRITISH inquiry announced this week that Alexander V. Litvinenko, a Russian security officer turned defector who died in a London hospital of polonium poisoning in 2006, was “probably” murdered on the instructions of President Vladimir V. Putin. That’s little surprise. For more than eight years the world ha