nt_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-23T07:08:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/edaafc1b-cedc-53fb-8c97-7887eb579f7e', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edaafc1b-cedc-53fb-8c97-7887eb579f7e'}, {'abstract': 'Creditors blamed the Puerto Rican utility for the failure late Friday of talks to restructure about $9 billion worth of its debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/business/dealbook/puerto-rico-debt-talks-collapse.html', 'snippet': 'Creditors blamed the Puerto Rican utility for the failure late Friday of talks to restructure about $9 billion worth of its debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN JUAN, Puerto Rico — Negotiations to restructure roughly $9 billion of the debt of Puerto Rico’s power company collapsed late Friday, according to a statement from a group of creditors involved in the talks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talks to Restructure Puerto Rico Power Company’s Debt Collapse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico Electric Power Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-23T07:50:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dealbook', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec98541a-77d3-5401-9c24-76b7fe2159ec', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec98541a-77d3-5401-9c24-76b7fe2159ec'}, {'abstract': 'A Neolithic community buried its members in layers. Those on top died unhappily, it appears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/science/in-an-ancient-tomb-a-hierarchy-of-the-dead.html', 'snippet': 'A Neolithic community buried its members in layers. Those on top died unhappily, it appears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 6,000-year-old tomb in Northern Spain provides valuable information about an ancient Neolithic community, according to a new study in the journal PLOS One. The tomb holds the remains of 47 individuals, laid to rest in several layers. Individuals in the bottom tomb were closely related, and family members were buried side-by-side, DNA analysis suggests. In layers above, however, the bodies appear to be missing skeletal parts, including skulls. The bones were manipulated, possibly for ritualistic purposes. . The analysis also showed that the community relied on cereals and other plant-based food for sustenance.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1514, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/23/science/26obs-tomb/26obs-tomb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In an Ancient Tomb, a Hierarchy of the Dead', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Archaeology: A Hierarchy of Death in an Ancient Tomb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tombs and Tombstones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY AND ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PLoS One (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-23T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/908b158d-6313-5e33-9277-f39a55910db7', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/908b158d-6313-5e33-9277-f39a55910db7'}, {'abstract': 'Marie Kondo, sparking yet more joy as she tours for her new book on “compassionate organizing.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/fashion/marie-kondo-spark-joy.html', 'snippet': 'Marie Kondo, sparking yet more joy as she tours for her new book on “compassionate organizing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday evening, the tidy and the would-be tidy sat very still on the fourth floor of the Barnes & Noble bookstore at Union Square in Manhattan, craning to hear the soft voice of Marie Kondo, the Japanese author of “The Life-Changing Magic of Tidying Up,” as she demonstrated her folding technique on ever more complex garments. She was balletic and masterly. When done, Ms. Kondo received a standing ovation.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/fashion/24KONDO/24KONDO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/24/fashion/24KONDO/24KONDO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/fashion/24KONDO/24KONDO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/fashion/24KONDO/24KONDO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 1931, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/24/fashion/24KONDO/24KONDO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/24/fashion/24KONDO/24KONDO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credi