itics/republicans-risk-repeating-mistake-on-hispanic-vote.html', 'snippet': 'Demographic trends and the outcome of the 2012 presidential election don’t bode well for a Republican approach highlighting hostility to immigration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years ago, high-level Republicans declared that after losing the popular vote in five of the past six presidential elections, the party needed to appeal more to Latinos to win the White House. Immigration was a threshold issue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Risk Repeating Mistake on Hispanic Vote', 'kicker': 'Letter From Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-24T17:45:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Albert R. Hunt | Bloomberg View', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Albert', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/637274c8-1d3a-5ab7-af34-eed984302caf', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/637274c8-1d3a-5ab7-af34-eed984302caf'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Indira Gandhi becomes prime minister of India in 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/24/1966-indira-gandhi-becomes-prime-minister/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Indira Gandhi becomes prime minister of India in 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Mrs. Indira Gandhi was sworn in today [Jan. 24] as India’s third prime minister and the first woman to lead the nation’s millions. The 48-year-old daughter of India’s first prime minister, Jawaharlal Nehru, took the brief oath before turbaned President Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan in the same room where he administered the same oath 19 months earlier to Lal Bahadur Shastri. Fifteen other cabinet ministers were sworn in at the same time by Mr. Radhakrishnan, including Gulzarilal Nanda, home minister; Y. B. Chavan, defense; Chidambaram Subramaniam, food; and the Untouchables leader, Jagjivan Ram, labor and employment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Indira Gandhi Becomes Prime Minister', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Indira', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-24T17:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/160026b3-c905-53e1-957a-4ad5c1298220', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/160026b3-c905-53e1-957a-4ad5c1298220'}, {'abstract': 'Peyton Manning and the Denver Broncos knocked off Tom Brady and the defending champion New England Patriots in the A.F.C