e': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardephe, Paul G', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qian, Pei-Shen', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-24T22:47:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley and Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/810076c3-893e-5ad7-8f9a-4576990ae06d', 'word_count': 1414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/810076c3-893e-5ad7-8f9a-4576990ae06d'}, {'abstract': 'As the price keeps rising for the Joint Strike Fighter, the world’s costliest weapon, the program has raised questions of whether it will ever be ready, or effective.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/25/us/despite-decades-of-stealth-sticking-points-bedevil-f-35-jet.html', 'snippet': 'As the price keeps rising for the Joint Strike Fighter, the world’s costliest weapon, the program has raised questions of whether it will ever be ready, or effective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the earliest stealth weapons on record was a stone used by the young Israelite David to kill the Philistine giant Goliath. In the biblical account, David shunned the conventional armaments of his time: sword, helmet, armor. Instead, he went forth with a slingshot and a few stones, kept undetected in a pouch. As any schoolchild knows, one well-aimed fling was all it took to put Goliath down for good. The big guy never saw it coming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Decades of Stealth, Sticking Points Bedevil F-35 Jet', 'kicker': 'Retro Report', 'content_kicker': None, 