thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/21/blogs/20160121-lens-crewdson-slide-EFN5/20160121-lens-crewdson-slide-EFN5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alone, in a Crowd, With Gregory Crewdson', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T07:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/87c4600a-f821-5734-8c93-1adce34d8f00', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/87c4600a-f821-5734-8c93-1adce34d8f00'}, {'abstract': 'Gregory Crewdson’s photographs almost always project solitude and intimacy, even if his images take a team to organize. The subject of one of his images looks back at the experience.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/25/alone-in-a-crowd-with-gregory-crewdson/', 'snippet': 'Gregory Crewdson’s photographs almost always project solitude and intimacy, even if his images take a team to organize. The subject of one of his images looks back at the experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One push through a revolving door and I was in complete darkness. I walked to the right to get a sheet of resin-coated paper and then turned toward the enlarger, where I could finally rest my mind. The most sacred moments were when I could just stand there and dissolve into the test prints. There were no New York hospitals, no expectations of my father’s recovery or death. Not even the constant companion of intensive care beeping sounds, those Montefiore monitors I couldn’t get out of my head.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alone, in a Crowd, With Gregory Crewdson', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head