ue': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T17:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4a91fc6-a13f-555e-a722-5290620069de', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4a91fc6-a13f-555e-a722-5290620069de'}, {'abstract': 'Also, peppery watercress; a halvah makeover in Chelsea Market; treats from a chocolate lab; da Vinci’s diet; and online lessons from Wolfgang Puck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/27/dining/vincent-price-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'Also, peppery watercress; a halvah makeover in Chelsea Market; treats from a chocolate lab; da Vinci’s diet; and online lessons from Wolfgang Puck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1965, Vincent Price, the actor and connoisseur of art and food, wrote a cookbook with his wife, Mary, featuring recipes from restaurants in destinations including New York, California, France, Italy and England. The book became a collector’s item; now a 50th-anniversary edition has been published with the help of the Prices’ daughter, Victoria, who has written the preface. The Proust in all of us will relish the profiles of ghosts like Le Pavillon and the Forum of the Twelve Caesars in New York, the original La Pyramide in France and Bali in Amsterdam. Reproductions of menus, with prices like $3.25 for Lüchow’s Wiener schnitzel and $5.95 for roast duck at the Four Seasons (soon to be another fond memory) will give you pause. There are well-detailed, pre-food-processor recipes, including an unapologetic quiche Lorraine calling for eight egg yolks: “A Treasury of Great Recipes: 50th Anniversary Edition” (Dover, $50).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 811}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1515, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/dining/27BURNER6/27BURNER6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vincent Price’s Cookbook Lives On', 'kicker'