dependent analysis of the trade deal suggested that displacement of workers in industries most vulnerable to competition would be relatively small.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A far-reaching trade pact binding a dozen Pacific Rim nations would increase incomes, exports and growth in the United States but is unlikely to add to overall employment, according to an independent analysis released Monday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26trade-web/26trade-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trans-Pacific Trade Pact Would Lift U.S. Incomes, but Not Jobs Overall, Study Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wide-Ranging Trade Pact Would Lift American Incomes, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calmes, Jackie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Pacific Partnership', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peterson, Peter G, Institute for International Economics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T17:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32dc56c9-0823-59a5-9374-52910ac44f78', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32dc56c9-0823-59a5-9374-52910ac44f78'}, {'abstract': 'The justice ruled that the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission could encourage electricity users to adopt “demand response” programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/business/energy-environment/supreme-court-upholds-a-federal-approach-to-power-pricing.html', 'snippet': 'The justice ruled that the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission could encourage electricity users to adopt “demand response” programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court on Monday ruled that federal regulators may encourage electricity users like schools, hospitals and shopping centers to reduce consumption at peak times in exchange for price breaks. The regulatory approach, known as “demand response,” lowers costs for consumers and lessens the risk of system failures that can cause blackouts.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Upholds Efforts on Managing Electricity Use Through Pricing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Upholds Efforts on Managing Electricity Use Through Pricing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Energy Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T17:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/211c000b-e3cd-5f11-ac2e-10d1bf11c960', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/211c000b-e3cd-5f11-ac2e-10d1bf11c960'}, {'abstract': 'A lawsuit was filed Jan. 15 in a Swiss regional court over the work, once owned by Anna Jaffé, a childless British expatriate whose belongings were seized a year after she died and auctioned off in July 1943 in Nice, France.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/25/jewish-heirs-sue-swiss-museum-to-recover-constable-painting/', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit was filed Jan. 15 in a Swiss regional court over the work, once owned by Anna Jaffé, a childless British expatriate whose belongings were seized a year after she died and auctioned off in July 1943 in Nice, France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Jewish descendants of the owner of a John Constable landscape have sued to reclaim the painting from a regional Swiss museum where it hangs now with a note acknowledging that it was illegally seized during World War II. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jewish Heirs Sue Swiss Museum to Recover Constable Painting', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawsuit Is Filed Over Painting Seized in War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Constable, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaffe, Anna', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monteagle, Alain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T17:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/440bd535-9d61-5c29-8a35-77d76ab42680', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/440bd535-9d61-5c29-8a35-77d76ab42680'}, {'abstract': 'Marco Rubio has a carefully curated campaign playlist, one tailored to the conservative voters he is trying to reach in states like Iowa, that includes some modern Christian rock — a list somewhat different from his personal musical tastes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/25/marco-rubios-campaign-playlist-is-more-mercyme-than-minaj/', 'snippet': 'Marco Rubio has a carefully curated campaign playlist, one tailored to the conservative voters he is trying to reach in states like Iowa, that includes some modern Christian rock — a list somewhat different from his personal musical tastes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Marco Rubio’s musical tastes run toward electronic dance music, Nicki Minaj and rap. But don’t expect to hear them playing over the speakers at his campaign rallies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/25/us/25firstdraft-rubio1/25firstdraft-rubio1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/25/us/25firstdraft-rubio1/25firstdraft-rubio1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/25/us/25firstdraft-rubio1/25firstdraft-rubio1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/25/us/25firstdraft-rubio1/25firstdraft-rubio1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/25/us/25firstdraft-rubio1/25firstdraft-rubio1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thu