ops-billboard-chart/', 'snippet': 'Panic! At the Disco achieves the relatively rare feat these days of topping the Billboard chart with a rock album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not often that a rock album tops the Billboard album chart, but Panic! At the Disco did it this week with its new release, “Death of a Bachelor” (Fueled by Ramen/DCD2), which sold 169,000 copies and had 17 million streams, according to Nielsen. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock Is Back as Panic! At the Disco Tops Billboard Chart', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rock Is Back at No. 1', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adele (Singer)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowie, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T20:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcb42341-aa85-5fae-91b3-4e1507dcb4ac', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcb42341-aa85-5fae-91b3-4e1507dcb4ac'}, {'abstract': 'A new hotel brand, Tru by Hilton, will attempt to be the first design-forward hotel chain in the midscale category where rooms start at $80.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/25/travel/tru-hilton-hotels-millennials.html', 'snippet': 'A new hotel brand, Tru by Hilton, will attempt to be the first design-forward hotel chain in the midscale category where rooms start at $8