t Monmouth University poll asked respondents which caused more problems\xa0in the federal government: elected officials’ failure to compromise, or their failure to stand by their principles. Sixty-eight percent of Democrats said lack of compromise was the bigger problem, while 25 percent chose failure to stand on principle. Among Republicans, meanwhile,\xa054 percent said failure to stand on principle was the bigger issue, and just 36 percent picked lack of compromise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: What Democrats and Republicans Want From Politicians', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monmouth University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T21:12:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78c51ccb-ced9-5c57-9dd7-27250ab3aeba', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78c51ccb-ced9-5c57-9dd7-27250ab3aeba'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Clinton shifted from attacking Mr. Sanders to a stump speech delivered in December that criticizes Republicans and praises the Vermont senator as her “esteemed” rival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/25/hillary-clinton-holds-fire-on-bernie-sanders-taking-aim-at-repu