e-W5N6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1427, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/25/t-magazine/25tmag-schai-slide-W5N6/25tmag-schai-slide-W5N6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/25/t-magazine/25tmag-schai-slide-W5N6/25tmag-schai-slide-W5N6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/25/t-magazine/25tmag-schai-slide-W5N6/25tmag-schai-slide-W5N6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looks from Schai’s fall/winter 2016 collection', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T22:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/af997fb2-7332-5d84-adf2-56223ef3beb3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/af997fb2-7332-5d84-adf2-56223ef3beb3'}, {'abstract': 'Suk Chai of the brand Schai studied clothes she inherited from her brothers and sister before launching her own line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/25/t-magazine/schai-suk-chai-clothing-profile.html', 'snippet': 'Suk Chai of the brand Schai studied clothes she inherited from her brothers and sister before launching her own line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listening to the designer Suk Chai describe a garment in thorough detail is almost like seeing it and touching it for yourself. She fine-tuned her fashion vocabulary as a child, watching items that originally belonged to her eldest brother get passed to her second-oldest brother, then to her older sister, and finally to her. “I waited for this particular tweed coat and red beret for at least six years,” says Chai, now 43, who was born in Korea and raised in Seattle. Her first non-hand-me-down came in the form of a white, crew-neck, short-sleeved, all-cotton dress with patchwork and a poofy skirt (the occasion: her second-grade piano recital). “Both outfits were special,” she remarks. “The tweed coat — I had my eye on that for a long, long time, and I loved it and knew it’d eventually be mine; but I did like having my own clothes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For One Designer, Inspiration That Began With Hand-Me-Downs', 'kicker': 'On the Verge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coats and Jackets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nordstrom Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-25T22:48:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ee9ff7c-275d-55f9-9a5f-0445662de9ec', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ee9ff7c-275d-55f9-9a5f-0445662de9ec'}, {'abstract': 'Some couples were in denial about how disruptive one of the biggest blizzards in the city’s history would be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/31/fashion/weddings/blizzard-weddings-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'Some couples were in denial about how disruptive one of t