'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18d5807-f9c1-512b-9cf9-bfff08df759d', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18d5807-f9c1-512b-9cf9-bfff08df759d'}, {'abstract': 'Airstrikes by the Saudi-led military coalition hit the home of a senior judge in Sana, killing the judge along with his relatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/world/middleeast/yemen-top-judge-and-6-relatives-are-killed-in-airstrike.html', 'snippet': 'Airstrikes by the Saudi-led military coalition hit the home of a senior judge in Sana, killing the judge along with his relatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Airstrikes by the Saudi-led military coalition on Monday hit the home of a senior judge in Sana, Yemen’s capital, killing the judge along with six relatives, according to witnesses and medics. The judge, Yayha Alrubaid, who headed a court that dealt with national security matters and terrorism, had recently prosecuted members of Yemen’s Saudi-backed government in exile for high treason, officials said. Saudi Arabia entered Yemen’s civil war in March on the side of President Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi, who was driven from power by Houthi rebels last year. Coalition airstrikes have routinely hit civilian targets and killed hundreds of people, according to human rights workers. The Obama administration, which has supported the Saudi-led campaign in Yemen, issued an unusual statement on Saturday, criticizing recent airstrikes that killed a Yemeni journalist and an ambulance driver working with Doctors Without Borders, though the statement made no mention of Saudi Arabia or the coalition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen: Top Judge and 6 Relatives Are Killed in Airstrike', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Yemen: Senior Judge and 6 Relatives Are Killed in Airstrike on His Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almosawa, Shuaib', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadi, Abdu Rabbu Mansour', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-26T01:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shuaib Almosawa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shuaib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almosawa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/408ce0f4-cf02-5c37-9923-8c3ad2c4c49e', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/408ce0f4-cf02-5c37-9923-8c3ad2c4c49e'}, {'abstract': 'At the 2016 Sundance Film Festival, the big streaming services, not the traditional studios, are driving the deal-making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/business/media/so-far-amazon-and-netflix-are-sundances-top-buyers.html', 'snippet': 'At the 2016 Sundance Film Festival, the big streaming services, not the traditional studios, are driving the deal-making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — It was the independent film equivalent of a crack of thunder.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26SUNDANCE1/26SUNDANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/26/business/26SUNDANCE1/26SUNDANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '