riginal': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d97b42e-57a4-57d6-af55-dc02b3966cf8', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d97b42e-57a4-57d6-af55-dc02b3966cf8'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers in Libya overwhelmingly rejected a proposed United Nations-backed unity cabinet on Monday, dealing a blow to diplomatic efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/world/africa/libya-parliament-rejects-cabinet-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers in Libya overwhelmingly rejected a proposed United Nations-backed unity cabinet on Monday, dealing a blow to diplomatic efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawmakers in Libya’s internationally recognized Parliament overwhelmingly rejected a proposed United Nations-backed unity cabinet on Monday, dealing a blow to diplomatic efforts to swiftly reconcile the country’s splintered factions. Parliament, which sits in the eastern city of Tobruk, rejected the 32-member cabinet out of concern that it was too large and that its members had been chosen not for their competency but to satisfy various regional factions, according to Abu Bakr Buera, an influential lawmaker. Diplomats have been urging Libyan officials to bridge the divisions that emerged after the 2011 revolt against Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya: Parliament Rejects Cabinet Plan', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya: Parliament Rejects Cabinet Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-26T01:35:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By KAREEM FAHIM', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'FAHIM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/26a1c186-5354-5e5d-8e5f-7dbb308f83c8', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26a1c186-5354-5e5d-8e5f-7dbb308f83c8'}, {'abstract': 'The number of people who get insurance this year through the Affordable Care Act’s public marketplaces is expected to be 13 million, down from a prior projection of 21 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/us/budget-office-sharply-cuts-health-exchange-estimate.html', 'snippet': 'The number of people who get insurance this year through the Affordable Care Act’s public marketplaces is expected to be 13 million, down from a prior projection of 21 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Congressional Budget Office on Monday sharply reduced its estimate of how many people would get health insurance this year through the Affordable Care Act’s public marketplaces, to 13 million, from a prior estimate of 21 million.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/us/26Budget-web/26Budget-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Office Sharply Cuts Health Exchange Estimate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Office Sharply Cuts Health Exchange Estimate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burwell, Sylvia Mathews', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-26T01:40:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13b38162-94f9-5fd9-b993-201b95b8fd48', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13b38162-94f9-5fd9-b993-201b95b8fd48'}, {'abstract': 'The Central African Republic’s constitutional court scrapped results from a legislative election, citing irregularities like illegible ballots and poor training for election workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/world/africa/central-african-republic-court-invalidates-legislative-election.html', 'snippet': 'The Central African Republic’s constitutional court scrapped results from a legislative election, citing irregularities like illegible ballots and poor training for election workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Central African Republic’s constitutional court certified presidential election results Monday but separately scrapped results from a legislative election, citing irregularities like illegible ballots and poor training for election workers. The court’s validation sets the stage for a runoff for the presidential election that pits Anicet-Georges Dologuélé against Faustin Archange Touadera, two former prime ministers. They will face each other in a vote scheduled for no sooner than Feb. 7. Election observers said that redoing the legislative vote, which took place simultaneously with the presidential vote, would be costly. Candidates were puzzled by the court’s decision. “This is illogical,” said Lydie Nzengou, the communications officer for Karim Meckassoua, a presidential candidate. “Why would the results for the presidential vote be more credible than those of the legislative vote?” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Central African Republic: Court Invalidates Legislative Election', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; Central African Republic: Court Invalidates Legislative Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dologuele, Anicet-Georges', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Touadera, Faustin-Archange', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-26T01:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaux Benn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaux', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f564d3d5-bf08-5384-a3e2-18b28a426c2e', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f564d3d5-bf08-5384-a3e2-18b28a426c2e'}, {'abstract': 'Donald J. Trump asked New Hampshire voters Monday to hand him a victory so big, so beautiful, that only one word in the political lexicon could describe it: mandate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/25/trump-to-new-hampshire-give-me-a-mandate/', 'snippet': 'Donald J. Trump asked New Hampshire voters Monday to hand him a victory so big, so beautiful, that only one word in the political lexicon could describe it: mandate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FARMINGTON, N.H. – Donald J. Trump asked New Hampshire voters on Monday to hand him a victory so big, so beautiful, that only one word in the political lexicon could describe it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/26/us/politics/26firstdraft-trump-2/26firstdraft-trump-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/26/us/politics/26firstdraft-trump-2/26firstdraft-trump-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank