teral support of the Free the Nipple movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a warm fall day, members of a literary group gathered in Prospect Park to soak in the sun and snack on chocolate pretzels. Most book clubs in a park in Brooklyn wouldn’t cause much of a stir, but as the mostly female group read, men gawked and children stared. Police officers were called to the scene. The members of the Outdoor Co-ed Topless Pulp Fiction Appreciation Society are used to such attention. They are part of a larger movement called Free the Nipple, and see themselves as proponents of gender equality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fight to Free the Nipple', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Free the Nipple (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-26T10:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Acosta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Acosta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e53d2548-f80b-5620-a888-798c2dc2a323', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e53d2548-f80b-5620-a888-798c2dc2a323'}, {'abstract': 'A reader asks: Why is it important to take all the antibiotics a doctor prescribes?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/ask-well-taking-all-your-antibiotics/', 'snippet': 'A reader asks: Why is it important to take all the antibiotics a doctor prescribes?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Question:', 'source': 'The 