International Herald Tribune archives: A Nazi pilot arrives in New York after his escape from a Canadian prison train in 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/26/1941-nazi-flyer-escapes-canada/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A Nazi pilot arrives in New York after his escape from a Canadian prison train in 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A garrulous young German aviator with taped ears and an exuberant grin arrived in Grand Central Terminal early yesterday, eager to tell the world how he escaped from a Canadian prison train. Baron Franz von Werra found no time for conversation, however. A brusque German consular attache shouldered his way down platform 32 when the train from Ogdensburg pulled in at 6:45 a.m. and collared the twenty-six-year-old pursuit pilot as soon as he alighted.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 27, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/blogs/27iht-oldjan27-ears/27iht-oldjan27-ears-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 704, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/27/blogs/27iht-oldjan27-ears/27iht-oldjan27-ears-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 704}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/blogs/27iht-oldjan27-ears/27iht-oldjan27-ears-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 723, 'width': 616, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/blogs/27iht-oldjan27-ears/27iht-oldjan27-ears-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 723, 'width': 616, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images