.html', 'snippet': 'Talk of two potential big transactions dominated in Davos. Given the world’s parlous state, there are reasons to hope that both deals are made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two big deals dominated the agenda in Davos, Switzerland, last week: Argentina’s negotiations with holdout creditors and Saudi Arabia’s potential sale of a piece of its national energy leviathan, Saudi Aramco.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina and Aramco Are Deals for Difficult Times', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saudi Aramco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macri, Mauricio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Paul E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-26T17:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37dc9cca-0653-54d5-9f1a-ba818f59ed60', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37dc9cca-0653-54d5-9f1a-ba818f59ed60'}, {'abstract': 'The Grammy-nominated performer posted photos of flat horizons and a recording — a “diss track” — critical of the celebrity astrophysicist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/27/arts/music/rapper-bob-insists-earth-is-flat-take-that