: 'nyt://article/fdc4b0a3-2a56-58c6-b9f6-5f561fcb076f', 'word_count': 1972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdc4b0a3-2a56-58c6-b9f6-5f561fcb076f'}, {'abstract': 'The bursting of the bubble did not cause the recession. The Fed did.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/27/opinion/subprime-reasoning-on-housing.html', 'snippet': 'The bursting of the bubble did not cause the recession. The Fed did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT has become part of the accepted history of our time: The bursting of the housing bubble was the primary cause of a financial crisis, a sharp recession and prolonged slow growth. The story makes intuitive sense, since the economic crisis included a collapse in the prices of housing and related securities. The movie “The Big Short,” which is based on a book by Michael Lewis, takes this cause-and-effect relationship as a given.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 688}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 894, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1519, 'width': 1325, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/27/opinion/27ponnuru/27ponnuru-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Subprime Reasoning on Housing', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subprime Reasoning on Housing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponnuru, Ramesh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckworth, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-27T08:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Beckworth and Ramesh Ponnuru', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beckworth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ramesh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ponnuru', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ab2873f-679a-5db7-8914-d52b8bf2bca5', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab2873f-679a-5db7-8914-d52b8b