16-01-27T08:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/178ecdf5-47e0-509c-a1f7-4cc79e07e357', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/178ecdf5-47e0-509c-a1f7-4cc79e07e357'}, {'abstract': 'Had I prolonged my Indian grandmother’s suffering with my stubborn belief in the power of medicine to fix things?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/27/when-the-hospital-cant-help/', 'snippet': 'Had I prolonged my Indian grandmother’s suffering with my stubborn belief in the power of medicine to fix things?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were ants crawling on my grandmother’s feet in the hospital. My mother and I slapped towels at the insects, scoured the rusted metal legs of the bed, moved my unconscious grandmother’s limbs to search every wrinkle of the dingy sheets. The ants were a portent, I thought. This was all my fault. My grandmother was going to die in this filthy hospital, far from everything she knew and loved, because of me and my insistence on medical intervention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Hospital Is Not a Haven', 'kicker': 'The End', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-27T08:45:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meera Nair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meera', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cd10fa6-23ce-5258-a3b6-4caffe3ca711', 'word_count': 1586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cd10fa6-23ce-5258-a3b6-4caffe3ca711'}, {'abstract': 'A video of a woman denouncing those who resell hospital access for a profit was widely circulated online this week, inciting outrage among many.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/28/world/asia/beijing-hospital-ticket-scalpers.html', 'snippet': 'A video of a woman denouncing those who resell hospital access for a profit was widely circulated online this week, inciting outrage among many.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Ticket scalpers can be a headache in China, raising the prices of concerts, train trips and more. But no scalpers are more detested than those selling tickets for hospital visits. A video of a woman in Beijing denouncing the practice circulated widely this week, as many others shared their own experiences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/world/asia/28chinahospital-promo/28chinahospital-promo-jumbo.png', 'height': 438, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/world/asia/28chinahospital-promo/28chinahospital-promo-superJumbo.png', 'height': 438, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/world/asia/28chinahospital-promo/28chinahospital-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':