er pressure from hedge funds, Claire Gogel, a former Greenlight executive, will join the board of the struggling renewable energy company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SunEdison, the renewable energy company, was once the darling of the hedge fund world. Big-name investors like Steven A. Cohen, Leon G. Cooperman and David Einhorn rode the stock as it soared to ever increasing heights. And then it crashed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1424, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/business/28db-einhorn-web/28db-einhorn-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Pressure, SunEdison Gives David Einhorn’s Fund a Board Seat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under Pressure, SunEdison Adds Einhorn to Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SunEdison Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevenson, Alexandra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Einhorn, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenlight Capital Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-27T14:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbcdc032-cd20-596e-949f-fefe19670282', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbcdc032-cd20-596e-949f-fefe19670282'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A new drama, “Jeanne d’Arc,” receives rave reviews in Paris in 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/27/1891-rave-reviews-for-fabre-drama/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A new drama, “Jeanne d’Arc,” receives rave reviews in Paris in 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over four thousand patriotic Frenchmen and Frenchwomen enthusiastically applauded ‘‘Jeanne d’Arc,’’ a drama by M. Joseph Fabre, music by M. Benjamin Goldard, which was given last night at the Châtelet. The plot of necessity follows the story of the Maid of Orleans, from her departure to arouse the King from his lethargy to the stake at Rouen. It is treated in a poetic way and the tirades placed in the heroine’s mouth are of the loftiest strain and full of the most patriotic spirit. All of this is set in the midst of a splendid mise-en-scène. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 28, 1891', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 1459, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/blogs/28iht-oldjan28-fabre/28iht-oldjan28-fabre-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1891: Rave Reviews for Fabre Drama', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-27T14:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4189b7f6-08dc-530e-bbc6-23dd5f241b6e', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4189b7f6-08dc-530e-bbc6-23dd5f241b6e'}, {'abstract': 'In order to be of use, assistants like Cortana and Siri need to know a lot about you. Reading the companies’ privacy statements can give you an idea of how much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/28/technology/personaltech/protecting-personal-information-from-virtual-assistants.html', 'snippet': 'In order to be of use, assistants like Cortana and Siri need to know a lot about you. Reading the companies’ privacy statements can give you an idea of how much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I was going to try Cortana, Microsoft’s version of Siri, but to use it, you have to allow Microsoft access to your location, your contacts, voice input, information from email and text messages, browser history, search history, calendar details “and other information.” Naturally, I declined. Why does Microsoft need so much personal information and what does Microsoft do with it?', 'print_section': 'B', 'prin