', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Portable Veblen (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-27T22:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Senior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Senior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8384c1cb-6b01-56f9-8d6a-76bf0b9b0929', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8384c1cb-6b01-56f9-8d6a-76bf0b9b0929'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist performed at the 92nd Street Y as part of the Seeing Music Festival, which runs through Feb. 18.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/28/arts/music/review-matan-porat-plays-an-improvised-score-to-the-general.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist performed at the 92nd Street Y as part of the Seeing Music Festival, which runs through Feb. 18.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Timing, momentum and pluck: That’s pretty much all that the young hero of Buster Keaton’s silent movie “The General” has going for him as he sets off to retrieve his locomotive, his girl and his honor in this madcap Civil War comedy from 1927. Timing, momentum and fierce technical chops were the main qualities the pianist Matan Porat brought to the stage on Tuesday evening at the 92nd Street Y when he performed an improvised score  to “The General” that was as propulsive, vivid and fun as the film itself.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/arts/28PORAT-WEB/28PORAT-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/28/arts/28PORAT-WEB/28PORAT-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 4