'nyt://article/b2966951-bdbc-5ee7-8630-d5b9fe45d650'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Cara, a young Canadian singer who got her start on YouTube, headlined at Webster Hall on Tuesday behind her 2015 debut album, “Know-It-All.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/28/arts/music/review-alessia-cara-voice-for-outsiders-becomes-an-insider.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Cara, a young Canadian singer who got her start on YouTube, headlined at Webster Hall on Tuesday behind her 2015 debut album, “Know-It-All.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wallflowers have a champion in Alessia Cara, the 19-year-old Canadian singer and songwriter who headlined Webster Hall on Tuesday night. Ms. Cara’s lyrics pivot from self-doubt to self-affirmation in songs like “Wild Things,” which declares, “Don’t wanna hang around the in crowd/The cool kids aren’t cool to me.” The hit that sold out the club for Ms. Cara is “Here”: a jazzily sung, finely detailed depiction of a party she wishes she’d never attended. She calls herself an “antisocial pessimist” and sings on the chorus, “I ask myself, what am I doin’ here?” It’s far and away the best song on her 2015 debut album, “Know-It-All” (Def Jam).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/arts/28CARA/28CARA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/28/arts/28CARA/28CARA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/arts/28CARA/28CARA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/arts/28CARA/28CARA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2