ers said the interrogation was the sharpest grilling that Mr. Rusk had ever received in Congress during his entire five-year career as secretary of state. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 29, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/blogs/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright/29iht-oldjan29-fulbright-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Attack on Vietnam Policies', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-28T16:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8127ac31-ad92-5c9d-b2a9-7eeca9d793c5', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8127ac31-ad92-5c9d-b2a9-7eeca9d793c5'}, {'abstract': 'Anyone who thinks Warsaw or Budapest will give in to pressure on issues of national sovereignty should look at how far the Greeks were prepared to go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/29/opinion/in-greeces-populism-precious-lessons-for-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Anyone who thinks Warsaw or Budapest will give in to pressure on issues of national sovereignty should look at how far the Greeks were prepared to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Athens — It may just be coincidence, but in the year since a radical left movement and an extreme right-wing party joined forces to govern Greece, the resilience of the European Union has been tested. But it may be also that the forces released in Greece have emerged in many other countries, poisoning relations among member states.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandara