 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LINDSAY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4eb8d969-d441-5bca-8be7-ffee80b39cb5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4eb8d969-d441-5bca-8be7-ffee80b39cb5'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Chris Fritton is visiting more than 100 shops across America, creating postcards and prints to send to his backers along the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/28/t-magazine/art/chris-fritton-letterpress-project.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Chris Fritton is visiting more than 100 shops across America, creating postcards and prints to send to his backers along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last half of the 19th century and in the early years of the 20th, back when printing was a trade, there was enough work to carve out a living for anyone with the skills and a union card almost anywhere in the U.S. — and some printers with a taste for travel found their work on the road. The peripatetic lives of these tramp printers, as they were known, are the inspiration for artist Chris Fritton’s crowdfunded Itinerant Printer Project. The campaign will take him to more than 100 letterpress shops across the country, creating postcards and prints to send his backers along the way. (So far he’s visited 67.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/28/t-magazine/28tma-printer-01/28tma-printer-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/28/t-magazine/28tma-printer-01/28tma-printer-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ