 debate before the Iowa caucuses took a surreal turn as seven candidates found their messages overshadowed by Donald J. Trump’s boycott of the event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — The Republican presidential candidates competed vigorously to fill the vacuum created by Donald J. Trump’s boycott of Thursday night’s debate, with Senator Ted Cruz of Texas and Senator Marco Rubio of Florida trading ferocious attacks on immigration and taking fire from rivals seeking advantage in the Iowa caucuses on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ted Cruz and Marco Rubio Clash Harshly, Filling Void on G.O.P. Debate Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cruz and Rubio Clash Harshly, Filling a Void', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasich, John R', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carson, Benjamin S', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N