'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c120318e-7dff-59d8-aeab-8ae2ff759010', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c120318e-7dff-59d8-aeab-8ae2ff759010'}, {'abstract': 'William Gedney once said he was not “a social problem photographer.” Working in places like Appalachia and Northern California, he challenged preconceived notions to find enduring — and unexpected — images.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/29/beyond-stereotypes-in-california-and-kentucky/', 'snippet': 'William Gedney once said he was not “a social problem photographer.” Working in places like Appalachia and Northern California, he challenged preconceived notions to find enduring — and unexpected — images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Urban California and rural Appalachia were amply documented in the 1960s, even if the usual narratives were often polar opposites: the Bay Area, with its free-loving, psychedelic hippie counterculture or Kentucky with its gritty backwoods scenes of despair and poverty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Stereotypes in California and Kentucky', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenberg, Howard, Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'APPALACHIAN REGION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T08:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rena Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rena', 'middlename':