 Inc', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T17:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phoebe Lett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phoebe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3ffaf99-c124-5c43-b86b-63e583b3ca21', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3ffaf99-c124-5c43-b86b-63e583b3ca21'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Myles, who published two books in 2015 and won fame through the TV series “Transparent,” meditates, writes and acknowledges doing “secret things.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/31/nyregion/how-eileen-myles-poet-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Myles, who published two books in 2015 and won fame through the TV series “Transparent,” meditates, writes and acknowledges doing “secret things.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'She’s long been a figure in the counter culture, but recently the writer Eileen Myles has also become something of a household name. In 2015 she published two books: “Chelsea Girls,” a reissue of an autobiographical novel, and “I Must Be Living Twice: New and Selected Poems 1975-2014.” She also made it to television, where the hit series “Transparent” quoted her poetry and featured a character based on her. “I’ve had a lifelong waiting-for-the-other-shoe-to-drop feeling when something good happens,” Ms. Myles said. “But oddly, that’s not happening.” Ms. Myles, 66, splits her time between Marfa, Tex., and Manhattan, where she lives with her golden pit bull, Honey, in the rent-stabilized o