state constable, who fired in return and accidentally killed the man’s 12-year-old daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pennsylvania man who the authorities say pointed a rifle at a state constable evicting him has been charged in the death of his 12-year-old daughter, who was accidentally shot when the officer fired his weapon in response.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Is Charged in Death of His Daughter After Eviction Confrontation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evictions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harrisburg (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T18:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7053a3e6-e704-52bd-80f5-726820f5f6ec', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7053a3e6-e704-52bd-80f5-726820f5f6ec'}, {'abstract': 'An energy revolution, suddenly in reach.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/29/a-renewable-feast/', 'snippet': 'An energy revolution, suddenly in reach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So you say you want a revolution? Politically, I’m afraid you’ll be disappointed — unless the revolution you have in mind involves putting Donald Trump’s finger on the button. But an environmental/energy revolution? That’s looking remarkably within reach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Renewable Feast', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T18:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6737a794-4220-5786-95d3-2da701b7f910', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6737a794-4220-5786-95d3-2da701b7f910'}, {'abstract': 'The actress is being honored, along with her daughter, Charlotte Gainsbourg, with the “Jane and Charlotte Forever” series at Film Society of Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/29/t-magazine/entertainment/jane-birkin-interview.html', 'snippet': 'The actress is being honored, along with her daughter, Charlotte Gainsbourg, with the “Jane and Charlotte Forever” series at Film Society of Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Birkin doesn’t watch her own films. “I don’t even know that I saw most of them when they came out,” she says, laughing. “There are a few I have seen and thank goodness never saw again.” But when T sat down with Birkin ahead of “Jane and Charlotte Forever,” a series at the Film Society of Lincoln Center dedicated to the acting work of Birkin and daughter Charlotte Gainsbourg, she was eager to talk about her many collaborations — with former partners Serge Gainsbourg and Jacques Doillon, as well as Agnès Varda — and why’s she now more content doing her own thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/t-magazine/29tmag-birkin-01/29tmag-birkin-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/29/t-magazine/29tmag-birkin-01/29tmag-birkin-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidt