'_id': 'nyt://article/e795a8fd-3e6a-5cd7-a8cb-60f36cdf0c8a', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e795a8fd-3e6a-5cd7-a8cb-60f36cdf0c8a'}, {'abstract': 'The presidential candidate’s life story is told in picture books aimed at young children and searching biographies meant for tweens and teenagers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/29/books/review/review-biographies-of-hillary-clinton-for-kids-of-all-ages.html', 'snippet': 'The presidential candidate’s life story is told in picture books aimed at young children and searching biographies meant for tweens and teenagers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month brings four new biographies of Hillary Clinton — for kids. The wonder is that whether it’s for preschoolers or for teenagers, each in its own way presents a coherent picture of her. Getting a handle on the Democratic presidential candidate’s swerving, crowded life is a challenge for any biographer, and turning her into a subject for children seems yet more daunting. Even putting aside her husband’s PG-13 affair with an intern, it’s still not clear what the ending of Hillary’s story will be. (As of now, no children’s books about the other candidates are on the horizon.) Yet publishers have done an admirable job packaging just plain Hillary as someone whose life story children may find inspirational, and perhaps even relatable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/books/review/29clinton/29clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/29/books/review/29clinton/29clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/books/review/29clinton/29clinton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'ju