n and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T22:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Men’s Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By NOAH JOHNSON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'JOHNSON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/6b354fad-d4c6-57d9-8020-81bd334a32e2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/6b354fad-d4c6-57d9-8020-81bd334a32e2'}, {'abstract': 'Jeremy Tiang’s adaptation of Cao Xueqin’s sprawling 18th-century novel about an aristocratic family focuses on a love story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/30/theater/review-a-dream-of-red-pavilions-a-love-story-born-in-the-spirit-world.html', 'snippet': 'Jeremy Tiang’s adaptation of Cao Xueqin’s sprawling 18th-century novel about an aristocratic family focuses on a love story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life could be complicated for Chinese aristocrats in the 1700s. Just ask the members of the Jia family, who populate “A Dream of Red Pavilions,” Pan Asian Repertory’s handsome and solemn new production at the Clurman Theater. They think everything is going to be fine when one of the daughters is chosen to be a royal courtesan. And they never even know that they have two immortal beings living with them, incarnated as family members.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30DREAM/30DREAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘A Dream of Red Pavilions,’ a Love Story Born in the Spirit World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stone Meets Flower, and Love Blooms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Anita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tiang, Jeremy (Playwright)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pan Asian Repertory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Dream of Red Pavilions (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T22:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a22993e-0fca-52e4-a8e1-2945bd2dffee', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a22993e-0fca-52e4-a8e1-2945bd2dffee'}, {'abstract': 'This choreographer’s company danced “Set and Reset,” “Present Tense” and “Newark (Niweweorce),” works the company says it expects to stop performing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/30/arts/dance/review-from-trisha-brown-three-last-dances-maybe-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'This choreographer’s company danced “Set and Reset,” “Present Tense” and “Newark (Niweweorce),” works the company says it expects to stop performing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rigor; wit; experimentalism; sensuousness. The three works by Trisha Brown being performed at the Brooklyn Academy of Music — “Set and Reset” (1983), “Present Tense” (2003), “Newark (Niweweorce)” (1987) — blend these virtues so provocatively that they make the best case to date for her greatness as a choreographer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30TRISHA/30TRISHA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30TRISHA/30TRISHA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 669}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30TRISHA/30TRISHA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 919, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30TRISHA/30TRISHA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'wid