rsons', 'value': 'McAuliffe, Terry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Everytown for Gun Safety', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-29T22:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd764aac-a9f0-548c-bf49-c07be74ea678', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd764aac-a9f0-548c-bf49-c07be74ea678'}, {'abstract': 'These two plays — “Tonight With Donny Stixx” and “Dark Vanilla Jungle,” playing in repertory at Here — consist of monologues by people who have committed unspeakable crimes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/30/theater/review-in-tonight-jungle-by-philip-ridley-darkness-rules.html', 'snippet': 'These two plays — “Tonight With Donny Stixx” and “Dark Vanilla Jungle,” playing in repertory at Here — consist of monologues by people who have committed unspeakable crimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just how dark do you like it? The British dramatist Philip Ridley, whose excellent “Dark Vanilla Jungle” and “Tonight With Donny Stixx” are in repertory at Here, is notorious for testing the palates of theatergoers who think they prefer their humor black, strong and bitter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/arts/30TONIGHT/30TONIGHT-ar