ead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday I attended a small performance by the band Lucius, one of my favorites, and had a wonderful time despite Kylo Ren in the way:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Lucius, Madness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-30T00:12:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61268578-fd45-519e-b275-ac6cdfad45e5', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61268578-fd45-519e-b275-ac6cdfad45e5'}, {'abstract': 'If there is a single symbol summing up Mrs. Clinton on the campaign trail, it is, perhaps, an enormous 3D printer she first encountered at a community college in Waterloo, Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2016/01/29/hillary-clinton-and-the-huge-3d-printer/', 'snippet': 'If there is a single symbol summing up Mrs. Clinton on the campaign trail, it is, perhaps, an enormous 3D printer she first encountered at a community college in Waterloo, Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBUQUE, Iowa — If there is a single symbol to sum up the standard Hillary Clinton stump speech, it is, perhaps, the enormous 3D printer she first encountered at a technical training center in Waterloo, Iowa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/us/29firstdraft-priorities/29firstdraft-priorities-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton and the Huge 3D Printer', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-30T00:25:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbbb1451-d0d8-5e1c-bcc4-ed7b2cc07b1f', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbbb1451-d0d8-5e1c-bcc4-ed7b2cc07b1f'}, {'abstract': 'What actually gets classified?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/29/my-classified-life/', 'snippet': 'What actually gets classified?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gah. Another Clinton email story, this time involving emails covering material that wasn’t classified when sent but is now deemed top-secret — with the Clinton campaign demanding that they be released, presumably to show how innocuous they really were. Max Fisher at Vox suggests that it’s basically a story about the craziness and excesses of the classification system, and my own experience — although deeply out of date — suggests that he’s probably right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Classified Life', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-30T00:43:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66f0117a-bf0d-5497-a1cf-95fe7194c061', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66f0117a-bf0d-5497-a1cf-95fe7194c061'}, {'abstract': 'Bac Duong, one of three men who escaped from an Orange County jail, turned himself in to the police after a week on the run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/30/us/california-escapee-turns-himself-in.html', 'snippet': 'Bac Duong, one of three men who escaped from an Orange County jail, turned himself in to the police after a week on the run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of three men who escaped from an Orange County jail turned himself in to the police on Friday after a week on the run. The man, Bac Duong, 43, “contacted a civilian on the streets of Santa Ana and stated he wanted to turn himself in,” said Sandra Hutchens, the Orange County sheriff. Mr. Duong is charged with attempted murder and had been in custody since December. The sheriff did not release any details of his capture. The search continues for the other two men who broke out of the Orange County Central Men’s Jail — Hossein Nayeri, 37, and Jonathan Tieu, 20 — neither of whom has been seen since a 5 a.m. head count on Jan. 22. Sheriff’s department officials previously said they believed the three escapees were together in Southern California and could be receiving assistance from Vietnamese organized crime groups. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Escapee Turns Himself In ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Escapee Turns Himself In ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orange County (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duong, Bac', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nayeri, Hossein', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tieu, Jonathan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-30T00:46:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifi