fers dishes that are savory, sweet and piquant, and tries to educate diners who might not be familiar with the cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the first things you will see when you enter Spice Kitchen, a North Indian restaurant that opened in Mamaroneck in early September, is a lovely metal carving of Annapurna Devi, the Hindu goddess of nourishment. One evening we were seated beneath a mural of the Buddha at a comfortable banquette, and the ambience had a wonderfully calming effect, which, as it turned out, was very helpful because sometimes the patience of Job was needed when dining there.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/nyregion/31DINEWE1/31DINEWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/31/nyregion/31DINEWE1/31DINEWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/nyregion/31DINEWE1/31DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/nyregion/31DINEWE1/31DINEWE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/nyregion/31DINEWE1/31DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/31/nyregion/31DINEWE1/31DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':