rray’s older brother, Jamie, paused in mid-interview to scold him. “Andy, you should be in bed,” he said.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 788}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1559, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/30/sports/doubles-1-web/doubles-1-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jamie Murray Wins in Doubles; Andy Murray Has a Long Night, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Brother Wins; the Other Has a Late Night, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Jamie (1986- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-30T19:44:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/125cdcf0-5b94-56c3-a771-10fb6fa03227', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/125cdcf0-5b94-56c3-a771-10fb6fa03227'}, {'abstract': 'From the perspective of the teams, it’s easy to understand the T-shirt-cannon phenomenon. But from the fans’ perspective, the phenomenon mystifies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/01/31/sports/why-sports-fans-risk-life-and-limb-for-a-rolled-up-t-shirt.html', 'snippet': 'From the perspective of the teams, it’s easy to understand the T-shirt-cannon phenomenon. But from the fans’ perspective, the phenomenon mystifies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Knicks games, it’s the 7th Avenue Squad. The Mets have the Pepsi Party Patrol. The Nets have the inanimate Team Hype. But every team in sports with any semblance of a marketing department has its own version of the Fan Patrol or Fun Police. This unnaturally peppy collective represents a cross between a cheerleading squad and the “motivators” at a bar mitzvah party. Their demeanor and high energy often totally at odds with the tenor of the game, they attempt to energize the crowd by cavorting with the mascot and dancing with kids on the Jumbotron and hosting the fan contest during breaks in the game. But the highlight of their shift comes when they launch T-shirts into the crowd.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1435, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/31/sports/31TSHIRTCANNON1/31TSHIRTCANNON1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Sports Fans Risk Life and Limb for a Rolled-Up T-shirt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It&#8217;s Free? Then Fire Away. Up Here!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'T-Shirts (Apparel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value