ust-languished-in-a-downing-street-cupboard.html', 'snippet': 'The moon dust’s fate was revealed by Britain’s National Archives, which released 178 pages of correspondence on the subject going back 30 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a space problem of sorts for the new British prime minister: where to put the minuscule sample of the lunar dust that America’s Apollo 11 astronauts had scooped from the surface of the moon in their giant leap for mankind?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/world/01MOONDUST/01MOONDUST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Moon Dust Languished in a Downing Street Cupboard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Moon to a Cupboard at 10 Downing Street ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Archives and Records Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heath, Edward', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-31T21:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2af0ccd8-2f3d-5c90-be2a-20d5ecf58323', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2af0ccd8-2f3d-5c90-be2a-20d5ecf58323'}, {'abstract': 'Pat Mahony, whose father and grandfather helped develop parimutuel wagering in the United States, has retired from his job at Aqueduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/02/01/sports/horse-racing/in-building-a-modern-betting-system-a-family-was-an-eyewitness-to-horse-racing-history.html', 'snippet': 'Pat Mahony, whose father and grandfather helped develop parimutuel wagering in the United States, has retired from his job at Aqueduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late Sunday afternoon, when the tote board went dark after the final race of the day at Aqueduct Racetrack, Pat Mahony called it a career, one he has cherished and one that has been part of his family history for more than a century. Like his father and grandfather before him, Mahony is a mutuels man.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Family Helped Build Betting System, It Witnessed Horse Racing History', 'kicker': 'On Horse Racing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building a Betting System, and Witnessing History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahony, Pat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aqueduct Racetrack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-31T21:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Horse Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00e7ae2d-1ceb-55b4-938f-e670d22af464', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00e7ae2d-1ceb-55b4-938f-e670d22af464'}, {'abstract': 'The battle is threatening to complicate government efforts to attract desperately needed foreign investment, two weeks after the lifting of sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/02/01/world/middleeast/iran-sanctions-oil-investment.html', 'snippet': 'The battle is threatening to complicate government efforts to attract desperately needed foreign investment, two weeks after the lifting of sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — A political battle is taking shape in Iran over any new foreign role in developing the country’s enormous oil wealth, only a few weeks after the Iranian nuclear deal with foreign powers relaxed tough economic sanctions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Iran, New Battle Brews Over Contracts With Foreign Oil Giants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Iran Battle Brews Over Foreign Oil Titans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-31T21:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d585d8cd-fd27-5693-bdc9-fe5a2b04f243', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d585d8cd-fd27-5693-bdc9-fe5a2b04f243'}, {'abstract': 'Different kinds of enthusiasm.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/01/31/pre-iowa-notes/', 'snippet': 'Different kinds of enthusiasm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t know what will happen in the caucuses tomorrow. Actually, I know what will happen on the Republican side: someone horrifying will come in first, and someone horrifying will come in second. The names are less clear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pre-Iowa Notes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-01-31T21:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89372ddd-87a8-5320-8c5f-4770b54558db', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89372ddd-87a8-5320-8c5f-4770b54558db'}, {'abstract': 'Argentina’s new government has vowed to get to the bottom of a 1994 attack on a Jewish center that killed 85 people and led to a lasting rift with Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/02/01/world/americas/argentina-inquiry-jewish-center-bombing-new-turn.html', 'snippet': 'Argentina’s new government has vowed to get to the bottom of a 1994 attack on a Jewish center that killed 85 people and led to a lasting rift with Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — For more than two decades, an investigation into the suicide bombing of a Jewish center here in 1994 that killed 85 people has faced setbacks and controversy. It caused an intractable rift between Argentina and Iran. A former president has been put on trial, accused of orchestrating a cover-up. And a prosecutor involved in the case died last year in murky circumstances.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/world/argentina-web/argentina-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/01/29/world/argentina-web/argentina-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/01/29/world/argentina-web/argentina-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 