et': 'At least 50 people, including children, were killed by gunmen and suicide bombers in a series of raids on villages outside the city of Maiduguri, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KADUNA, Nigeria — More than 50 people were killed in a series of raids on villages in northeastern Nigeria that officials say was the work of the Islamist extremist group Boko Haram.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boko Haram Burns Villages in Northeastern Nigeria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dozens Are Killed in Raids in Nigeria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maiduguri (Nigeria)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-01-31T22:18:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sunday Isuwa and Dionne Searcey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sunday', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isuwa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dionne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Searcey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb9f571b-77f0-5a44-98f7-90c8ef91c166', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb9f571b-77f0-5a44-98f7-90c8ef91c166'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Paxton is the choreographic force behind this 2011 Robert Ashley mystery story opera, now at the Kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/02/01/arts/dance/review-quicksand-driven-by-the-rhythm-of-words-light-and-bodies.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Paxton is the choreographic force behind this 2011 Robert Ashley mystery story opera, now at the Kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Told from the point of view of a wry, vodka-swilling composer and freelance spy, Robert Ashley’s “Quicksand,” a 2011 opera written as a novel, anticipates action from the start: “I’m sitting on the bathroom floor, leaning back against the sink. I have the gun in my hands.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QUICKDANCE/01QUICKDANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QUICKDANCE/01QUICKDANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QUICKDANCE/01QUICKDANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QUICKDANCE/01QUICKDANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QUICKDANCE/01QUICKDANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QUICKDANCE/01QUICKDANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/02/01/arts/01QU